{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Na4T2wMAPFbcm84SjWJXwv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BKiR6fdipH8LKpVWU6RQkN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — sos_1 The Dawning Archaic\n\n## File: `cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py`\n\nThe Dawning Archaic is a `{10}` Legendary Creature — Avatar, 7/7, with three\ndistinct mechanics drawn from its oracle text:\n\n1. Cost reduction: \"This spell costs {1} less to cast for each instant and\n   sorcery card in your graveyard.\"\n2. Reach (static keyword).\n3. Attack trigger: \"Whenever The Dawning Archaic attacks, you may cast target\n   instant or sorcery card from your graveyard without paying its mana cost. If\n   that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n\nTests follow the FDN per-card conventions (class-based `TestX` layout, imports\nfrom `cards.sos.sos_1.card_impl`, `engine.*`, and `test_utils`). The\nimplementation is a stub, so all behavioral tests fail in the TDD red phase.\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicProperties — static card data\n- `test_is_creature` — card is a `Creature` instance.\n- `test_name` — name is \"The Dawning Archaic\".\n- `test_mana_cost` — mana cost parses to `{10}`.\n- `test_power_toughness` — 7/7 base P/T.\n- `test_is_legendary` — has the `LEGENDARY` supertype (Legendary Creature).\n- `test_is_avatar` — has the \"Avatar\" subtype.\n- `test_has_reach` — has the `REACH` keyword.\n- `test_is_colorless` — `{10}` is generic-only, so there are no colored pips\n  (guards against a buggy cost with stray colored mana).\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicCostReduction — generic cost reduction hook\nValidates the `cost_reduction(game)` hook (the engine's cost-reduction surface,\nper `engine/casting.py::get_cost_reduction`). Only generic mana is reducible.\n- `test_no_reduction_with_empty_graveyard` — 0 when graveyard is empty.\n- `test_one_instant_reduces_by_one` — one instant → reduction 1.\n- `test_one_sorcery_reduces_by_one` — one sorcery → reduction 1.\n- `test_mixed_instants_and_sorceries_sum` — counts all instants + sorceries\n  (2 instants + 1 sorcery → 3).\n- `test_noninstant_nonsorcery_cards_do_not_reduce` — creatures in the graveyard\n  do NOT reduce the cost (guards over-counting by zone size).\n- `test_only_your_graveyard_counts` — the opponent's graveyard is ignored;\n  \"your graveyard\" only. This is the key word \"your\" in the oracle text.\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicTriggerRegistration — attack trigger wiring\nMirrors the FDN attack-trigger pattern (`fdn_45` Kiora) using\n`register_triggers` + `AttacksTriggeredEvent`.\n- `test_registers_one_attack_trigger` — registering adds exactly one trigger.\n- `test_registered_trigger_watches_attacks_event` — the registered\n  `TriggerRegistration.event_type` is `AttacksTriggeredEvent`.\n- `test_trigger_condition_matches_self_attacking` — the condition fires when\n  this card is the attacker. (If the implementation uses no condition and\n  self-guards in the effect instead, the test tolerates `condition is None`.)\n- `test_trigger_condition_ignores_other_attacker` — a different attacker does\n  not satisfy the condition (the trigger is \"Whenever *The Dawning Archaic*\n  attacks\", not any creature).\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicTargeting — target requirement\nThe trigger targets an instant/sorcery in your graveyard.\n- `test_get_targets_advertises_graveyard_zone` — `get_targets` returns one\n  requirement whose `zone == GRAVEYARD`.\n- `test_target_filter_accepts_instant` / `test_target_filter_accepts_sorcery` —\n  the filter accepts both card types named in the oracle text.\n- `test_target_filter_rejects_creature` — a creature is not a legal target.\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicFreeCast — cast from graveyard without paying\nFires the attack event, then resolves the trigger off the stack.\n- `test_targeted_spell_leaves_graveyard_when_cast` — the chosen spell is no\n  longer in the graveyard after the free cast resolves (it was put on the stack\n  and cast).\n- `test_no_mana_required_for_free_cast` — with an empty mana pool the spell is\n  still cast, proving \"without paying its mana cost\".\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicExileReplacement — exile instead of graveyard\n- `test_free_cast_spell_is_exiled_after_resolution` — after the free-cast spell\n  resolves, it ends up in exile (not back in the graveyard), per \"If that spell\n  would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicNoOp — defensive edge cases\n- `test_no_target_chosen_is_a_noop` — firing the trigger with no chosen target\n  does not raise and does not move any card (the ability is \"may\" / target may\n  be absent).\n- `test_empty_graveyard_no_targets_available` — with no instants/sorceries in\n  the graveyard, no card satisfies the target filter.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately covered\n- \"Your graveyard\" only (opponent's graveyard excluded) for both cost reduction\n  and targeting scope.\n- Non-spell cards excluded from both the cost reduction count and the target\n  filter.\n- Free cast with zero mana available (proves no mana payment).\n- Exile-instead-of-graveyard replacement after resolution.\n\n## Edge cases NOT covered (out of scope / engine-owned)\n- Reach combat-blocking interactions: covered by engine combat tests\n  (`engine/combat._can_block`) and the FDN reach example; not re-tested here to\n  avoid duplicating engine behavior.\n- The full sorcery-speed/timing pipeline of casting the Archaic itself: the\n  generic casting flow is engine-owned and covered by `engine_tests`.\n- \"may\" prompt UX (whether the player declines): modeled as the no-target noop;\n  the precise decline-prompt API is not asserted to avoid coupling to a specific\n  yes/no choice surface.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":380,"cache_read_input_tokens":80391,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":380,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":68,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XD2FdaWwdM2D8M6HaFcj1t","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"b503b2cc-3e45-422a-bdc9-eb7b92992547","request_id":"req_011CbcDs6SqEBc5UFhdmui4d","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_1"}
