{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01AtskSSd7Sq8oZqAtKbyCAt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VCq9HWsVRXD5hx23ysiUYE","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl-rationale.md","content":"# sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic — Implementation Rationale\n\n## Approach\n`TheDawningArchaic` subclasses `engine.card.Creature` and sets static data via\n`kwargs.setdefault` (name, `{10}` cost, Legendary supertype, Avatar subtype,\nReach keyword, 7/7), matching the FDN reference pattern (e.g. fdn_194 Etali).\n\n### Cost reduction\n`cost_reduction(game)` counts instant/sorcery cards in the controller's\ngraveyard and returns that count. The engine clamps this against generic mana in\n`casting.get_cost_reduction`, and only generic is reduced — matching the spec\n(\"{1} less for each instant and sorcery card in your graveyard\"). Controller is\nresolved as `controller or owner` so it works both at cast time (engine sets\ncontroller) and in the property tests (which pass `controller=p1`).\n\n### Targeting\n`get_targets` returns a single `TargetRequirement` in `Zone.GRAVEYARD` whose\n`filter_fn` accepts instants/sorceries only. This serves the attack trigger's\n\"target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard\".\n\n### Attack trigger\n`register_triggers` registers one `TriggerRegistration` watching\n`AttacksTriggeredEvent` with a condition `event.creature is self` (self-guard so\nother attackers don't fire it). The effect free-casts the chosen target.\n\n### Free cast + exile replacement\nThe effect reads `self.chosen_targets` (set by the engine resolve pipeline, or\ndirectly by tests). With no legal chosen target it is a no-op (modeling the\n\"may\"), so it does not call `choose_*` on the player — important because the\ntest players have empty deterministic scripts. It validates the target is an\ninstant/sorcery still in the controller's graveyard, then calls\n`engine.casting.cast_spell_free(..., Zone.GRAVEYARD)`.\n\nThe exile clause is the only subtle part. `cast_spell_free` resolves a\nnon-permanent via `_resolve_spell`, which moves STACK -> GRAVEYARD using\n`move_to_zone` *without* a replacement event (no replacement effect is consulted\nfor stack-to-graveyard). Rather than alter that engine path, I wrap the pushed\nStackObject's `on_resolve`: it runs the original resolution, then if the spell\nlanded in the controller's graveyard it calls `engine.game.exile` to redirect it\nto exile. This faithfully reproduces \"If that spell would be put into your\ngraveyard, exile it instead\" for the post-resolution move that the tests assert.\n\n## Engine changes\nNone. All behavior is implemented in `cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py` using\nexisting engine APIs (`cast_spell_free`, `exile`, `TargetRequirement`,\n`TriggerRegistration`, zone accessors).\n\n## Conventions for future cards\n- Free-cast-from-graveyard with a graveyard-redirect-to-exile rider can be done\n  purely at the card level by wrapping the StackObject's `on_resolve` after\n  `cast_spell_free`, without touching the engine.\n- Model \"may cast target ...\" abilities by reading `chosen_targets` and treating\n  an absent/illegal target as a no-op, avoiding `choose_*` calls that would\n  exhaust deterministic test scripts.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":228,"cache_read_input_tokens":79109,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":228,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":62,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JiLujFtEyXTYwHwVbp4cog","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"d8564998-f9a7-421c-94b8-b3121e4525da","request_id":"req_011CbcE4suMqRchUxFZgNg5h","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_1"}
