{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q6Kh2VB4xjPxSoE5YEWZSv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic — Implementation Rationale\n2\t\n3\t## Approach\n4\t`TheDawningArchaic` subclasses `engine.card.Creature` and sets static data via\n5\t`kwargs.setdefault` (name, `{10}` cost, Legendary supertype, Avatar subtype,\n6\tReach keyword, 7/7), matching the FDN reference pattern (e.g. fdn_194 Etali).\n7\t\n8\t### Cost reduction\n9\t`cost_reduction(game)` counts instant/sorcery cards in the controller's\n10\tgraveyard and returns that count. The engine clamps this against generic mana in\n11\t`casting.get_cost_reduction`, and only generic is reduced — matching the spec\n12\t(\"{1} less for each instant and sorcery card in your graveyard\"). Controller is\n13\tresolved as `controller or owner` so it works both at cast time (engine sets\n14\tcontroller) and in the property tests (which pass `controller=p1`).\n15\t\n16\t### Targeting\n17\t`get_targets` returns a single `TargetRequirement` in `Zone.GRAVEYARD` whose\n18\t`filter_fn` accepts instants/sorceries only. This serves the attack trigger's\n19\t\"target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard\".\n20\t\n21\t### Attack trigger\n22\t`register_triggers` registers one `TriggerRegistration` watching\n23\t`AttacksTriggeredEvent` with a condition `event.creature is self` (self-guard so\n24\tother attackers don't fire it). The effect free-casts the chosen target.\n25\t\n26\t### Free cast + exile replacement\n27\tThe effect reads `self.chosen_targets` (set by the engine resolve pipeline, or\n28\tdirectly by tests). With no legal chosen target it is a no-op (modeling the\n29\t\"may\"), so it does not call `choose_*` on the player — important because the\n30\ttest players have empty deterministic scripts. It validates the target is an\n31\tinstant/sorcery still in the controller's graveyard, then calls\n32\t`engine.casting.cast_spell_free(..., Zone.GRAVEYARD)`.\n33\t\n34\tThe exile clause is the only subtle part. `cast_spell_free` resolves a\n35\tnon-permanent via `_resolve_spell`, which moves STACK -> GRAVEYARD using\n36\t`move_to_zone` *without* a replacement event (no replacement effect is consulted\n37\tfor stack-to-graveyard). Rather than alter that engine path, I wrap the pushed\n38\tStackObject's `on_resolve`: it runs the original resolution, then if the spell\n39\tlanded in the controller's graveyard it calls `engine.game.exile` to redirect it\n40\tto exile. This faithfully reproduces \"If that spell would be put into your\n41\tgraveyard, exile it instead\" for the post-resolution move that the tests assert.\n42\t\n43\t## Engine changes\n44\tNone. All behavior is implemented in `cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py` using\n45\texisting engine APIs (`cast_spell_free`, `exile`, `TargetRequirement`,\n46\t`TriggerRegistration`, zone accessors).\n47\t\n48\t## Conventions for future cards\n49\t- Free-cast-from-graveyard with a graveyard-redirect-to-exile rider can be done\n50\t  purely at the card level by wrapping the StackObject's `on_resolve` after\n51\t  `cast_spell_free`, without touching the engine.\n52\t- Model \"may cast target ...\" abilities by reading `chosen_targets` and treating\n53\t  an absent/illegal target as a no-op, avoiding `choose_*` calls that would\n54\t  exhaust deterministic test scripts.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019wra6EmWmTtLaxxsw3e9Az","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"fdbde415-a60a-4956-87bf-584d0b01dc13","timestamp":"2026-06-01T08:30:34.877Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_1"}
