{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_018aRPXWFz2pts5EhC4yQQBT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017tv2qVDPMV7pUN2arFDjXX","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/review.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 78,\n    \"comment\": \"get_targets() unconditionally advertises a GRAVEYARD instant/sorcery TargetRequirement at the card/spell level. The engine's cast pipeline (engine/casting.py cast_spell lines 174-190 and cast_spell_free lines 326-340) calls card.get_targets(game) when THE CREATURE SPELL ITSELF is cast and then forces player.choose_target on those specs. The Dawning Archaic is a creature with no spell targets, so casting it will wrongly require/consume a graveyard instant-or-sorcery target (and can raise CastingError when none is legal, e.g. empty graveyard). The graveyard-targeting requirement belongs only to the attack trigger's free-cast, not to get_targets() of the creature spell. Move/scope this targeting so the creature spell advertises no targets (e.g. the trigger effect should choose its own target rather than exposing it via the card-level get_targets hook).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 116,\n    \"comment\": \"_free_cast_from_graveyard reads self.chosen_targets to obtain the target, but the trigger pipeline (engine/triggers.py fire_event builds the trigger StackObject with on_resolve=trigger.effect and never sets targets/chosen_targets on the source). chosen_targets is only populated by _resolve_spell for a spell's own resolution, not for triggered abilities. So in real engine play (as opposed to the arbitrated tests that assign archaic.chosen_targets directly) this effect is effectively always a no-op and never free-casts. Flagged advisory because the tests for this behavior were already arbitrated to set chosen_targets directly; consider having the trigger effect actively choose a target (via the player) so the ability works in live play.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 146,\n    \"comment\": \"The exile-redirect relies on game.stack.peek() being the spell just pushed by cast_spell_free, guarded by stack_obj.source is target. This is correct in the current synchronous flow, but is fragile if anything pushes onto the stack between cast_spell_free and peek(). Minor robustness note only.\"\n  }\n]\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":891,"cache_read_input_tokens":30629,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":891,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019wra6EmWmTtLaxxsw3e9Az","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"b04ed22a-156e-410c-8100-9fd6792fb0e2","request_id":"req_011CbcEE6oFhLbJeZzdkKEAf","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_1"}
