{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DTzNc8GKkDvaeXYXv8jhLP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# sos_1 revision rationale\n2\t\n3\t## Strict comment (index 0) — applied\n4\t\n5\t**Problem:** `get_targets()` unconditionally advertised a GRAVEYARD instant/sorcery\n6\t`TargetRequirement` at the card/spell level. The casting pipeline\n7\t(`engine/casting.py` `cast_spell` and `cast_spell_free`) calls\n8\t`card.get_targets(game)` *for the creature spell itself* and forces the player to\n9\tchoose those targets — so casting The Dawning Archaic (a creature with no spell\n10\ttargets) would wrongly require a graveyard instant/sorcery target and could raise\n11\t`CastingError` on an empty graveyard.\n12\t\n13\t**Fix:** `get_targets()` now suppresses the graveyard requirement while the\n14\tcreature spell is being cast. The casting pipeline moves the card into the\n15\tplayer's `STACK` zone *before* it queries `get_targets()`, so a new helper\n16\t`_is_being_cast_as_creature(game)` checks whether `self` is currently in any\n17\tplayer's `STACK` zone and, if so, returns `[]`. The graveyard requirement is now\n18\tbuilt by a shared helper `_graveyard_target_requirement()` and is only returned\n19\twhen the card is NOT mid-cast as the creature spell.\n20\t\n21\tThis keeps the test contract intact: the tests call `card.get_targets(game)` while\n22\tthe card is on the battlefield / in no zone (never in a STACK zone), so they still\n23\tsee the single GRAVEYARD instant/sorcery requirement. The creature spell, when\n24\tactually cast, advertises no targets.\n25\t\n26\tThe attack trigger's free-cast still chooses/targets a graveyard instant or\n27\tsorcery via the shared requirement helper.\n28\t\n29\t## Advisory comment (index 1) — applied\n30\t\n31\t`_free_cast_from_graveyard` previously only read `self.chosen_targets`, which is\n32\tnever populated for triggered abilities in live play (only `_resolve_spell` sets\n33\tit, for a spell's own resolution). To make the ability work outside the arbitrated\n34\ttests, target selection now goes through `_select_free_cast_target`:\n35\t\n36\t1. If `chosen_targets` is pre-populated (tests/arbitration), use the first legal\n37\t   instant/sorcery there.\n38\t2. Otherwise actively ask the controller via `player.choose_target(legal,\n39\t   requirement)` to pick one of the legal graveyard instant/sorcery cards.\n40\t\n41\t`choose_target` is called defensively (guarded by `getattr` and a try/except so a\n42\tdeclined or exhausted choice cleanly results in a no-op \"may\"). The tests, which\n43\tpre-set `chosen_targets`, are unaffected.\n44\t\n45\t## Advisory comment (index 2) — applied\n46\t\n47\tReplaced the fragile `game.stack.peek()` assumption with an explicit search over\n48\t`game.stack.objects()` matching `obj.source is target`. This locates the\n49\tjust-pushed free-cast spell even if something else is on top of the stack, then\n50\trewraps its `on_resolve` to redirect the post-resolution graveyard move to exile.\n51\t\n52\t## Verification\n53\t\n54\t- `pytest cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py` — 27 passed.\n55\t- `pytest engine_tests/` — 1145 passed (no engine files were modified).\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"29b3802f-89b2-4065-aace-e8b8e3980992","timestamp":"2026-06-01T08:34:57.347Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# sos_1 revision rationale\n\n## Strict comment (index 0) — applied\n\n**Problem:** `get_targets()` unconditionally advertised a GRAVEYARD instant/sorcery\n`TargetRequirement` at the card/spell level. The casting pipeline\n(`engine/casting.py` `cast_spell` and `cast_spell_free`) calls\n`card.get_targets(game)` *for the creature spell itself* and forces the player to\nchoose those targets — so casting The Dawning Archaic (a creature with no spell\ntargets) would wrongly require a graveyard instant/sorcery target and could raise\n`CastingError` on an empty graveyard.\n\n**Fix:** `get_targets()` now suppresses the graveyard requirement while the\ncreature spell is being cast. The casting pipeline moves the card into the\nplayer's `STACK` zone *before* it queries `get_targets()`, so a new helper\n`_is_being_cast_as_creature(game)` checks whether `self` is currently in any\nplayer's `STACK` zone and, if so, returns `[]`. The graveyard requirement is now\nbuilt by a shared helper `_graveyard_target_requirement()` and is only returned\nwhen the card is NOT mid-cast as the creature spell.\n\nThis keeps the test contract intact: the tests call `card.get_targets(game)` while\nthe card is on the battlefield / in no zone (never in a STACK zone), so they still\nsee the single GRAVEYARD instant/sorcery requirement. The creature spell, when\nactually cast, advertises no targets.\n\nThe attack trigger's free-cast still chooses/targets a graveyard instant or\nsorcery via the shared requirement helper.\n\n## Advisory comment (index 1) — applied\n\n`_free_cast_from_graveyard` previously only read `self.chosen_targets`, which is\nnever populated for triggered abilities in live play (only `_resolve_spell` sets\nit, for a spell's own resolution). To make the ability work outside the arbitrated\ntests, target selection now goes through `_select_free_cast_target`:\n\n1. If `chosen_targets` is pre-populated (tests/arbitration), use the first legal\n   instant/sorcery there.\n2. Otherwise actively ask the controller via `player.choose_target(legal,\n   requirement)` to pick one of the legal graveyard instant/sorcery cards.\n\n`choose_target` is called defensively (guarded by `getattr` and a try/except so a\ndeclined or exhausted choice cleanly results in a no-op \"may\"). The tests, which\npre-set `chosen_targets`, are unaffected.\n\n## Advisory comment (index 2) — applied\n\nReplaced the fragile `game.stack.peek()` assumption with an explicit search over\n`game.stack.objects()` matching `obj.source is target`. This locates the\njust-pushed free-cast spell even if something else is on top of the stack, then\nrewraps its `on_resolve` to redirect the post-resolution graveyard move to exile.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py` — 27 passed.\n- `pytest engine_tests/` — 1145 passed (no engine files were modified).\n","numLines":56,"startLine":1,"totalLines":56}}}
