{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a811c69df989220d0","tool_use_id":"toolu_014vwTGsbMHjs8pBAQfXYvUx","description":"Writing /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/test-rationale.md","subagent_type":"Tester","usage":{"total_tokens":65217,"tool_uses":31,"duration_ms":149504},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"e1693676-6534-445c-8ba9-5d72b337a1a6","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_0113j4DUX22zmauggPZF33LA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R33SfWs2aoRLH1oem8kWMV","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test rationale — sos_4 Together as One\n\nCard: **Together as One** — `{6}` Sorcery (Converge).\nOracle: \"Converge — Target player draws X cards, Together as One deals X damage\nto any target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana\nspent to cast this spell.\"\n\nTest file: `cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py`\n\n## Engine contract this card relies on\n- Converge: the casting pipeline (`engine/casting.py`) writes the distinct\n  colors of mana spent to `card.colors_spent` as a **list** of\n  `engine.types.Color` (from `mana_pool.last_payment_colors`). X is therefore\n  `len(self.colors_spent)`. Tests set `colors_spent` directly (a list of\n  `Color`), matching the real pipeline shape, rather than an int.\n- Targeting: cards advertise targets via `get_targets()` returning a list of\n  `TargetRequirement`. Players are detected by `hasattr(obj, \"life\")`;\n  creatures by `CardType.CREATURE in card_types` (per existing FDN conventions,\n  e.g. fdn_192 \"any target\", fdn_202 \"target player\").\n- Resolution reads `self.chosen_targets` (set by the cast pipeline or test).\n- `deal_damage` / `draw_card` live in `engine.game`; controller life gain is a\n  direct `controller.life += X`.\n\n## Test classes and what each validates\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneProperties\n- `test_is_sorcery` — card is a `Sorcery`.\n- `test_name` / `test_mana_cost` — name and `{6}` cost match the spec.\n- `test_not_a_creature` — SORCERY in card_types, CREATURE absent (guards\n  against using the wrong base class).\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneTargeting\nValidates the spell exposes **two** targets in oracle order.\n- `test_returns_two_target_requirements` — exactly two `TargetRequirement`s.\n- `test_player_target_accepts_player_rejects_creature` — requirement[0] is\n  \"target player\": accepts a player, rejects a creature.\n- `test_any_target_accepts_player` / `test_any_target_accepts_creature` —\n  requirement[1] is \"any target\": accepts both a player and a creature.\n- `test_any_target_rejects_noncreature_nonplayer` — \"any target\" rejects a\n  non-creature, non-player object (an enchantment).\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneConvergeX\nDrives the three clauses off `len(colors_spent)`.\n- `test_colors_spent_defaults_empty` — with no payment, X would be 0.\n- `test_two_colors_target_player_draws_two` — the **target player** (not the\n  caster) draws X cards.\n- `test_three_colors_deals_three_damage_to_creature` — X damage to a creature\n  chosen as \"any target\".\n- `test_two_colors_deals_two_damage_to_player` — X damage to a player chosen as\n  \"any target\".\n- `test_controller_gains_x_life` — the caster gains X life.\n- `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player` — disambiguates \"you\":\n  the *controller* gains life even when the draw target is a different player,\n  and the damaged player is the chosen any-target, not the life-gain recipient.\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneZeroColors\nWhen only generic/colorless mana is spent, X = 0 and all three clauses no-op.\nThese are guard tests: an implementation that unconditionally draws / burns /\ngains would fail them.\n- `test_zero_colors_draws_nothing`\n- `test_zero_colors_deals_no_damage`\n- `test_zero_colors_gains_no_life`\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneFiveColors\n- `test_five_colors_full_effect` — a WUBRG payment sets X = 5 across draw,\n  damage, and life gain simultaneously (here the same player is both draw\n  target and any-target).\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneResolutionRobustness\n- `test_resolves_without_targets_is_noop` — resolving with `chosen_targets`\n  unset must not raise.\n- `test_resolves_without_colors_spent_is_noop` — resolving with `colors_spent`\n  unset (defaulting to empty) must not raise and produces no effect.\n\n## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered\n- **Optimal generic-mana coloring for Converge.** `engine/casting.py` notes a\n  TODO that generic mana is not auto-optimized for color count, and the test\n  harness does not let a card choose which colors to spend. X is therefore\n  tested by setting `colors_spent` directly rather than through a full mana\n  payment. Covered conceptually by setting the list explicitly.\n- **Full cast-through-the-pipeline of a `{6}` spell with multicolored mana.**\n  `cast_spell` does not provide multi-target scripting plus colored-mana\n  bookkeeping ergonomically; the per-clause behavior is verified at\n  `on_resolve` level instead, matching the FDN reference style (fdn_13,\n  fdn_205, fdn_202).\n- **Illegal/changed targets between cast and resolution** (e.g. target creature\n  leaves the battlefield). This is general engine targeting behavior, out of\n  scope for this card's contract beyond the no-op robustness checks.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1447,"cache_read_input_tokens":63547,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1447,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_014vwTGsbMHjs8pBAQfXYvUx","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"f65bfb8d-d133-447a-a7d3-de66a0d3e06e","request_id":"req_011CbcEf3ewPhYv9kALAswbQ","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_4"}
