{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GKvmbnaQ7Ahc2DiVqXtZNR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test rationale — sos_4 Together as One\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Together as One** — `{6}` Sorcery (Converge).\n4\tOracle: \"Converge — Target player draws X cards, Together as One deals X damage\n5\tto any target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana\n6\tspent to cast this spell.\"\n7\t\n8\tTest file: `cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py`\n9\t\n10\t## Engine contract this card relies on\n11\t- Converge: the casting pipeline (`engine/casting.py`) writes the distinct\n12\t  colors of mana spent to `card.colors_spent` as a **list** of\n13\t  `engine.types.Color` (from `mana_pool.last_payment_colors`). X is therefore\n14\t  `len(self.colors_spent)`. Tests set `colors_spent` directly (a list of\n15\t  `Color`), matching the real pipeline shape, rather than an int.\n16\t- Targeting: cards advertise targets via `get_targets()` returning a list of\n17\t  `TargetRequirement`. Players are detected by `hasattr(obj, \"life\")`;\n18\t  creatures by `CardType.CREATURE in card_types` (per existing FDN conventions,\n19\t  e.g. fdn_192 \"any target\", fdn_202 \"target player\").\n20\t- Resolution reads `self.chosen_targets` (set by the cast pipeline or test).\n21\t- `deal_damage` / `draw_card` live in `engine.game`; controller life gain is a\n22\t  direct `controller.life += X`.\n23\t\n24\t## Test classes and what each validates\n25\t\n26\t### TestTogetherAsOneProperties\n27\t- `test_is_sorcery` — card is a `Sorcery`.\n28\t- `test_name` / `test_mana_cost` — name and `{6}` cost match the spec.\n29\t- `test_not_a_creature` — SORCERY in card_types, CREATURE absent (guards\n30\t  against using the wrong base class).\n31\t\n32\t### TestTogetherAsOneTargeting\n33\tValidates the spell exposes **two** targets in oracle order.\n34\t- `test_returns_two_target_requirements` — exactly two `TargetRequirement`s.\n35\t- `test_player_target_accepts_player_rejects_creature` — requirement[0] is\n36\t  \"target player\": accepts a player, rejects a creature.\n37\t- `test_any_target_accepts_player` / `test_any_target_accepts_creature` —\n38\t  requirement[1] is \"any target\": accepts both a player and a creature.\n39\t- `test_any_target_rejects_noncreature_nonplayer` — \"any target\" rejects a\n40\t  non-creature, non-player object (an enchantment).\n41\t\n42\t### TestTogetherAsOneConvergeX\n43\tDrives the three clauses off `len(colors_spent)`.\n44\t- `test_colors_spent_defaults_empty` — with no payment, X would be 0.\n45\t- `test_two_colors_target_player_draws_two` — the **target player** (not the\n46\t  caster) draws X cards.\n47\t- `test_three_colors_deals_three_damage_to_creature` — X damage to a creature\n48\t  chosen as \"any target\".\n49\t- `test_two_colors_deals_two_damage_to_player` — X damage to a player chosen as\n50\t  \"any target\".\n51\t- `test_controller_gains_x_life` — the caster gains X life.\n52\t- `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player` — disambiguates \"you\":\n53\t  the *controller* gains life even when the draw target is a different player,\n54\t  and the damaged player is the chosen any-target, not the life-gain recipient.\n55\t\n56\t### TestTogetherAsOneZeroColors\n57\tWhen only generic/colorless mana is spent, X = 0 and all three clauses no-op.\n58\tThese are guard tests: an implementation that unconditionally draws / burns /\n59\tgains would fail them.\n60\t- `test_zero_colors_draws_nothing`\n61\t- `test_zero_colors_deals_no_damage`\n62\t- `test_zero_colors_gains_no_life`\n63\t\n64\t### TestTogetherAsOneFiveColors\n65\t- `test_five_colors_full_effect` — a WUBRG payment sets X = 5 across draw,\n66\t  damage, and life gain simultaneously (here the same player is both draw\n67\t  target and any-target).\n68\t\n69\t### TestTogetherAsOneResolutionRobustness\n70\t- `test_resolves_without_targets_is_noop` — resolving with `chosen_targets`\n71\t  unset must not raise.\n72\t- `test_resolves_without_colors_spent_is_noop` — resolving with `colors_spent`\n73\t  unset (defaulting to empty) must not raise and produces no effect.\n74\t\n75\t## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered\n76\t- **Optimal generic-mana coloring for Converge.** `engine/casting.py` notes a\n77\t  TODO that generic mana is not auto-optimized for color count, and the test\n78\t  harness does not let a card choose which colors to spend. X is therefore\n79\t  tested by setting `colors_spent` directly rather than through a full mana\n80\t  payment. Covered conceptually by setting the list explicitly.\n81\t- **Full cast-through-the-pipeline of a `{6}` spell with multicolored mana.**\n82\t  `cast_spell` does not provide multi-target scripting plus colored-mana\n83\t  bookkeeping ergonomically; the per-clause behavior is verified at\n84\t  `on_resolve` level instead, matching the FDN reference style (fdn_13,\n85\t  fdn_205, fdn_202).\n86\t- **Illegal/changed targets between cast and resolution** (e.g. target creature\n87\t  leaves the battlefield). This is general engine targeting behavior, out of\n88\t  scope for this card's contract beyond the no-op robustness checks.\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"ef3110fd-42c6-436b-8bbb-7a6177fe6978","timestamp":"2026-06-01T08:42:10.579Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test rationale — sos_4 Together as One\n\nCard: **Together as One** — `{6}` Sorcery (Converge).\nOracle: \"Converge — Target player draws X cards, Together as One deals X damage\nto any target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana\nspent to cast this spell.\"\n\nTest file: `cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py`\n\n## Engine contract this card relies on\n- Converge: the casting pipeline (`engine/casting.py`) writes the distinct\n  colors of mana spent to `card.colors_spent` as a **list** of\n  `engine.types.Color` (from `mana_pool.last_payment_colors`). X is therefore\n  `len(self.colors_spent)`. Tests set `colors_spent` directly (a list of\n  `Color`), matching the real pipeline shape, rather than an int.\n- Targeting: cards advertise targets via `get_targets()` returning a list of\n  `TargetRequirement`. Players are detected by `hasattr(obj, \"life\")`;\n  creatures by `CardType.CREATURE in card_types` (per existing FDN conventions,\n  e.g. fdn_192 \"any target\", fdn_202 \"target player\").\n- Resolution reads `self.chosen_targets` (set by the cast pipeline or test).\n- `deal_damage` / `draw_card` live in `engine.game`; controller life gain is a\n  direct `controller.life += X`.\n\n## Test classes and what each validates\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneProperties\n- `test_is_sorcery` — card is a `Sorcery`.\n- `test_name` / `test_mana_cost` — name and `{6}` cost match the spec.\n- `test_not_a_creature` — SORCERY in card_types, CREATURE absent (guards\n  against using the wrong base class).\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneTargeting\nValidates the spell exposes **two** targets in oracle order.\n- `test_returns_two_target_requirements` — exactly two `TargetRequirement`s.\n- `test_player_target_accepts_player_rejects_creature` — requirement[0] is\n  \"target player\": accepts a player, rejects a creature.\n- `test_any_target_accepts_player` / `test_any_target_accepts_creature` —\n  requirement[1] is \"any target\": accepts both a player and a creature.\n- `test_any_target_rejects_noncreature_nonplayer` — \"any target\" rejects a\n  non-creature, non-player object (an enchantment).\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneConvergeX\nDrives the three clauses off `len(colors_spent)`.\n- `test_colors_spent_defaults_empty` — with no payment, X would be 0.\n- `test_two_colors_target_player_draws_two` — the **target player** (not the\n  caster) draws X cards.\n- `test_three_colors_deals_three_damage_to_creature` — X damage to a creature\n  chosen as \"any target\".\n- `test_two_colors_deals_two_damage_to_player` — X damage to a player chosen as\n  \"any target\".\n- `test_controller_gains_x_life` — the caster gains X life.\n- `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player` — disambiguates \"you\":\n  the *controller* gains life even when the draw target is a different player,\n  and the damaged player is the chosen any-target, not the life-gain recipient.\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneZeroColors\nWhen only generic/colorless mana is spent, X = 0 and all three clauses no-op.\nThese are guard tests: an implementation that unconditionally draws / burns /\ngains would fail them.\n- `test_zero_colors_draws_nothing`\n- `test_zero_colors_deals_no_damage`\n- `test_zero_colors_gains_no_life`\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneFiveColors\n- `test_five_colors_full_effect` — a WUBRG payment sets X = 5 across draw,\n  damage, and life gain simultaneously (here the same player is both draw\n  target and any-target).\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneResolutionRobustness\n- `test_resolves_without_targets_is_noop` — resolving with `chosen_targets`\n  unset must not raise.\n- `test_resolves_without_colors_spent_is_noop` — resolving with `colors_spent`\n  unset (defaulting to empty) must not raise and produces no effect.\n\n## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered\n- **Optimal generic-mana coloring for Converge.** `engine/casting.py` notes a\n  TODO that generic mana is not auto-optimized for color count, and the test\n  harness does not let a card choose which colors to spend. X is therefore\n  tested by setting `colors_spent` directly rather than through a full mana\n  payment. Covered conceptually by setting the list explicitly.\n- **Full cast-through-the-pipeline of a `{6}` spell with multicolored mana.**\n  `cast_spell` does not provide multi-target scripting plus colored-mana\n  bookkeeping ergonomically; the per-clause behavior is verified at\n  `on_resolve` level instead, matching the FDN reference style (fdn_13,\n  fdn_205, fdn_202).\n- **Illegal/changed targets between cast and resolution** (e.g. target creature\n  leaves the battlefield). This is general engine targeting behavior, out of\n  scope for this card's contract beyond the no-op robustness checks.\n","numLines":89,"startLine":1,"totalLines":89}}}
