{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Hh6v2sBKj1KwagNBWW1TGm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KjACso4G83Xyvi5o4dZA8K","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator directives — sos_4 (dispute resolution)\n\n**Decision: the Implementer's feasibility objection is upheld.** The suite's\nconvention is fixed as:\n- `chosen_targets[0]` = the \"target player\" that draws X\n- `chosen_targets[1]` = the \"any target\" that takes X damage\n- life gain = the controller (caster)\n\nThis convention is correct and matches the oracle text. Do NOT change the\nimplementation's mapping. Do NOT touch any other test.\n\n## Rewrite ONLY this one test\n`TestTogetherAsOneConvergeX::test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player`\n(`cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py`, ~L180-198).\n\nIts current data `card.chosen_targets = [p2, p1]` is internally inconsistent with\nthe rest of the suite: it names p1 (the controller, index 1) as the damage\nany-target, yet asserts p2 is the one damaged. Under the index-1=damage\nconvention that the other tests require, that is impossible.\n\nFix: change the data to `card.chosen_targets = [p2, p2]` so the draw target is p2\nand the \"any target\" damaged is also p2. Keep the assertions that express the\ntest's real intent:\n- the **controller** p1 gains X life (e.g. `p1.life == 22` for X=2),\n- p2 (the chosen any-target) takes X damage (`p2.life == 18`),\n- the life gain does NOT go to the draw/target player.\n\nDo not weaken the test's intent — it must still prove \"you\" = controller, not the\ntarget player. Only the `chosen_targets` data and any directly-dependent\nassertions need correcting for consistency.\n\nLeave all other tests in the file exactly as they are.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13