{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013UZpBmey3WnwJMESSYdSE7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# sos_4 Together as One — Implementation Rationale\n2\t\n3\t## Approach\n4\t`TogetherAsOne` subclasses `engine.card.Sorcery` ({6}, no power/toughness).\n5\t\n6\t- `colors_spent` is initialized to an empty list in `__init__`; X = `len(colors_spent)`\n7\t  per the Converge convention (the casting pipeline records distinct colors spent\n8\t  as a list of `Color`). This mirrors fdn_205 but as a list (per the Tester note),\n9\t  not an int.\n10\t- `get_targets()` advertises exactly two `TargetRequirement`s:\n11\t  1. \"target player\" — `_is_player`: has a `life` attribute and no `card_types`\n12\t     (accepts players, rejects creatures).\n13\t  2. \"any target\" — `_is_any_target`: a creature OR a player (rejects a\n14\t     non-creature/non-player permanent such as a plain Enchantment).\n15\t- `on_resolve()`:\n16\t  - `chosen_targets[0]` = the target player who draws X cards (via `draw_card`).\n17\t  - `chosen_targets[1]` = the \"any target\" that takes X damage (via `deal_damage`,\n18\t    with `self` as source).\n19\t  - The controller (`self.controller` or `self.owner`) gains X life directly\n20\t    (`controller.life += x`); there is no `gain_life` engine helper.\n21\t  - X <= 0 short-circuits to a no-op; missing `chosen_targets`/`colors_spent` are\n22\t    handled defensively so resolution never raises.\n23\t\n24\t## chosen_targets convention\n25\tOrder is `[draw_target, damage_target]`, derived from the dominant pattern across\n26\tthe tests (index 0 = draw target; index 1 = \"any target\" damage). Life gain always\n27\tgoes to the controller, independent of either target.\n28\t\n29\t## Engine changes\n30\tNone. Implemented entirely within the card using existing helpers\n31\t(`engine.game.draw_card`, `engine.game.deal_damage`).\n32\t\n33\t## Dispute\n34\tOne test, `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player`, is internally\n35\tinconsistent with the rest of the suite: it sets `chosen_targets = [p2, p1]`\n36\t(so index 1 = the controller p1) but asserts p2 takes the damage and p1 only\n37\tgains life. That requires the damage target to be index 0, the opposite of\n38\t`test_two_colors_deals_two_damage_to_player` (`[p1, p2]` → index 1 damaged).\n39\tNo single index mapping satisfies both. See `test-dispute.md`. 20/21 tests pass;\n40\tthe disputed one would pass if its data were `[p2, p2]`.\n41\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"6b4def2e-141b-47a0-b328-26b8fb82abbd","timestamp":"2026-06-01T08:44:41.962Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/impl-rationale.md","content":"# sos_4 Together as One — Implementation Rationale\n\n## Approach\n`TogetherAsOne` subclasses `engine.card.Sorcery` ({6}, no power/toughness).\n\n- `colors_spent` is initialized to an empty list in `__init__`; X = `len(colors_spent)`\n  per the Converge convention (the casting pipeline records distinct colors spent\n  as a list of `Color`). This mirrors fdn_205 but as a list (per the Tester note),\n  not an int.\n- `get_targets()` advertises exactly two `TargetRequirement`s:\n  1. \"target player\" — `_is_player`: has a `life` attribute and no `card_types`\n     (accepts players, rejects creatures).\n  2. \"any target\" — `_is_any_target`: a creature OR a player (rejects a\n     non-creature/non-player permanent such as a plain Enchantment).\n- `on_resolve()`:\n  - `chosen_targets[0]` = the target player who draws X cards (via `draw_card`).\n  - `chosen_targets[1]` = the \"any target\" that takes X damage (via `deal_damage`,\n    with `self` as source).\n  - The controller (`self.controller` or `self.owner`) gains X life directly\n    (`controller.life += x`); there is no `gain_life` engine helper.\n  - X <= 0 short-circuits to a no-op; missing `chosen_targets`/`colors_spent` are\n    handled defensively so resolution never raises.\n\n## chosen_targets convention\nOrder is `[draw_target, damage_target]`, derived from the dominant pattern across\nthe tests (index 0 = draw target; index 1 = \"any target\" damage). Life gain always\ngoes to the controller, independent of either target.\n\n## Engine changes\nNone. Implemented entirely within the card using existing helpers\n(`engine.game.draw_card`, `engine.game.deal_damage`).\n\n## Dispute\nOne test, `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player`, is internally\ninconsistent with the rest of the suite: it sets `chosen_targets = [p2, p1]`\n(so index 1 = the controller p1) but asserts p2 takes the damage and p1 only\ngains life. That requires the damage target to be index 0, the opposite of\n`test_two_colors_deals_two_damage_to_player` (`[p1, p2]` → index 1 damaged).\nNo single index mapping satisfies both. See `test-dispute.md`. 20/21 tests pass;\nthe disputed one would pass if its data were `[p2, p2]`.\n","numLines":41,"startLine":1,"totalLines":41}}}
