{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013dnMquwAjmB1PKx9g9S9DP","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"2e95e28f-73e5-4183-a319-bdb870c5c5d7","timestamp":"2026-06-01T08:44:51.374Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"triggered ability choose its own target (via `player.choose_target`) at resolution.\n","newString":"triggered ability choose its own target (via `player.choose_target`) at resolution.\n\n## Converge / multi-target / life-gain conventions (from sos_4)\n- **Converge X** = `len(self.colors_spent)`. The casting pipeline records the\n  distinct colors of mana spent as a LIST of `engine.types.Color` on\n  `card.colors_spent` (not an int). Initialize `colors_spent` to `[]` in\n  `__init__`; compute X with `len(...)`. (Note: fdn_205 used an int because it\n  bypassed the cast pipeline — prefer the list shape for real cards.)\n- **Multi-target ordering**: `chosen_targets` is ordered to match the oracle text\n  order of the `TargetRequirement`s returned by `get_targets()`. E.g. \"Target\n  player ... deals X damage to any target\" → `chosen_targets[0]` = target player,\n  `chosen_targets[1]` = any-target.\n- **Life gain**: there is no `gain_life` engine helper. Gain life directly via\n  `controller.life += x`. Damage uses `engine.game.deal_damage`, draw uses\n  `engine.game.draw_card`.\n- Resolution should short-circuit on X <= 0 and defend against missing\n  `chosen_targets`/`colors_spent` so it never raises.\n","originalFile":"# Key Decisions\n\nPersistent, append-only conventions and decisions across runs.\n\n## Card-level `get_targets()` vs. triggered-ability targets (from sos_1)\nThe casting pipeline (`engine/casting.py`) calls `card.get_targets(game)` for the\nSPELL ITSELF and forces the controller to choose those targets when the spell is\ncast. So `get_targets()` must only advertise targets the *spell* takes. If a card's\ntargeting belongs to a triggered ability (e.g. \"whenever this attacks, target ...\"),\ndo NOT expose it via the card-level `get_targets()` — otherwise casting the permanent\nwrongly requires/consumes a target (and can raise `CastingError` when none is legal).\nThe pipeline moves the card into the controller's `STACK` zone before querying\n`get_targets()`, so a card can detect \"am I being cast right now?\" by checking\nwhether `self` is in any player's `STACK` zone and return `[]` in that case. Have the\ntriggered ability choose its own target (via `player.choose_target`) at resolution.\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":3,"newStart":14,"newLines":19,"lines":[" whether `self` is in any player's `STACK` zone and return `[]` in that case. Have the"," triggered ability choose its own target (via `player.choose_target`) at resolution."," ","+## Converge / multi-target / life-gain conventions (from sos_4)","+- **Converge X** = `len(self.colors_spent)`. The casting pipeline records the","+  distinct colors of mana spent as a LIST of `engine.types.Color` on","+  `card.colors_spent` (not an int). Initialize `colors_spent` to `[]` in","+  `__init__`; compute X with `len(...)`. (Note: fdn_205 used an int because it","+  bypassed the cast pipeline — prefer the list shape for real cards.)","+- **Multi-target ordering**: `chosen_targets` is ordered to match the oracle text","+  order of the `TargetRequirement`s returned by `get_targets()`. E.g. \"Target","+  player ... deals X damage to any target\" → `chosen_targets[0]` = target player,","+  `chosen_targets[1]` = any-target.","+- **Life gain**: there is no `gain_life` engine helper. Gain life directly via","+  `controller.life += x`. Damage uses `engine.game.deal_damage`, draw uses","+  `engine.game.draw_card`.","+- Resolution should short-circuit on X <= 0 and defend against missing","+  `chosen_targets`/`colors_spent` so it never raises.","+"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
