{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01XV31jK1x3KnSS77hnBRAZB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013WYrCixJCLRXdKfrex4ycQ","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md","old_string":"## Test dispute: sos_4","new_string":"## Untestable resolution: sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n- **Item 1 — \"Prepared\" keyword as a first-class flag**: resolved via (a) build it.\n  Implementer adds `PREPARED` to `engine.types.Keyword` (additive) and declares it\n  on the creature face. Tester re-invoked once to add a keyword-membership test.\n- **Item 2 — \"cast a copy of its spell while prepared, unpreparing it\"**: resolved\n  via (b) accept partial coverage. Requires major copy-cast/split-card engine\n  machinery; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:` marker added in card_impl.py.\n- **Item 3 — the \"Swords to Plowshares\" {W} instant face**: resolved via (b). The\n  engine has no second-castable-face representation; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:`\n  marker added in card_impl.py.\n- The conditional prepared STATE is exposed as an `is_prepared` bool (tested).\n\n## Test dispute: sos_4"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2984,"cache_read_input_tokens":49910,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2984},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"15b5abe9-146c-4981-9bff-b19fbc71e324","request_id":"req_011CbcFSDCRMKekj1dUsK36G"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013WYrCixJCLRXdKfrex4ycQ","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"aae3e328-bb1a-4f5d-b4da-232581d953fd","timestamp":"2026-06-01T08:48:12.899Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"## Test dispute: sos_4","newString":"## Untestable resolution: sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n- **Item 1 — \"Prepared\" keyword as a first-class flag**: resolved via (a) build it.\n  Implementer adds `PREPARED` to `engine.types.Keyword` (additive) and declares it\n  on the creature face. Tester re-invoked once to add a keyword-membership test.\n- **Item 2 — \"cast a copy of its spell while prepared, unpreparing it\"**: resolved\n  via (b) accept partial coverage. Requires major copy-cast/split-card engine\n  machinery; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:` marker added in card_impl.py.\n- **Item 3 — the \"Swords to Plowshares\" {W} instant face**: resolved via (b). The\n  engine has no second-castable-face representation; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:`\n  marker added in card_impl.py.\n- The conditional prepared STATE is exposed as an `is_prepared` bool (tested).\n\n## Test dispute: sos_4","originalFile":"# Run Decisions\n\nDecisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n\n## Test dispute: sos_4\n- **Disputed test**: `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player` (tests.py L180-198)\n- **Tester's intent**: verify \"you gain X life\" goes to the controller, not the target player, while the chosen any-target takes damage.\n- **Implementer's objection (feasibility)**: the test uses `chosen_targets=[p2, p1]`, naming p1 (controller) as the damage any-target (index 1), but asserts p2 (index 0) is damaged. This contradicts `test_two_colors_deals_two_damage_to_player` ([p1,p2] -> p2 damaged at index 1). No single index mapping satisfies both.\n- **Decision**: accept implementer (feasibility objection — test data is internally contradictory). Convention is draw=chosen_targets[0], damage any-target=chosen_targets[1], life gain=controller.\n- **Action**: re-invoke Tester to rewrite ONLY the disputed test, changing its data to `[p2, p2]` (draw target p2, damage any-target p2) so the intended \"life goes to controller p1\" check holds under the suite's index-1=damage convention.\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":6,"newStart":2,"newLines":18,"lines":[" "," Decisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`."," ","+## Untestable resolution: sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)","+- **Item 1 — \"Prepared\" keyword as a first-class flag**: resolved via (a) build it.","+  Implementer adds `PREPARED` to `engine.types.Keyword` (additive) and declares it","+  on the creature face. Tester re-invoked once to add a keyword-membership test.","+- **Item 2 — \"cast a copy of its spell while prepared, unpreparing it\"**: resolved","+  via (b) accept partial coverage. Requires major copy-cast/split-card engine","+  machinery; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:` marker added in card_impl.py.","+- **Item 3 — the \"Swords to Plowshares\" {W} instant face**: resolved via (b). The","+  engine has no second-castable-face representation; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:`","+  marker added in card_impl.py.","+- The conditional prepared STATE is exposed as an `is_prepared` bool (tested).","+"," ## Test dispute: sos_4"," - **Disputed test**: `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player` (tests.py L180-198)"," - **Tester's intent**: verify \"you gain X life\" goes to the controller, not the target player, while the chosen any-target takes damage."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Bp3J4GBoqEiTGNZuL8nCvg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HaKNPU6WbaH5aNferGK3oc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator directives — sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n\nThis card is a split card whose full mechanics exceed current engine support. The\ncoordinator has scoped the implementation as follows. Implement the **creature\nface** (`Emeritus of Truce`) fully; record the unsupported portions with grep-able\nmarkers.\n\n## Build (in scope)\n1. **Creature face** `Emeritus of Truce` — `{1}{W}{W}`, 3/3, Cat Cleric, white.\n2. **ETB ability**: \"When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white\n   and black Inkling creature token with flying.\" The token enters under the\n   TARGETED player's control. Token: 1/1, white+black, flying, subtype Inkling,\n   `is_token=True`.\n3. **Conditional prepared state**: \"Then if an opponent controls more creatures\n   than you, this creature becomes prepared.\" Expose this as an `is_prepared`\n   boolean on the card (default `False`); set it `True` only when an opponent\n   controls STRICTLY more creatures than the controller, evaluated after the token\n   resolves.\n4. **Prepared keyword (untestable item 1 — BUILD IT)**: Add a new `PREPARED`\n   member to `engine.types.Keyword` (ADDITIVE only — do not rename/remove existing\n   members). Declare `Keyword.PREPARED` in the creature face's keywords so the card\n   advertises it as a first-class keyword. The runtime conditional state stays the\n   `is_prepared` bool.\n5. **Targeting**: per KEY_DECISIONS.md (sos_1 convention), the \"target player\"\n   belongs to the ETB triggered ability, NOT the creature spell. `get_targets()`\n   must return `[]` while the card is in a STACK zone (being cast).\n\n## Record as UNVERIFIED (out of scope — DO NOT attempt full engine support)\nAdd `# UNVERIFIED: <requirement> — <reason>` comments in `cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py`\nso the gaps are grep-able:\n- **Item 2**: \"While prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell; doing so\n  unprepares it.\" — no copy-cast / split-face casting machinery in the engine.\n- **Item 3**: the `Swords to Plowshares` {W} instant face (exile target creature;\n  its controller gains life equal to its power) — engine has no second castable\n  face representation.\n\nYou MAY still store the spell-face metadata (name half, etc.) if convenient, but\ndo not build the copy-cast or instant-face resolution.\n\n## Constraints\n- Make ALL tests in `cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` pass. Do NOT modify tests.\n- Engine changes additive only; do not touch engine_tests/ or FDN tests.\n- After your changes, run `pytest engine_tests/` to confirm the new Keyword member\n  didn't regress anything.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2710,"cache_read_input_tokens":52894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2710},"output_tokens":46,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"e50fabb8-4458-40c4-871a-b1d430560618","request_id":"req_011CbcFUeYEEzMASwxwRMkRL"}
