{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012T6ypmYCms5CN2nA8wS5FB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale — sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n2\t\n3\tCard spec (creature face): `Emeritus of Truce` — `{1}{W}{W}` — 3/3 —\n4\tCreature — Cat Cleric — keyword `Prepared`.\n5\t\n6\tOracle text:\n7\t> When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white and black\n8\t> Inkling creature token with flying. Then if an opponent controls more\n9\t> creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared. (While it's prepared,\n10\t> you may cast a copy of its spell. Doing so unprepares it.)\n11\t\n12\tSpell face: `Swords to Plowshares` — `{W}` — Instant.\n13\t\n14\tTest file: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py`\n15\t\n16\tThe card mixes several mechanics, some of which the current engine cannot\n17\texpress (the `Prepared` keyword as a first-class flag, casting a copy of the\n18\tspell face, and the `Swords to Plowshares` instant face itself). The tests\n19\tassert every requirement the engine *can* express today; the rest are recorded\n20\tin `untestable.json`.\n21\t\n22\t## Helpers\n23\t\n24\t- `_inkling_tokens(game, player)` — collects every token on a player's\n25\t  battlefield whose subtypes include `\"Inkling\"`.\n26\t- `_resolve_etb(card, game)` — drives the enters-the-battlefield effect. It\n27\t  first calls `on_resolve` (the pattern used by the FDN 205 converge reference,\n28\t  which models a \"When this creature enters\" ability inside `on_resolve`). If\n29\t  that left the stack empty (implying a trigger-based contract instead), it\n30\t  falls back to registering triggers and firing an\n31\t  `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`, then drains the stack. This keeps the\n32\t  behavioural tests robust to either reasonable implementation contract.\n33\t\n34\t## TestEmeritusProperties\n35\t\n36\tStatic card data for the **creature face** (the face that is a permanent):\n37\t\n38\t- `test_is_creature` — instance of `Creature`, has `CardType.CREATURE`.\n39\t- `test_name` — full split name `\"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\"`.\n40\t- `test_creature_face_mana_cost` — `{1}{W}{W}` (the permanent face's cost).\n41\t- `test_power_toughness` — base 3/3.\n42\t- `test_subtypes_cat_cleric` — subtypes include `Cat` and `Cleric`.\n43\t- `test_is_white` — mono-white (derived from mana cost via `card_colors`).\n44\t\n45\t## TestEmeritusInklingToken\n46\t\n47\tThe ETB token requirement — \"target player creates a 1/1 white and black\n48\tInkling creature token with flying\":\n49\t\n50\t- `test_etb_creates_one_inkling_for_chosen_player` — exactly one Inkling\n51\t  appears on the chosen player's battlefield.\n52\t- `test_inkling_is_one_one` — token base P/T is 1/1.\n53\t- `test_inkling_has_flying` — token has `Keyword.FLYING`.\n54\t- `test_inkling_is_white_and_black` — token exposes colors and they include\n55\t  both white and black.\n56\t- `test_inkling_is_a_token` — `is_token` is `True`.\n57\t- `test_token_created_for_targeted_opponent_not_controller` — validates the\n58\t  \"**target player**\" clause: when the controller targets the opponent, the\n59\t  token enters under the opponent's control, not the controller's.\n60\t\n61\t## TestEmeritusTargeting\n62\t\n63\t- `test_no_targets_while_on_stack` — following the sos_1 convention recorded\n64\t  in `KEY_DECISIONS.md`, the \"target player\" belongs to the ETB triggered\n65\t  ability, not the creature spell. While the card sits in a STACK zone (being\n66\t  cast), `get_targets` must return `[]` so the cast pipeline doesn't wrongly\n67\t  consume a target.\n68\t\n69\t## TestEmeritusBecomesPrepared\n70\t\n71\tThe conditional \"Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this\n72\tcreature becomes prepared.\" Since the engine has no `Prepared` keyword/flag,\n73\tthe contract is assumed to expose the result as an `is_prepared` boolean on the\n74\tcard (defaulting to `False`).\n75\t\n76\t- `test_not_prepared_by_default` — fresh card is not prepared.\n77\t- `test_becomes_prepared_when_opponent_has_more_creatures` — opponent ends with\n78\t  strictly more creatures than the controller after the token resolves ⇒\n79\t  `is_prepared` becomes `True`.\n80\t- `test_not_prepared_when_counts_equal` — equal counts ⇒ not prepared (the\n81\t  clause requires *more*, not *>=*).\n82\t- `test_not_prepared_when_you_have_more_creatures` — controller ahead ⇒ not\n83\t  prepared.\n84\t\n85\t## TestEmeritusRobustness\n86\t\n87\t- `test_resolve_without_chosen_target_does_not_raise` — resolving with no\n88\t  chosen target must not raise (defensive, matching the FDN 13 no-op-target\n89\t  convention).\n90\t\n91\t## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (see untestable.json)\n92\t\n93\t- The `Prepared` keyword as a first-class engine `Keyword` flag — it does not\n94\t  exist in `engine.types.Keyword`.\n95\t- Casting a copy of the spell face while prepared, and unpreparing afterward —\n96\t  no copy-casting / split-card-face machinery in the engine.\n97\t- The `Swords to Plowshares` instant face (exile target creature; its\n98\t  controller gains life equal to its power) — the engine has no split / DFC\n99\t  representation that exposes the second face as a castable spell.\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018HjxydzbZjdJ1XwBSsXCWM","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"9be88820-621a-4778-adce-aed950d7699e","timestamp":"2026-06-01T08:51:47.488Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_13"}
