{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015TPm4RTFZhQdWQ1mi89iE1","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"cdacc278-0237-46bf-b5c7-a06390e5de9f","timestamp":"2026-06-01T08:52:29.390Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"- **Item 1 — \"Prepared\" keyword as a first-class flag**: resolved via (a) build it.\n  Implementer adds `PREPARED` to `engine.types.Keyword` (additive) and declares it\n  on the creature face. Tester re-invoked once to add a keyword-membership test.","newString":"- **Item 1 — \"Prepared\" keyword as a first-class flag**: INITIALLY directed as (a)\n  build it, but DOWNGRADED to (b) accept partial coverage. Adding `PREPARED` to\n  `engine.types.Keyword` regresses the authoritative read-only engine test\n  `engine_tests/test_types.py::TestKeyword::test_exactly_sixteen_members`\n  (asserts `len(Keyword) == 16`). Since engine_tests/ is authoritative for grading\n  and must not be modified, the keyword cannot be added without zeroing that test.\n  Implementer correctly declined and marked it `# UNVERIFIED`. The prepared state is\n  fully expressed via the `is_prepared` bool (tested). No Tester re-invocation.","originalFile":"# Run Decisions\n\nDecisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n- **Item 1 — \"Prepared\" keyword as a first-class flag**: resolved via (a) build it.\n  Implementer adds `PREPARED` to `engine.types.Keyword` (additive) and declares it\n  on the creature face. Tester re-invoked once to add a keyword-membership test.\n- **Item 2 — \"cast a copy of its spell while prepared, unpreparing it\"**: resolved\n  via (b) accept partial coverage. Requires major copy-cast/split-card engine\n  machinery; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:` marker added in card_impl.py.\n- **Item 3 — the \"Swords to Plowshares\" {W} instant face**: resolved via (b). The\n  engine has no second-castable-face representation; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:`\n  marker added in card_impl.py.\n- The conditional prepared STATE is exposed as an `is_prepared` bool (tested).\n\n## Test dispute: sos_4\n- **Disputed test**: `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player` (tests.py L180-198)\n- **Tester's intent**: verify \"you gain X life\" goes to the controller, not the target player, while the chosen any-target takes damage.\n- **Implementer's objection (feasibility)**: the test uses `chosen_targets=[p2, p1]`, naming p1 (controller) as the damage any-target (index 1), but asserts p2 (index 0) is damaged. This contradicts `test_two_colors_deals_two_damage_to_player` ([p1,p2] -> p2 damaged at index 1). No single index mapping satisfies both.\n- **Decision**: accept implementer (feasibility objection — test data is internally contradictory). Convention is draw=chosen_targets[0], damage any-target=chosen_targets[1], life gain=controller.\n- **Action**: re-invoke Tester to rewrite ONLY the disputed test, changing its data to `[p2, p2]` (draw target p2, damage any-target p2) so the intended \"life goes to controller p1\" check holds under the suite's index-1=damage convention.\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":9,"newStart":3,"newLines":14,"lines":[" Decisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`."," "," ## Untestable resolution: sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)","-- **Item 1 — \"Prepared\" keyword as a first-class flag**: resolved via (a) build it.","-  Implementer adds `PREPARED` to `engine.types.Keyword` (additive) and declares it","-  on the creature face. Tester re-invoked once to add a keyword-membership test.","+- **Item 1 — \"Prepared\" keyword as a first-class flag**: INITIALLY directed as (a)","+  build it, but DOWNGRADED to (b) accept partial coverage. Adding `PREPARED` to","+  `engine.types.Keyword` regresses the authoritative read-only engine test","+  `engine_tests/test_types.py::TestKeyword::test_exactly_sixteen_members`","+  (asserts `len(Keyword) == 16`). Since engine_tests/ is authoritative for grading","+  and must not be modified, the keyword cannot be added without zeroing that test.","+  Implementer correctly declined and marked it `# UNVERIFIED`. The prepared state is","+  fully expressed via the `is_prepared` bool (tested). No Tester re-invocation."," - **Item 2 — \"cast a copy of its spell while prepared, unpreparing it\"**: resolved","   via (b) accept partial coverage. Requires major copy-cast/split-card engine","   machinery; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:` marker added in card_impl.py."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
