{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EEtD3BbkqRDDi1Qv2BEusK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares — Implementation rationale\n2\t\n3\t## Scope (per coordinator-directives.md)\n4\tOnly the creature face `Emeritus of Truce` is built. The copy-cast-while-prepared\n5\tmechanic and the `Swords to Plowshares` instant face are recorded as `# UNVERIFIED`\n6\tin `card_impl.py` (no copy-cast / second-castable-face engine machinery exists).\n7\t\n8\t## What was implemented\n9\t- `EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature)`: `{1}{W}{W}`, 3/3, Cat Cleric, mono-white\n10\t  (`self.colors = {Color.WHITE}`; the `card_colors` test helper derives `{\"W\"}` from the\n11\t  `{1}{W}{W}` cost).\n12\t- ETB (`on_resolve` -> `_resolve_etb`): the chosen target player creates a 1/1 white & black\n13\t  Inkling with flying. The token is built as a `Creature(subtypes={\"Inkling\"},\n14\t  keywords=Keyword.FLYING, 1/1)` with `token.colors = {Color.WHITE, Color.BLACK}`, then placed\n15\t  via `engine.game.create_token(game, target_player, token)`, which sets `is_token=True` and\n16\t  enters it under the TARGETED player's control (test confirms it can land on an opponent).\n17\t- Conditional prepared state: `is_prepared` bool, default `False`. Set `True` only when an\n18\t  opponent controls STRICTLY more creatures than the controller.\n19\t- Targeting: per the sos_1 KEY_DECISIONS convention, the \"target player\" belongs to the ETB\n20\t  triggered ability, not the creature spell. `get_targets()` returns `[]` (and explicitly `[]`\n21\t  while in a STACK zone). `chosen_targets` carries the ETB target player.\n22\t- Robustness: `on_resolve` with no `chosen_targets` does not raise (token creation is skipped).\n23\t\n24\t## Design decision: ordering of the \"becomes prepared\" check\n25\tThe prepared comparison is evaluated BEFORE the Inkling is created (see `_resolve_etb`). The\n26\ttest contract (`TestEmeritusBecomesPrepared::test_becomes_prepared_when_opponent_has_more_creatures`)\n27\tsets opponent=2 creatures, controller=1 (the card), targets the controller, and expects\n28\t`is_prepared is True`. If the freshly created token were counted toward the controller, the\n29\tcounts would be 2 vs 2 (equal) and the card would NOT become prepared, contradicting the test.\n30\tEvaluating the relative counts before the token enters (so the new token is excluded from the\n31\tcomparison) satisfies that test and the equal/you-have-more cases. This matches the test\n32\tauthor's stated intent (\"the conditional ... evaluated against relative creature counts\" with\n33\tthe token excluded).\n34\t\n35\t## Engine change: Keyword.PREPARED — NOT added (UNVERIFIED)\n36\tThe directive (item 4) asked to add a `PREPARED` member to `engine.types.Keyword` and declare it\n37\ton the creature face. This is IMPOSSIBLE without regressing a read-only engine test:\n38\t`engine_tests/test_types.py::TestKeyword::test_exactly_sixteen_members` asserts\n39\t`len(Keyword) == 16`. The enum already has exactly 16 members (FLYING..PROWESS); adding PREPARED\n40\tmakes it 17 and fails that test. `engine_tests/` is read-only (AGENTS.md hard rule), and the\n41\tdirective's own verification gate requires `pytest engine_tests/` to keep passing.\n42\t\n43\tResolution: the `Keyword.PREPARED` enum member was NOT added (the attempted edit to\n44\t`engine/types.py` was reverted, so there is no net engine diff). The prepared mechanic is\n45\texpressed solely via the runtime `is_prepared` bool, which is what the SOS test contract checks\n46\t(the SOS tests never reference a `Keyword.PREPARED` member). An `# UNVERIFIED:` comment in\n47\t`card_impl.py` records this gap. This keeps BOTH `pytest cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` (18 passed)\n48\tand `pytest engine_tests/` (all passed) green.\n49\t\n50\t## UNVERIFIED items recorded in card_impl.py\n51\t1. `Keyword.PREPARED` first-class enum member — cannot add without regressing the read-only\n52\t   16-member engine test.\n53\t2. \"While prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell; doing so unprepares it\" — no copy-cast\n54\t   machinery.\n55\t3. `Swords to Plowshares` {W} instant face — no second-castable-face representation.\n56\t\n57\t## Verification\n58\t- `pytest cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` -> 18 passed.\n59\t- `pytest engine_tests/` -> all passed (no regression).\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01F9yafmNtMYgjRqYhvsF8zA","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"b3660a36-8f71-474d-83eb-2eef5d083179","timestamp":"2026-06-01T08:52:52.906Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_13"}
