{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011QCQQFQd6ry2kxPyWuz47m","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator directives — sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n2\t\n3\tThis card is a split card whose full mechanics exceed current engine support. The\n4\tcoordinator has scoped the implementation as follows. Implement the **creature\n5\tface** (`Emeritus of Truce`) fully; record the unsupported portions with grep-able\n6\tmarkers.\n7\t\n8\t## Build (in scope)\n9\t1. **Creature face** `Emeritus of Truce` — `{1}{W}{W}`, 3/3, Cat Cleric, white.\n10\t2. **ETB ability**: \"When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white\n11\t   and black Inkling creature token with flying.\" The token enters under the\n12\t   TARGETED player's control. Token: 1/1, white+black, flying, subtype Inkling,\n13\t   `is_token=True`.\n14\t3. **Conditional prepared state**: \"Then if an opponent controls more creatures\n15\t   than you, this creature becomes prepared.\" Expose this as an `is_prepared`\n16\t   boolean on the card (default `False`); set it `True` only when an opponent\n17\t   controls STRICTLY more creatures than the controller, evaluated after the token\n18\t   resolves.\n19\t4. **Prepared keyword (untestable item 1 — BUILD IT)**: Add a new `PREPARED`\n20\t   member to `engine.types.Keyword` (ADDITIVE only — do not rename/remove existing\n21\t   members). Declare `Keyword.PREPARED` in the creature face's keywords so the card\n22\t   advertises it as a first-class keyword. The runtime conditional state stays the\n23\t   `is_prepared` bool.\n24\t5. **Targeting**: per KEY_DECISIONS.md (sos_1 convention), the \"target player\"\n25\t   belongs to the ETB triggered ability, NOT the creature spell. `get_targets()`\n26\t   must return `[]` while the card is in a STACK zone (being cast).\n27\t\n28\t## Record as UNVERIFIED (out of scope — DO NOT attempt full engine support)\n29\tAdd `# UNVERIFIED: <requirement> — <reason>` comments in `cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py`\n30\tso the gaps are grep-able:\n31\t- **Item 2**: \"While prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell; doing so\n32\t  unprepares it.\" — no copy-cast / split-face casting machinery in the engine.\n33\t- **Item 3**: the `Swords to Plowshares` {W} instant face (exile target creature;\n34\t  its controller gains life equal to its power) — engine has no second castable\n35\t  face representation.\n36\t\n37\tYou MAY still store the spell-face metadata (name half, etc.) if convenient, but\n38\tdo not build the copy-cast or instant-face resolution.\n39\t\n40\t## Constraints\n41\t- Make ALL tests in `cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` pass. Do NOT modify tests.\n42\t- Engine changes additive only; do not touch engine_tests/ or FDN tests.\n43\t- After your changes, run `pytest engine_tests/` to confirm the new Keyword member\n44\t  didn't regress anything.\n45\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01F9yafmNtMYgjRqYhvsF8zA","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"97c2dd54-d833-4dd1-b53d-f318af7f14aa","timestamp":"2026-06-01T08:52:53.304Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_13"}
