{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VDYNqLA4cboav5NP7PDFPP","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"d6c51d82-7ed4-401a-9a22-a2b3d58ee8e0","timestamp":"2026-06-01T08:58:28.464Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"## Untestable resolution: sos_13","newString":"## Untestable resolution: sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)\n- Counter half (core) is fully testable/implemented.\n- The Wizard-gated delayed \"{C} at the beginning of your next main phase = mana\n  spent on the countered spell\" needs two ADDITIVE engine capabilities:\n  (1) a beginning-of-main-phase triggered event in engine/events.py fired from the\n  turn loop, and (2) recording total mana spent to cast a spell on the card/StackObject.\n- **Decision**: option (a) attempt to BUILD it additively. Implementer instructed to\n  add both capabilities additively; if any part would regress engine_tests/ or require\n  non-additive engine changes, fall back to (b) `# UNVERIFIED` markers for that part\n  and report. Tester re-invoked once IFF the engine support lands, to add {C}-bonus tests.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_13","originalFile":"# Run Decisions\n\nDecisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n- **Item 1 — \"Prepared\" keyword as a first-class flag**: INITIALLY directed as (a)\n  build it, but DOWNGRADED to (b) accept partial coverage. Adding `PREPARED` to\n  `engine.types.Keyword` regresses the authoritative read-only engine test\n  `engine_tests/test_types.py::TestKeyword::test_exactly_sixteen_members`\n  (asserts `len(Keyword) == 16`). Since engine_tests/ is authoritative for grading\n  and must not be modified, the keyword cannot be added without zeroing that test.\n  Implementer correctly declined and marked it `# UNVERIFIED`. The prepared state is\n  fully expressed via the `is_prepared` bool (tested). No Tester re-invocation.\n- **Item 2 — \"cast a copy of its spell while prepared, unpreparing it\"**: resolved\n  via (b) accept partial coverage. Requires major copy-cast/split-card engine\n  machinery; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:` marker added in card_impl.py.\n- **Item 3 — the \"Swords to Plowshares\" {W} instant face**: resolved via (b). The\n  engine has no second-castable-face representation; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:`\n  marker added in card_impl.py.\n- The conditional prepared STATE is exposed as an `is_prepared` bool (tested).\n\n## Test dispute: sos_4\n- **Disputed test**: `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player` (tests.py L180-198)\n- **Tester's intent**: verify \"you gain X life\" goes to the controller, not the target player, while the chosen any-target takes damage.\n- **Implementer's objection (feasibility)**: the test uses `chosen_targets=[p2, p1]`, naming p1 (controller) as the damage any-target (index 1), but asserts p2 (index 0) is damaged. This contradicts `test_two_colors_deals_two_damage_to_player` ([p1,p2] -> p2 damaged at index 1). No single index mapping satisfies both.\n- **Decision**: accept implementer (feasibility objection — test data is internally contradictory). Convention is draw=chosen_targets[0], damage any-target=chosen_targets[1], life gain=controller.\n- **Action**: re-invoke Tester to rewrite ONLY the disputed test, changing its data to `[p2, p2]` (draw target p2, damage any-target p2) so the intended \"life goes to controller p1\" check holds under the suite's index-1=damage convention.\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":6,"newStart":2,"newLines":17,"lines":[" "," Decisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`."," ","+## Untestable resolution: sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)","+- Counter half (core) is fully testable/implemented.","+- The Wizard-gated delayed \"{C} at the beginning of your next main phase = mana","+  spent on the countered spell\" needs two ADDITIVE engine capabilities:","+  (1) a beginning-of-main-phase triggered event in engine/events.py fired from the","+  turn loop, and (2) recording total mana spent to cast a spell on the card/StackObject.","+- **Decision**: option (a) attempt to BUILD it additively. Implementer instructed to","+  add both capabilities additively; if any part would regress engine_tests/ or require","+  non-additive engine changes, fall back to (b) `# UNVERIFIED` markers for that part","+  and report. Tester re-invoked once IFF the engine support lands, to add {C}-bonus tests.","+"," ## Untestable resolution: sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)"," - **Item 1 — \"Prepared\" keyword as a first-class flag**: INITIALLY directed as (a)","   build it, but DOWNGRADED to (b) accept partial coverage. Adding `PREPARED` to"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014jC2pPANWZKSmv137A9U3t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RKzTGjsnT54fXAeqw4nP6w","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator directives — sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)\n\n## Build (in scope, fully tested)\nThe counterspell half: target a spell on the stack, counter it (remove its\nStackObject from the stack, move the card to its OWNER's graveyard without running\nits on_resolve). `get_targets()` advertises a single `TargetRequirement` with\n`zone == Zone.STACK` filtering for spells. Make all current tests pass.\n\n## Attempt to BUILD the delayed Wizard bonus (additive engine work)\nOracle bonus: \"If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of\nmana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\"\n\nThis needs two ADDITIVE engine capabilities. Attempt both:\n1. **Beginning-of-main-phase trigger event** — add a new event class to\n   `engine/events.py` (e.g. `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`, following the\n   existing pattern of upkeep/begin-combat/end-step events) and FIRE it from the\n   turn/phase progression (engine turn loop / `engine/game_state.py`) at the start\n   of each main phase. Register a delayed trigger from the card's resolution.\n2. **Mana-spent tracking** — record the total quantity of mana paid to cast a spell\n   (e.g. set a `mana_spent` int attribute on the card / StackObject during payment\n   in `engine/casting.py`), so the {C} amount can equal the mana spent on the\n   countered spell.\n\nThen implement: on resolution, if the controller controls a Wizard, register a\ndelayed one-shot trigger for the controller's next main phase that adds `{C}` equal\nto the countered spell's recorded `mana_spent` to the controller's mana pool.\n\n### HARD CONSTRAINT — additive only\n- All engine changes must be ADDITIVE: new event classes, new attributes, new\n  branches. Do NOT rename/move/delete existing engine symbols.\n- After ANY engine change you MUST run `pytest engine_tests/` and it must stay green.\n- If a part of this bonus CANNOT be built without regressing `engine_tests/` or\n  without non-additive changes, DO NOT force it: mark that specific part with a\n  grep-able `# UNVERIFIED: <requirement> — <reason>` in `cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py`\n  and clearly report in your rationale which parts you built vs. left UNVERIFIED.\n\nPrefer correctness and a green engine_tests/ suite over completeness. The counter\nhalf must always work.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2101,"cache_read_input_tokens":65246,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2101},"output_tokens":46,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"cc0c4250-d841-4386-867f-a1a85da175c3","request_id":"req_011CbcGG2Z4DjQx4u39GW1v4"}
