{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01124hY7CBe7D1YPxuaXBjm3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\tPersistent, append-only conventions and decisions across runs.\n4\t\n5\t## Card-level `get_targets()` vs. triggered-ability targets (from sos_1)\n6\tThe casting pipeline (`engine/casting.py`) calls `card.get_targets(game)` for the\n7\tSPELL ITSELF and forces the controller to choose those targets when the spell is\n8\tcast. So `get_targets()` must only advertise targets the *spell* takes. If a card's\n9\ttargeting belongs to a triggered ability (e.g. \"whenever this attacks, target ...\"),\n10\tdo NOT expose it via the card-level `get_targets()` — otherwise casting the permanent\n11\twrongly requires/consumes a target (and can raise `CastingError` when none is legal).\n12\tThe pipeline moves the card into the controller's `STACK` zone before querying\n13\t`get_targets()`, so a card can detect \"am I being cast right now?\" by checking\n14\twhether `self` is in any player's `STACK` zone and return `[]` in that case. Have the\n15\ttriggered ability choose its own target (via `player.choose_target`) at resolution.\n16\t\n17\t## Converge / multi-target / life-gain conventions (from sos_4)\n18\t- **Converge X** = `len(self.colors_spent)`. The casting pipeline records the\n19\t  distinct colors of mana spent as a LIST of `engine.types.Color` on\n20\t  `card.colors_spent` (not an int). Initialize `colors_spent` to `[]` in\n21\t  `__init__`; compute X with `len(...)`. (Note: fdn_205 used an int because it\n22\t  bypassed the cast pipeline — prefer the list shape for real cards.)\n23\t- **Multi-target ordering**: `chosen_targets` is ordered to match the oracle text\n24\t  order of the `TargetRequirement`s returned by `get_targets()`. E.g. \"Target\n25\t  player ... deals X damage to any target\" → `chosen_targets[0]` = target player,\n26\t  `chosen_targets[1]` = any-target.\n27\t- **Life gain**: there is no `gain_life` engine helper. Gain life directly via\n28\t  `controller.life += x`. Damage uses `engine.game.deal_damage`, draw uses\n29\t  `engine.game.draw_card`.\n30\t- Resolution should short-circuit on X <= 0 and defend against missing\n31\t  `chosen_targets`/`colors_spent` so it never raises.\n32\t\n33\t## Do NOT add members to `engine.types.Keyword` (from sos_13)\n34\tThe authoritative engine regression test\n35\t`engine_tests/test_types.py::TestKeyword::test_exactly_sixteen_members` asserts\n36\t`len(Keyword) == 16`. `engine_tests/` is read-only and authoritative for grading,\n37\tso adding ANY new `Keyword` enum member zeros that test. For cards introducing a\n38\tnew \"keyword\" that isn't already in the enum (e.g. \"Prepared\"), DO NOT add an enum\n39\tmember. Instead model the mechanic's runtime state with a plain attribute/bool on\n40\tthe card (e.g. `is_prepared`) and mark unimplementable sub-clauses with grep-able\n41\t`# UNVERIFIED: <requirement> — <reason>` comments. Same caution likely applies to\n42\tother \"exactly N members\" enum-count tests — check `engine_tests/test_types.py`\n43\tbefore extending any engine enum.\n44\t\n45\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018Kvfn4HqTQECn3S9uSoUJy","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"d246703f-2e8c-4198-8f03-3ef7d95e93ee","timestamp":"2026-06-01T08:59:06.226Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_57"}
