{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ECwbKfUGWq7TKDt31vRbhj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test rationale — sos_57 Mana Sculpt\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Mana Sculpt** — `{1}{U}{U}` Instant.\n4\tOracle: \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C}\n5\tequal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your\n6\tnext main phase.\"\n7\t\n8\tTest file: `cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py`\n9\t\n10\t## What each test covers\n11\t\n12\t### TestManaSculptProperties (static data)\n13\t- `test_is_instant` / `test_card_type_includes_instant` — the card is an\n14\t  `Instant` (so it can be cast at instant speed and goes to the graveyard on\n15\t  resolve).\n16\t- `test_name` — name matches the spec exactly.\n17\t- `test_mana_cost` — cost parses to `{1}{U}{U}`.\n18\t- `test_is_blue` — the cost has two blue pips and one generic (validates the\n19\t  card's blue identity from the spec `colors: [\"U\"]`).\n20\t\n21\t### TestManaSculptTargeting (\"Counter target spell\")\n22\t- `test_returns_single_target_requirement` — `get_targets()` advertises exactly\n23\t  one `TargetRequirement` (a single target spell).\n24\t- `test_target_zone_is_stack` — the target requirement's zone is `Zone.STACK`,\n25\t  because a \"spell\" is an object on the stack (rule 112.1).\n26\t- `test_filter_accepts_sorcery_spell` / `test_filter_accepts_instant_spell` —\n27\t  the filter accepts spell objects.\n28\t- `test_filter_rejects_non_spell` — a non-spell object (no spell card types) is\n29\t  not a legal target.\n30\t\n31\t### TestManaSculptCounter (counter behavior)\n32\t- `test_countered_spell_leaves_the_stack` — after Mana Sculpt resolves against a\n33\t  chosen target spell, that spell's `StackObject` is gone from the stack and the\n34\t  card is no longer in its controller's STACK zone.\n35\t- `test_countered_spell_goes_to_owner_graveyard` — a countered spell is put into\n36\t  its owner's graveyard (rule 701.5g / 608.2m).\n37\t- `test_countered_spell_does_not_resolve_its_effect` — the countered spell's\n38\t  `on_resolve` must not run (a marker subclass records whether it ran). Guards\n39\t  against an implementation that lets the spell resolve.\n40\t- `test_no_target_is_a_noop` — resolving with no chosen target neither raises\n41\t  nor moves the (unrelated) spell off the stack.\n42\t- `test_none_target_is_a_noop` — an explicit `[None]` target list is a no-op,\n43\t  not a crash (defends against the \"target became illegal\" case).\n44\t\n45\t### TestManaSculptWizardGateDoesNotAffectCounter\n46\t- `test_counters_even_without_a_wizard` — controlling a non-Wizard creature does\n47\t  not suppress the counter; the spell is still countered.\n48\t- `test_counters_when_controlling_a_wizard` — controlling a Wizard does not break\n49\t  the counter; the spell is still countered.\n50\t- These pin down that the conditional \"If you control a Wizard …\" clause governs\n51\t  only the bonus `{C}` mana, never the counter itself.\n52\t\n53\t## Edge cases deliberately covered\n54\t- No-target / `[None]`-target resolution (illegal/missing target) must be a safe\n55\t  no-op.\n56\t- Counter must move the spell to the **owner's** graveyard, not the caster's.\n57\t- Counter must work irrespective of the Wizard condition.\n58\t\n59\t## Edge cases NOT covered here (see untestable.json)\n60\tThe delayed bonus — \"If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the\n61\tamount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main\n62\tphase\" — cannot be asserted with the current engine surface:\n63\t\n64\t1. **No beginning-of-main-phase trigger event.** `engine/events.py` defines\n65\t   upkeep/combat/end-step/end-of-turn triggered events but no main-phase event,\n66\t   so a \"at the beginning of your next main phase\" delayed trigger has no event\n67\t   to fire on and no observable hook to assert against.\n68\t2. **The amount of mana spent to cast the countered spell is not recorded.**\n69\t   The casting pipeline stores only `colors_spent` on a card; it never records\n70\t   the total quantity of mana paid, and the `StackObject` carries no such field.\n71\t   So \"amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent\" has no ground-truth\n72\t   value the test could compare against.\n73\t\n74\tPer `KEY_DECISIONS.md`, no new `Keyword` enum member is needed for this card, so\n75\tthat locked-count constraint is not implicated.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015rJSnz1LezCJNzSZuKfbai","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"5966f829-9d24-4b07-b8b4-a8035194d2be","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:02:09.071Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend sos_57 tests for C bonus"}
