{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T5NRzBj42jfSGh6s2rZ5YR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# sos_57 Mana Sculpt — implementation rationale\n2\t\n3\t## Counter half (fully tested, all 17 tests pass)\n4\t`ManaSculpt(Instant)` with name/cost/types from the spec.\n5\t\n6\t- `get_targets()` returns a single `TargetRequirement(zone=Zone.STACK,\n7\t  filter_fn=_is_spell)`. The filter accepts an object whose `card_types`\n8\t  intersect a spell-type set (instant/sorcery/creature/artifact/enchantment/\n9\t  planeswalker) and rejects objects with no such types. It accepts either a\n10\t  bare card or a `StackObject` (unwraps `.source`), because the tests pass bare\n11\t  card objects (`_vanilla_sorcery()`) to `filter_fn` while the real cast\n12\t  pipeline would pass stack objects.\n13\t- `on_resolve()` reads `chosen_targets[0]`. The tests set `chosen_targets` to\n14\t  the **card** itself (not its StackObject), so `_find_stack_object()` locates\n15\t  the matching `StackObject` on the stack by identity, then `_counter_spell()`\n16\t  removes that StackObject from `game.stack._items`, removes the card from its\n17\t  controller's STACK zone, and adds it to its owner's graveyard — without ever\n18\t  invoking the countered spell's `on_resolve`. No / `[None]` / missing target is\n19\t  a safe no-op (matches the FDN `_counter_spell` pattern, fdn_153/fdn_160).\n20\t\n21\t## Wizard {C} bonus — BUILT (not UNVERIFIED)\n22\tThe directives' two additive engine capabilities were both added without\n23\tregressing `engine_tests/` (1145 passed):\n24\t\n25\t1. **Beginning-of-main-phase trigger event** — added\n26\t   `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, phase)` to `engine/events.py`,\n27\t   following the existing upkeep/begin-combat event pattern. It is fired from\n28\t   `GameState.advance_phase` via a new additive helper\n29\t   `GameState._fire_beginning_of_main_phase()` whenever the new phase is\n30\t   `PRECOMBAT_MAIN` or `POSTCOMBAT_MAIN`. This is purely additive: a new event\n31\t   class, a new method, and one added call line inside the existing\n32\t   `advance_phase` body.\n33\t\n34\t2. **Mana-spent tracking** — `engine/casting.cast_spell` now records\n35\t   `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` right after payment (alongside the\n36\t   existing `colors_spent`). This is the total mana value paid for the cast\n37\t   (X included via the effective cost), additive only.\n38\t\n39\tOn resolution, if the controller controls a creature with the `Wizard` subtype\n40\tand the countered spell recorded `mana_spent > 0`, `ManaSculpt` registers a\n41\tone-shot delayed `TriggerRegistration` watching\n42\t`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` for that controller; when it fires it adds\n43\tthat many `{C}` to the controller's mana pool and unregisters itself.\n44\t\n45\t## Engine capabilities added (summary)\n46\t- Event class: `engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`.\n47\t- Firing hook: `GameState._fire_beginning_of_main_phase()` called from\n48\t  `advance_phase`.\n49\t- `card.mana_spent` int recorded in `engine.casting.cast_spell`.\n50\t\n51\t## UNVERIFIED parts\n52\tNone. Both engine capabilities were added additively and the delayed bonus is\n53\twired up. The bonus itself has no dedicated SOS test (those clauses live in\n54\t`untestable.json`), so its runtime correctness is exercised only indirectly;\n55\tthe counter half is fully covered and green, and `engine_tests/` stays green.\n56\t\n57\t## Conventions established for future cards\n58\t- `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` now exists for \"at the beginning of your\n59\t  next main phase\" delayed triggers; condition should match on `event.player`.\n60\t- Total mana paid for a cast is available as `card.mana_spent` (mana value of\n61\t  the effective, cost-reduced cost).\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Um2fPsqJ5WALztNU1xs4f6","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"1533f8b2-c253-4e28-b4d7-7224b190222e","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:06:12.581Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_57"}
