{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_013B4a2zH89NXABw6cBuy1nh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014eTtfTAwaSb9L8t629bvHw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/review.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 48,\n    \"comment\": \"The `_is_spell` target filter does not exclude the casting card itself (`self`). The established counterspell convention in cards/fdn/fdn_160/card_impl.py explicitly does `if obj is self: return False` in its target filter, and the `get_targets` docstring here claims it avoids advertising a self-target requirement, but the filter does not actually enforce that. Whether this is reachable depends on how the player implementation enumerates STACK-zone candidates (Mana Sculpt's own card is moved to the STACK zone before target selection in casting.py step 4). Consider adding an explicit `if source is self: return False` guard to match the FDN convention and avoid Mana Sculpt being able to target/counter itself.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 197,\n    \"comment\": \"`_register_mana_bonus`'s one-shot cleanup calls `g.trigger_manager.unregister(self)`, which removes ALL triggers whose `source is self`. The local `fired` flag already makes a single registration one-shot, so the unregister is belt-and-suspenders here. However if the same Mana Sculpt card instance ever has two pending delayed bonuses queued simultaneously (e.g. recast from graveyard before the first resolves), the first resolution's `unregister(self)` would also drop the second registration. Edge case and unlikely in current usage, but unregistering by the specific TriggerRegistration rather than by `self` would be safer.\"\n  }\n]\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null