{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01MfLtrwMFkyjSsnZpDRS6qM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CenAMXtEQDMXh91ZYQnpnC","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — sos_97 Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\n\nCard: `{1}{B}{B}` Legendary Planeswalker — Ral, starting loyalty 3, with four\nloyalty abilities:\n\n- `+1: Surveil 2.`\n- `−1: Any number of target players each discard a card.`\n- `−2: Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.`\n- `−7: Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X is the number of coins that came up heads.`\n\n## File: `cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`\n\nConventions discovered and followed:\n- Planeswalker shape from fdn_134 (Ajani): abilities exposed via\n  `get_loyalty_abilities()` returning `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect)`\n  dataclasses; the effect reads its target from the planeswalker's\n  `chosen_targets` / `_resolve_target` attribute.\n- Surveil from fdn_53: top of library is the END of the zone list; the\n  controller uses `choose_yes_no` to decide whether each examined card goes to\n  the graveyard. The `DeterministicPlayer` script feeds those yes/no answers.\n- Mana value via `card.mana_cost.cmc`.\n\n### TestRalProperties\nStatic data contract: planeswalker type, exact name, `{1}{B}{B}` cost,\nLegendary supertype, `\"Ral\"` subtype, and starting/current loyalty of 3.\n\n### TestRalLoyaltyAbilityDeclaration\n- `test_returns_four_abilities` — all four printed abilities are exposed.\n- `test_each_is_loyalty_ability` — each is a `LoyaltyAbility` instance.\n- `test_loyalty_costs_match_spec` — the loyalty costs are exactly\n  `{+1, -1, -2, -7}`. This is the structural contract the rest of the\n  behavioural tests select abilities by.\n\n### TestRalSurveil (+1: Surveil 2)\n- `test_surveil_puts_both_chosen_cards_into_graveyard` — when the controller\n  opts to bin both examined cards, both top cards move to the graveyard.\n- `test_surveil_keeps_cards_on_top_when_declined` — declining leaves the\n  library size unchanged and the graveyard empty (cards stay on top).\n- `test_surveil_with_fewer_than_two_cards_does_not_raise` — edge case: only one\n  card in library; Surveil 2 must examine what's available without crashing.\n- `test_surveil_empty_library_does_not_raise` — edge case: empty library is a\n  safe no-op.\n\nI deliberately do NOT assert the relative ordering of cards kept on top (the\n\"put the rest back in any order\" clause) — ordering among retained cards is a\nfree player choice and not a defined contract.\n\n### TestRalDiscard (−1: target players each discard)\n- `test_targeted_player_discards_a_card` — the targeted opponent loses the\n  chosen card from hand to graveyard.\n- `test_no_targets_is_a_noop` — \"any number of target players\" includes zero;\n  with no targets nobody discards and nothing raises.\n- `test_targeted_player_with_empty_hand_does_not_raise` — a targeted player\n  with an empty hand simply discards nothing.\n\n### TestRalReanimate (−2: return mv≤3 creature from your graveyard)\n- `test_returns_low_mv_creature_to_battlefield` — mv-2 creature returns to the\n  battlefield and leaves the graveyard.\n- `test_mv_exactly_three_is_legal` — boundary: mana value exactly 3 is allowed.\n- `test_target_filter_rejects_high_mv_creature` — boundary: mv-4 creature is not\n  reanimated (stays in graveyard).\n- `test_target_filter_rejects_noncreature` — a noncreature card (instant) is not\n  a legal target even at low mana value.\n- `test_only_your_graveyard` — a low-mv creature in the opponent's graveyard is\n  not reanimated onto your battlefield.\n- `test_no_target_chosen_is_a_noop` — defensive: no chosen target leaves the\n  graveyard untouched.\n\n### TestRalUltimate (−7: coin flips + skip turns)\n- `test_ultimate_loyalty_cost_is_minus_seven` — structural: the ultimate is\n  declared at −7.\n- `test_ultimate_resolution_does_not_raise` — resolving the ultimate must not\n  crash regardless of coin outcomes.\n\nThe randomness of the five coin flips and the \"target opponent skips their next\nX turns\" effect are not backed by a deterministic engine API (no coin-flip\nhelper; `GameState.extra_turns` is an *insert* queue with a documented\nENGINE LIMITATION that `'skip your next turn'` is \"not fully handled\"). The\nexact number of skipped turns therefore can't be asserted deterministically.\nSee `untestable.json`. We still pin the loyalty cost and the no-raise contract.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1342,"cache_read_input_tokens":83438,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1342,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013p4dsUvinFeK7Udavv6oTb","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"24895b04-e2f9-4310-a7b6-5e58bc6a0707","request_id":"req_011CbcHgVZnzQb8kjpN12oQV","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_97"}
