{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kr6mGHKxEtVS7fFefsKB1H","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"1e9b737d-d4f7-41d9-8889-b05b0f762ca1","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:18:05.129Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"## Untestable resolution: sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)","newString":"## Untestable resolution: sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer — planeswalker)\n- Three of four abilities (Surveil 2, targeted discard, mv<=3 reanimation) fully\n  testable/implemented.\n- The -7 ultimate needs two ADDITIVE engine capabilities: (1) a deterministic\n  coin-flip helper (scriptable via DeterministicPlayer) so X = heads is assertable,\n  and (2) a per-player skipped-turns mechanism consulted by turn rotation.\n- **Decision**: option (a) attempt to BUILD both additively (mirroring sos_57). If a\n  part would regress engine_tests/ (esp. the turn loop) or need non-additive changes,\n  fall back to (b) `# UNVERIFIED` for that part. Tester re-invoked once for whatever lands.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)","originalFile":"# Run Decisions\n\nDecisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)\n- Counter half (core) is fully testable/implemented.\n- The Wizard-gated delayed \"{C} at the beginning of your next main phase = mana\n  spent on the countered spell\" needs two ADDITIVE engine capabilities:\n  (1) a beginning-of-main-phase triggered event in engine/events.py fired from the\n  turn loop, and (2) recording total mana spent to cast a spell on the card/StackObject.\n- **Decision**: option (a) attempt to BUILD it additively. Implementer instructed to\n  add both capabilities additively; if any part would regress engine_tests/ or require\n  non-additive engine changes, fall back to (b) `# UNVERIFIED` markers for that part\n  and report. Tester re-invoked once IFF the engine support lands, to add {C}-bonus tests.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n- **Item 1 — \"Prepared\" keyword as a first-class flag**: INITIALLY directed as (a)\n  build it, but DOWNGRADED to (b) accept partial coverage. Adding `PREPARED` to\n  `engine.types.Keyword` regresses the authoritative read-only engine test\n  `engine_tests/test_types.py::TestKeyword::test_exactly_sixteen_members`\n  (asserts `len(Keyword) == 16`). Since engine_tests/ is authoritative for grading\n  and must not be modified, the keyword cannot be added without zeroing that test.\n  Implementer correctly declined and marked it `# UNVERIFIED`. The prepared state is\n  fully expressed via the `is_prepared` bool (tested). No Tester re-invocation.\n- **Item 2 — \"cast a copy of its spell while prepared, unpreparing it\"**: resolved\n  via (b) accept partial coverage. Requires major copy-cast/split-card engine\n  machinery; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:` marker added in card_impl.py.\n- **Item 3 — the \"Swords to Plowshares\" {W} instant face**: resolved via (b). The\n  engine has no second-castable-face representation; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:`\n  marker added in card_impl.py.\n- The conditional prepared STATE is exposed as an `is_prepared` bool (tested).\n\n## Test dispute: sos_4\n- **Disputed test**: `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player` (tests.py L180-198)\n- **Tester's intent**: verify \"you gain X life\" goes to the controller, not the target player, while the chosen any-target takes damage.\n- **Implementer's objection (feasibility)**: the test uses `chosen_targets=[p2, p1]`, naming p1 (controller) as the damage any-target (index 1), but asserts p2 (index 0) is damaged. This contradicts `test_two_colors_deals_two_damage_to_player` ([p1,p2] -> p2 damaged at index 1). No single index mapping satisfies both.\n- **Decision**: accept implementer (feasibility objection — test data is internally contradictory). Convention is draw=chosen_targets[0], damage any-target=chosen_targets[1], life gain=controller.\n- **Action**: re-invoke Tester to rewrite ONLY the disputed test, changing its data to `[p2, p2]` (draw target p2, damage any-target p2) so the intended \"life goes to controller p1\" check holds under the suite's index-1=damage convention.\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":6,"newStart":2,"newLines":16,"lines":[" "," Decisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`."," ","+## Untestable resolution: sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer — planeswalker)","+- Three of four abilities (Surveil 2, targeted discard, mv<=3 reanimation) fully","+  testable/implemented.","+- The -7 ultimate needs two ADDITIVE engine capabilities: (1) a deterministic","+  coin-flip helper (scriptable via DeterministicPlayer) so X = heads is assertable,","+  and (2) a per-player skipped-turns mechanism consulted by turn rotation.","+- **Decision**: option (a) attempt to BUILD both additively (mirroring sos_57). If a","+  part would regress engine_tests/ (esp. the turn loop) or need non-additive changes,","+  fall back to (b) `# UNVERIFIED` for that part. Tester re-invoked once for whatever lands.","+"," ## Untestable resolution: sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)"," - Counter half (core) is fully testable/implemented."," - The Wizard-gated delayed \"{C} at the beginning of your next main phase = mana"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01LFVcoFgpFDDVomJSGYHpTH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ScKkS3XgxuwhreTHCifvzq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator directives — sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer, planeswalker)\n\n## Build (in scope, fully tested)\nThe planeswalker with its 4 loyalty abilities, the three fully-testable ones built\nproperly:\n- Surveil 2 ability.\n- Targeted discard ability.\n- Reanimation of a mana-value <= 3 (per spec) ability.\n- The -7 ultimate's loyalty cost and ability declaration/structure.\nMake all current tests pass. Follow KEY_DECISIONS.md conventions (no Keyword enum\nadditions; get_targets()==[] while on stack for triggered/ability targets; etc.).\n\n## Attempt to BUILD the -7 ultimate's hard parts (additive engine work)\nOracle ultimate (paraphrase from spec — read card_spec.json for exact text):\n\"Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X = number of\ncoins that came up heads\" (or similar). Build both capabilities ADDITIVELY:\n\n1. **Deterministic coin-flip primitive** — add a helper (e.g. `game.flip_coin(player)`\n   or on GameState) whose result is SCRIPTABLE through the existing\n   DeterministicPlayer mechanism (look at how the engine scripts player choices, e.g.\n   in `engine/player.py` / test_utils), so a test can force a known head count and\n   assert X. Reuse the existing deterministic-choice plumbing rather than real RNG.\n2. **Turn-skipping** — add a per-player skipped-turns counter (e.g.\n   `player.skipped_turns` defaulting to 0) that the turn rotation / `advance_phase`\n   (or the turn-start logic in `engine/game_state.py` / turn loop) consults so a\n   player with skipped_turns > 0 loses that many upcoming turns (decrementing as\n   skipped). A test must be able to read the counter and/or observe the skipped turns.\n   NOTE: the engine source documents that \"skip your next turn\" is not fully handled —\n   so this is the riskiest part.\n\nThen implement the ultimate: flip five coins, X = heads, set the target opponent's\nskipped_turns += X (or push X skips).\n\n### HARD CONSTRAINT — additive only + green engine_tests/\n- All engine changes ADDITIVE: new methods/attributes/branches only. Do NOT\n  rename/move/delete existing engine symbols. Do NOT add Keyword enum members.\n- After ANY engine change, run `pytest engine_tests/` — it MUST stay green. The turn\n  loop is heavily tested; default behavior (skipped_turns == 0) must be a no-op so\n  existing turn tests are unaffected.\n- If a part CANNOT be built additively without regressing engine_tests/, DO NOT force\n  it: mark that specific part `# UNVERIFIED: <requirement> — <reason>` in\n  `cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py` and report which parts you built vs left UNVERIFIED.\n\nPrefer a green engine_tests/ suite and correct behavior of the three simple\nabilities over completeness of the ultimate.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1617,"cache_read_input_tokens":78021,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1617},"output_tokens":50,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"643862e3-e5ff-4813-9ee8-74614f37dd51","request_id":"req_011CbcHkmB1XB9iiAFWnpBeZ"}
