{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N9rKCkACebqB6fMybvsniB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator directives — sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer, planeswalker)\n2\t\n3\t## Build (in scope, fully tested)\n4\tThe planeswalker with its 4 loyalty abilities, the three fully-testable ones built\n5\tproperly:\n6\t- Surveil 2 ability.\n7\t- Targeted discard ability.\n8\t- Reanimation of a mana-value <= 3 (per spec) ability.\n9\t- The -7 ultimate's loyalty cost and ability declaration/structure.\n10\tMake all current tests pass. Follow KEY_DECISIONS.md conventions (no Keyword enum\n11\tadditions; get_targets()==[] while on stack for triggered/ability targets; etc.).\n12\t\n13\t## Attempt to BUILD the -7 ultimate's hard parts (additive engine work)\n14\tOracle ultimate (paraphrase from spec — read card_spec.json for exact text):\n15\t\"Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X = number of\n16\tcoins that came up heads\" (or similar). Build both capabilities ADDITIVELY:\n17\t\n18\t1. **Deterministic coin-flip primitive** — add a helper (e.g. `game.flip_coin(player)`\n19\t   or on GameState) whose result is SCRIPTABLE through the existing\n20\t   DeterministicPlayer mechanism (look at how the engine scripts player choices, e.g.\n21\t   in `engine/player.py` / test_utils), so a test can force a known head count and\n22\t   assert X. Reuse the existing deterministic-choice plumbing rather than real RNG.\n23\t2. **Turn-skipping** — add a per-player skipped-turns counter (e.g.\n24\t   `player.skipped_turns` defaulting to 0) that the turn rotation / `advance_phase`\n25\t   (or the turn-start logic in `engine/game_state.py` / turn loop) consults so a\n26\t   player with skipped_turns > 0 loses that many upcoming turns (decrementing as\n27\t   skipped). A test must be able to read the counter and/or observe the skipped turns.\n28\t   NOTE: the engine source documents that \"skip your next turn\" is not fully handled —\n29\t   so this is the riskiest part.\n30\t\n31\tThen implement the ultimate: flip five coins, X = heads, set the target opponent's\n32\tskipped_turns += X (or push X skips).\n33\t\n34\t### HARD CONSTRAINT — additive only + green engine_tests/\n35\t- All engine changes ADDITIVE: new methods/attributes/branches only. Do NOT\n36\t  rename/move/delete existing engine symbols. Do NOT add Keyword enum members.\n37\t- After ANY engine change, run `pytest engine_tests/` — it MUST stay green. The turn\n38\t  loop is heavily tested; default behavior (skipped_turns == 0) must be a no-op so\n39\t  existing turn tests are unaffected.\n40\t- If a part CANNOT be built additively without regressing engine_tests/, DO NOT force\n41\t  it: mark that specific part `# UNVERIFIED: <requirement> — <reason>` in\n42\t  `cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py` and report which parts you built vs left UNVERIFIED.\n43\t\n44\tPrefer a green engine_tests/ suite and correct behavior of the three simple\n45\tabilities over completeness of the ultimate.\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EVQk5wqb73SzprdJXKMZAu","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"5d2194b7-2ae4-4b4d-98ee-6979f0733ba2","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:18:36.891Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_97"}
