{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01GYseq1QSm9nLUW5Ugpnbfi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UYoY1B2fVm3UffLub1DpKC","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-rationale.md","content":"# sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer — implementation rationale\n\n## Card\n`RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker)` at `cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py`.\n- {1}{B}{B}, Legendary Planeswalker — Ral, starting loyalty 3.\n- Follows fdn_134 (Ajani) planeswalker pattern: `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns\n  `LoyaltyAbility` dataclasses; the ability's target is read from\n  `self.chosen_targets` / `self._resolve_target` (set by the resolution pipeline\n  or tests). `get_targets()` returns `[]` per KEY_DECISIONS so casting the\n  planeswalker never requires a card-level target.\n\n## Loyalty abilities (all four declared; three fully built)\n- **+1 Surveil 2**: top of library is the END of the internal list (fdn_53\n  convention). Examines up to two cards top-first; `controller.choose_yes_no`\n  decides whether each goes to the graveyard. Stops on the first \"keep\" so kept\n  cards stay on top (Surveil \"rest back on top\"). Safe on 0/1-card libraries.\n- **−1 each target player discards**: iterates `chosen_targets`; each target picks\n  a card via `choose_card` and is discarded via `engine.game.discard`. Empty hand\n  and zero targets are no-ops.\n- **−2 reanimate**: target must be a CREATURE card, mana value (`mana_cost.cmc`)\n  ≤ 3, and in the *controller's* graveyard. Filters reject mv≥4, noncreatures,\n  and opponent-graveyard cards; missing target is a no-op. Uses\n  `move_to_zone(GRAVEYARD → BATTLEFIELD)` after setting controller.\n- **−7 ultimate**: flips five coins, X = heads, then `target.skipped_turns += X`.\n\n## Engine capabilities added (ADDITIVE — both BUILT, not UNVERIFIED)\n1. **Coin-flip primitive** — `GameState.flip_coin(player)` returns True for heads.\n   When `player` is a scripted `DeterministicPlayer` with queued answers it reads\n   the result via `choose_yes_no` (so a test can force a known head count); else\n   falls back to `random.choice`. Purely additive new method.\n2. **Turn-skipping** — `Player.skipped_turns` (default 0) plus\n   `GameState._apply_skipped_turns()`, invoked from `advance_phase` right after\n   the active player rotates at end of turn. If the newly-active player has\n   `skipped_turns > 0`, it decrements one and advances the normal rotation to the\n   other player, looping for consecutive skips (bounded for termination).\n   Default `skipped_turns == 0` makes the hook a strict no-op, so existing turn\n   rotation is unchanged.\n\nThe real turn loop (`engine/turn.py::run_turn`) rotates via `advance_phase`, so\nthe skip hook is on the live path — the ultimate's turn-skip is genuinely BUILT,\nnot stubbed.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` → 24 passed.\n- `pytest engine_tests/` → 1145 passed (no regressions; default no-op preserved).\n- Full `pytest` → 1297 passed.\n\n## Notes for future cards\n- Reusable engine infra: `GameState.flip_coin(player)` (scriptable) and\n  `Player.skipped_turns` + `advance_phase` skip handling.\n- No Keyword enum members added; no `gain_life` helper used.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":208,"cache_read_input_tokens":58648,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":208,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":68,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EVQk5wqb73SzprdJXKMZAu","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"05dfa9c4-3fd2-49cd-8815-1cf299a5dfa7","request_id":"req_011CbcJ3zQiNMFUPuuHJCrzX","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_97"}
