{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U5Xgcc9BYxkE1cXn6vX2Zb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale — sos_97 Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\n2\t\n3\tCard: `{1}{B}{B}` Legendary Planeswalker — Ral, starting loyalty 3, with four\n4\tloyalty abilities:\n5\t\n6\t- `+1: Surveil 2.`\n7\t- `−1: Any number of target players each discard a card.`\n8\t- `−2: Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.`\n9\t- `−7: Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X is the number of coins that came up heads.`\n10\t\n11\t## File: `cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`\n12\t\n13\tConventions discovered and followed:\n14\t- Planeswalker shape from fdn_134 (Ajani): abilities exposed via\n15\t  `get_loyalty_abilities()` returning `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect)`\n16\t  dataclasses; the effect reads its target from the planeswalker's\n17\t  `chosen_targets` / `_resolve_target` attribute.\n18\t- Surveil from fdn_53: top of library is the END of the zone list; the\n19\t  controller uses `choose_yes_no` to decide whether each examined card goes to\n20\t  the graveyard. The `DeterministicPlayer` script feeds those yes/no answers.\n21\t- Mana value via `card.mana_cost.cmc`.\n22\t\n23\t### TestRalProperties\n24\tStatic data contract: planeswalker type, exact name, `{1}{B}{B}` cost,\n25\tLegendary supertype, `\"Ral\"` subtype, and starting/current loyalty of 3.\n26\t\n27\t### TestRalLoyaltyAbilityDeclaration\n28\t- `test_returns_four_abilities` — all four printed abilities are exposed.\n29\t- `test_each_is_loyalty_ability` — each is a `LoyaltyAbility` instance.\n30\t- `test_loyalty_costs_match_spec` — the loyalty costs are exactly\n31\t  `{+1, -1, -2, -7}`. This is the structural contract the rest of the\n32\t  behavioural tests select abilities by.\n33\t\n34\t### TestRalSurveil (+1: Surveil 2)\n35\t- `test_surveil_puts_both_chosen_cards_into_graveyard` — when the controller\n36\t  opts to bin both examined cards, both top cards move to the graveyard.\n37\t- `test_surveil_keeps_cards_on_top_when_declined` — declining leaves the\n38\t  library size unchanged and the graveyard empty (cards stay on top).\n39\t- `test_surveil_with_fewer_than_two_cards_does_not_raise` — edge case: only one\n40\t  card in library; Surveil 2 must examine what's available without crashing.\n41\t- `test_surveil_empty_library_does_not_raise` — edge case: empty library is a\n42\t  safe no-op.\n43\t\n44\tI deliberately do NOT assert the relative ordering of cards kept on top (the\n45\t\"put the rest back in any order\" clause) — ordering among retained cards is a\n46\tfree player choice and not a defined contract.\n47\t\n48\t### TestRalDiscard (−1: target players each discard)\n49\t- `test_targeted_player_discards_a_card` — the targeted opponent loses the\n50\t  chosen card from hand to graveyard.\n51\t- `test_no_targets_is_a_noop` — \"any number of target players\" includes zero;\n52\t  with no targets nobody discards and nothing raises.\n53\t- `test_targeted_player_with_empty_hand_does_not_raise` — a targeted player\n54\t  with an empty hand simply discards nothing.\n55\t\n56\t### TestRalReanimate (−2: return mv≤3 creature from your graveyard)\n57\t- `test_returns_low_mv_creature_to_battlefield` — mv-2 creature returns to the\n58\t  battlefield and leaves the graveyard.\n59\t- `test_mv_exactly_three_is_legal` — boundary: mana value exactly 3 is allowed.\n60\t- `test_target_filter_rejects_high_mv_creature` — boundary: mv-4 creature is not\n61\t  reanimated (stays in graveyard).\n62\t- `test_target_filter_rejects_noncreature` — a noncreature card (instant) is not\n63\t  a legal target even at low mana value.\n64\t- `test_only_your_graveyard` — a low-mv creature in the opponent's graveyard is\n65\t  not reanimated onto your battlefield.\n66\t- `test_no_target_chosen_is_a_noop` — defensive: no chosen target leaves the\n67\t  graveyard untouched.\n68\t\n69\t### TestRalUltimate (−7: coin flips + skip turns)\n70\t- `test_ultimate_loyalty_cost_is_minus_seven` — structural: the ultimate is\n71\t  declared at −7.\n72\t- `test_ultimate_resolution_does_not_raise` — resolving the ultimate must not\n73\t  crash regardless of coin outcomes.\n74\t\n75\tThe randomness of the five coin flips and the \"target opponent skips their next\n76\tX turns\" effect are not backed by a deterministic engine API (no coin-flip\n77\thelper; `GameState.extra_turns` is an *insert* queue with a documented\n78\tENGINE LIMITATION that `'skip your next turn'` is \"not fully handled\"). The\n79\texact number of skipped turns therefore can't be asserted deterministically.\n80\tSee `untestable.json`. We still pin the loyalty cost and the no-raise contract.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UumXJUJw93ejA2gnrdyZs9","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"35a539f4-2920-4635-9d33-05694c8f10e3","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:22:42.119Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend sos_97 tests for ultimate"}
