{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Gg4PYdcQdKRd4jsfoDCLUL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016j3VFAEhvEpfsZShdKk4xJ","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-rationale.md","old_string":"ENGINE LIMITATION that `'skip your next turn'` is \"not fully handled\"). The\nexact number of skipped turns therefore can't be asserted deterministically.\nSee `untestable.json`. We still pin the loyalty cost and the no-raise contract.","new_string":"ENGINE LIMITATION that `'skip your next turn'` is \"not fully handled\"). The\nexact number of skipped turns therefore can't be asserted deterministically.\nSee `untestable.json`. We still pin the loyalty cost and the no-raise contract.\n\n## Update — ultimate now fully covered (additive engine support landed)\n\nThe Implementer added two additive engine capabilities that unblock the two\npreviously-untestable −7 clauses:\n\n- `GameState.flip_coin(player)` — deterministic when `player` is a scripted\n  `DeterministicPlayer`; it reads each flip result from the player's\n  `choose_yes_no` script (`True` == heads). The ultimate flips with\n  `flipper = pw.controller`, so a test forces a known head count by extending\n  the controller's (`p1._script`) yes/no queue with five booleans.\n- `Player.skipped_turns` (default 0) — a per-player counter incremented by the\n  ultimate (`target.skipped_turns += X`) and consumed by\n  `GameState._apply_skipped_turns()` from `advance_phase` when the rotation\n  would make the skipped player active.\n\nNew tests added to `TestRalUltimate` in `cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` (all PASS\nagainst the current implementation):\n\n- `test_ultimate_forced_head_count_sets_skipped_turns` — scripts three heads +\n  two tails; asserts X == 3 by checking the opponent's `skipped_turns` becomes\n  exactly 3 (and was 0 beforehand). Validates the \"X = number of heads\"\n  computation and that the count is applied to the target opponent.\n- `test_ultimate_all_tails_skips_no_turns` — five tails -> X == 0 -> opponent's\n  `skipped_turns` stays 0. Lower boundary of the coin-flip count.\n- `test_ultimate_all_heads_skips_five_turns` — five heads -> X == 5 ->\n  opponent's `skipped_turns` increases by 5. Upper boundary.\n- `test_ultimate_adds_to_existing_skipped_turns` — pre-seeds one queued skip and\n  forces X == 2, asserting the result is 3. Confirms the effect *adds* X rather\n  than overwriting, matching `+=` semantics.\n- `test_skipped_turn_is_consumed_by_turn_rotation` — forces exactly one head,\n  then drives the live turn loop (`advance_to_phase(... ENDING/CLEANUP)` +\n  `advance_phase()`) through the end-of-turn wrap. Asserts the queued skip is\n  consumed (`skipped_turns` back to 0) and that the opponent did NOT become the\n  active player — the turn was handed back to the controller. This exercises the\n  skip on the real `advance_phase` rotation path, not just the counter.\n- `test_zero_heads_leaves_turn_rotation_unchanged` — control case: with X == 0 no\n  skip is queued, so the same turn-wrap hands the next turn to the opponent\n  normally. Confirms the skip hook is a strict no-op when nothing is queued\n  (guards against a regression that would skip turns unconditionally).\n\nThese replace the two `untestable.json` entries, which are now removed\n(`untestable.json` is `[]`). Coin-flip results are sourced from the controller's\n`DeterministicPlayer` script per the engine's `flip_coin` contract; turn\nrotation is driven through `test_utils.advance_to_phase` + the live\n`GameState.advance_phase`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":197,"cache_read_input_tokens":47063,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":197,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UumXJUJw93ejA2gnrdyZs9","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"448c6b1d-4753-4bb0-8907-a10bd75aeecc","request_id":"req_011CbcJCNgtKAh7ZnLJzZraB","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend sos_97 tests for ultimate"}
