{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01635CqLvoKtd3UuJejs8wag","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer — implementation rationale\n2\t\n3\t## Card\n4\t`RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker)` at `cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py`.\n5\t- {1}{B}{B}, Legendary Planeswalker — Ral, starting loyalty 3.\n6\t- Follows fdn_134 (Ajani) planeswalker pattern: `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns\n7\t  `LoyaltyAbility` dataclasses; the ability's target is read from\n8\t  `self.chosen_targets` / `self._resolve_target` (set by the resolution pipeline\n9\t  or tests). `get_targets()` returns `[]` per KEY_DECISIONS so casting the\n10\t  planeswalker never requires a card-level target.\n11\t\n12\t## Loyalty abilities (all four declared; three fully built)\n13\t- **+1 Surveil 2**: top of library is the END of the internal list (fdn_53\n14\t  convention). Examines up to two cards top-first; `controller.choose_yes_no`\n15\t  decides whether each goes to the graveyard. Stops on the first \"keep\" so kept\n16\t  cards stay on top (Surveil \"rest back on top\"). Safe on 0/1-card libraries.\n17\t- **−1 each target player discards**: iterates `chosen_targets`; each target picks\n18\t  a card via `choose_card` and is discarded via `engine.game.discard`. Empty hand\n19\t  and zero targets are no-ops.\n20\t- **−2 reanimate**: target must be a CREATURE card, mana value (`mana_cost.cmc`)\n21\t  ≤ 3, and in the *controller's* graveyard. Filters reject mv≥4, noncreatures,\n22\t  and opponent-graveyard cards; missing target is a no-op. Uses\n23\t  `move_to_zone(GRAVEYARD → BATTLEFIELD)` after setting controller.\n24\t- **−7 ultimate**: flips five coins, X = heads, then `target.skipped_turns += X`.\n25\t\n26\t## Engine capabilities added (ADDITIVE — both BUILT, not UNVERIFIED)\n27\t1. **Coin-flip primitive** — `GameState.flip_coin(player)` returns True for heads.\n28\t   When `player` is a scripted `DeterministicPlayer` with queued answers it reads\n29\t   the result via `choose_yes_no` (so a test can force a known head count); else\n30\t   falls back to `random.choice`. Purely additive new method.\n31\t2. **Turn-skipping** — `Player.skipped_turns` (default 0) plus\n32\t   `GameState._apply_skipped_turns()`, invoked from `advance_phase` right after\n33\t   the active player rotates at end of turn. If the newly-active player has\n34\t   `skipped_turns > 0`, it decrements one and advances the normal rotation to the\n35\t   other player, looping for consecutive skips (bounded for termination).\n36\t   Default `skipped_turns == 0` makes the hook a strict no-op, so existing turn\n37\t   rotation is unchanged.\n38\t\n39\tThe real turn loop (`engine/turn.py::run_turn`) rotates via `advance_phase`, so\n40\tthe skip hook is on the live path — the ultimate's turn-skip is genuinely BUILT,\n41\tnot stubbed.\n42\t\n43\t## Verification\n44\t- `pytest cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` → 24 passed.\n45\t- `pytest engine_tests/` → 1145 passed (no regressions; default no-op preserved).\n46\t- Full `pytest` → 1297 passed.\n47\t\n48\t## Notes for future cards\n49\t- Reusable engine infra: `GameState.flip_coin(player)` (scriptable) and\n50\t  `Player.skipped_turns` + `advance_phase` skip handling.\n51\t- No Keyword enum members added; no `gain_life` helper used.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01PySzzbrAYznBkWFA71GV2i","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"c352347c-e7c7-4bc0-bec7-649bf88c9211","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:24:53.926Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_97"}
