{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a9e435e9b4f189291","tool_use_id":"toolu_0198UBh9jYEY1h89QqAe4jK8","description":"Writing /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-rationale.md","subagent_type":"Tester","usage":{"total_tokens":83269,"tool_uses":33,"duration_ms":159973},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"238420be-3db2-416f-8973-ca858230c0e5","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01CGnvH4gNLbnwumw5aP9pqR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XbZvAqKJKWuPDNXnVbHV1m","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — sos_120 Improvisation Capstone\n\nCard: **Improvisation Capstone** — `{5}{R}{R}` Sorcery — Lesson (mythic).\n\nOracle text:\n> Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile cards with total mana\n> value 4 or greater. You may cast any number of spells from among them without\n> paying their mana costs.\n> Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this name,\n> you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the\n> beginning of each of your first main phases.)\n\n## File: `cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py`\n\nAll tests drive the card's `on_resolve(game)` directly with a staged library,\nfollowing the FDN/SOS convention of exercising resolution in isolation\n(fdn_205, sos_57). The `_set_library` helper places cards so the FIRST element\nis the TOP of the library (the engine's `ZoneContainer` treats index `-1` as\ntop), making the exile order unambiguous.\n\n### `TestImprovisationCapstoneProperties` — static card data\n- `test_is_sorcery` / `test_card_type_includes_sorcery` — it is a Sorcery.\n- `test_name` — name matches the spec.\n- `test_mana_cost` — cost is `{5}{R}{R}`.\n- `test_is_red` — two red pips + five generic (color identity).\n- `test_has_lesson_subtype` — the `Lesson` subtype from the `Sorcery — Lesson`\n  type line is present.\n\n### `TestImprovisationCapstoneExileUntilFour` — \"Exile … until total mana value 4 or greater\"\nThis is the card's central deterministic mechanic, tested for the exact\nthreshold semantics:\n- `test_exiles_until_total_mv_reaches_four` — three MV-2 cards: 2+2=4 reaches the\n  threshold on the second card; the third stays in the library (no over-exile).\n- `test_total_mana_value_of_exiled_is_at_least_four` — invariant: the exiled pile\n  always sums to >= 4 when the library can supply it.\n- `test_stops_on_card_that_crosses_threshold` — 1+1+3=5 crosses 4 on the third\n  card; exactly three are exiled and the fourth is untouched. Verifies the loop\n  stops on (and includes) the crossing card, not before/after.\n- `test_single_high_mv_card_stops_immediately` — a lone MV-4 card satisfies the\n  threshold by itself; only it is exiled.\n- `test_exiles_from_top_of_library` — confirms top-of-library order (not bottom).\n- `test_small_library_exiles_everything_without_raising` — library that can never\n  reach MV 4 is fully exiled with no exception (defensive edge case).\n- `test_empty_library_is_a_noop` — empty library exiles nothing, no exception.\n- `test_uses_controllers_library_not_opponents` — \"your library\" is the\n  controller's; the opponent's library/exile are never touched.\n\n### `TestImprovisationCapstoneFreeCast` — \"You may cast any number of spells … without paying their mana costs\"\n- `test_castable_spell_among_exiles_can_be_cast_for_free` — with the controller\n  holding zero mana, an exiled spell is cast for free: it leaves the library,\n  leaves exile, resolves into the graveyard, and no red mana is consumed. The\n  \"may\" is scripted via the DeterministicPlayer script. This is the end-to-end\n  proof of the free-cast clause.\n- `test_resolution_does_not_raise_when_no_spells_to_cast` — when the exiled pile\n  contains only a non-castable permanent (a creature can't be free-cast as a\n  sorcery-speed \"spell from among them\" without targeting/choices), resolution\n  still completes and the exile-to-threshold step still happened.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately NOT contract-tested\n- **Paradigm** (the entire reminder-text clause): recorded in `untestable.json`.\n  \"Paradigm\" is not a member of `engine.types.Keyword`, and per `KEY_DECISIONS.md`\n  the enum is frozen at 16 members (adding one zeros an authoritative engine\n  test). The delayed \"exile this spell, then cast a copy from exile at the\n  beginning of each of your first main phases\" recursion has no engine surface\n  to assert against in a way that wouldn't pin the implementer to one specific\n  (and possibly wrong) modeling choice.\n- **\"any number\" multi-spell free-casting** — the contract verifies that at\n  least one spell can be free-cast; the precise multi-choice loop (cast 0, 1, or\n  N of the exiled spells) is left to the implementer rather than over-specified,\n  since the choice-prompt protocol for \"cast any number\" is not fixed by the\n  engine API.\n- **Casting permanents from the exiled pile** — exiled creatures/artifacts are\n  technically castable spells, but free-casting a permanent at this point pins\n  the implementation to specific ETB/targeting behavior the engine does not\n  standardize; left out of scope.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":761,"cache_read_input_tokens":82176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":761,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0198UBh9jYEY1h89QqAe4jK8","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"aebee8ff-8f2c-4db1-b9a9-38e0eb24a296","request_id":"req_011CbcJbCiW688byir23B5bK","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_120"}
