{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016nBC1pN8nHhPWDXg1ooE4D","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator directives — sos_120 (Improvisation Capstone)\n2\t\n3\t## Build (in scope, fully tested)\n4\tThe core spell behavior, whatever the spec says — typically: exile cards from the\n5\ttop of your library until you exile one with mana value >= 4 (read card_spec.json\n6\tfor exact threshold/wording), then cast that exiled spell (free / per the spec).\n7\tMake ALL current tests in `cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py` pass. Follow KEY_DECISIONS.md\n8\tconventions (no Keyword enum additions; get_targets()==[] while on stack for ability\n9\ttargets; reuse existing free-cast helpers like cast_spell_free as in sos_1).\n10\t\n11\t## \"Paradigm\" mechanic — mark UNVERIFIED (out of scope)\n12\tOracle: \"Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this name, you\n13\tmay cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of\n14\teach of your first main phases.\"\n15\t\n16\tThis requires copy-from-exile machinery that the engine does NOT have (the same gap\n17\twe marked UNVERIFIED for sos_13's copy-cast). \"Paradigm\" also cannot be a `Keyword`\n18\tmember (the enum is frozen at 16 members — see KEY_DECISIONS.md).\n19\t\n20\tScope:\n21\t- You MAY add LOW-RISK additive scaffolding that doesn't require new fragile systems:\n22\t  e.g. exile the spell after it resolves, and record a first-resolution flag/state on\n23\t  the card. Only if it's clean and doesn't risk regressions.\n24\t- DO NOT build a generic \"cast a copy of a card from exile\" system or a recurring\n25\t  name-keyed delayed trigger pipeline — that is a large, fragile feature out of scope.\n26\t- Mark the recurring copy-cast clause with a grep-able\n27\t  `# UNVERIFIED: <requirement> — <reason>` comment in `cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py`,\n28\t  noting it needs copy-from-exile engine support.\n29\t\n30\t## Constraints\n31\t- Make ALL tests pass; do NOT modify tests.\n32\t- Engine changes ADDITIVE only; after any engine change run `pytest engine_tests/` and\n33\t  keep it green. Do NOT add Keyword enum members. Do NOT touch engine_tests/ or FDN tests.\n34\t- Prefer a green engine_tests/ suite and a correct core over Paradigm completeness.\n35\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017AGMNzioYKWCAQpAoWPvcJ","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"29a4c713-a7a3-422f-bd5c-7cd64bb872eb","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:32:53.552Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_120"}
