{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01JzUUHmuTL2hXXTnnoKqUYx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018mMwVxg6Ri7pxYyjU3djE1","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":950,"cache_read_input_tokens":22305,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":950,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017AGMNzioYKWCAQpAoWPvcJ","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"650a749e-a694-4395-924a-0be35bff232a","request_id":"req_011CbcJu5e6qTdMCiE2R6eMv","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_120"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018mMwVxg6Ri7pxYyjU3djE1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\tPersistent, append-only conventions and decisions across runs.\n4\t\n5\t## Card-level `get_targets()` vs. triggered-ability targets (from sos_1)\n6\tThe casting pipeline (`engine/casting.py`) calls `card.get_targets(game)` for the\n7\tSPELL ITSELF and forces the controller to choose those targets when the spell is\n8\tcast. So `get_targets()` must only advertise targets the *spell* takes. If a card's\n9\ttargeting belongs to a triggered ability (e.g. \"whenever this attacks, target ...\"),\n10\tdo NOT expose it via the card-level `get_targets()` — otherwise casting the permanent\n11\twrongly requires/consumes a target (and can raise `CastingError` when none is legal).\n12\tThe pipeline moves the card into the controller's `STACK` zone before querying\n13\t`get_targets()`, so a card can detect \"am I being cast right now?\" by checking\n14\twhether `self` is in any player's `STACK` zone and return `[]` in that case. Have the\n15\ttriggered ability choose its own target (via `player.choose_target`) at resolution.\n16\t\n17\t## Converge / multi-target / life-gain conventions (from sos_4)\n18\t- **Converge X** = `len(self.colors_spent)`. The casting pipeline records the\n19\t  distinct colors of mana spent as a LIST of `engine.types.Color` on\n20\t  `card.colors_spent` (not an int). Initialize `colors_spent` to `[]` in\n21\t  `__init__`; compute X with `len(...)`. (Note: fdn_205 used an int because it\n22\t  bypassed the cast pipeline — prefer the list shape for real cards.)\n23\t- **Multi-target ordering**: `chosen_targets` is ordered to match the oracle text\n24\t  order of the `TargetRequirement`s returned by `get_targets()`. E.g. \"Target\n25\t  player ... deals X damage to any target\" → `chosen_targets[0]` = target player,\n26\t  `chosen_targets[1]` = any-target.\n27\t- **Life gain**: there is no `gain_life` engine helper. Gain life directly via\n28\t  `controller.life += x`. Damage uses `engine.game.deal_damage`, draw uses\n29\t  `engine.game.draw_card`.\n30\t- Resolution should short-circuit on X <= 0 and defend against missing\n31\t  `chosen_targets`/`colors_spent` so it never raises.\n32\t\n33\t## Do NOT add members to `engine.types.Keyword` (from sos_13)\n34\tThe authoritative engine regression test\n35\t`engine_tests/test_types.py::TestKeyword::test_exactly_sixteen_members` asserts\n36\t`len(Keyword) == 16`. `engine_tests/` is read-only and authoritative for grading,\n37\tso adding ANY new `Keyword` enum member zeros that test. For cards introducing a\n38\tnew \"keyword\" that isn't already in the enum (e.g. \"Prepared\"), DO NOT add an enum\n39\tmember. Instead model the mechanic's runtime state with a plain attribute/bool on\n40\tthe card (e.g. `is_prepared`) and mark unimplementable sub-clauses with grep-able\n41\t`# UNVERIFIED: <requirement> — <reason>` comments. Same caution likely applies to\n42\tother \"exactly N members\" enum-count tests — check `engine_tests/test_types.py`\n43\tbefore extending any engine enum.\n44\t\n45\t## New engine infrastructure added (from sos_57) — reuse for later cards\n46\t- **`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`** added to `engine/events.py`, fired from\n47\t  `GameState.advance_phase` via `_fire_beginning_of_main_phase()`. It pushes a\n48\t  StackObject (does NOT resolve immediately), so `empty_mana_pools()` after it does\n49\t  not wipe mana the trigger later produces during stack resolution. Use this for any\n50\t  \"at the beginning of your/the next (pre/post-combat) main phase\" delayed trigger.\n51\t- **`card.mana_spent`** is now recorded during casting in `engine/casting.py`\n52\t  (`= effective_cost.cmc`), alongside `colors_spent`. Use it for effects keyed on\n53\t  \"the amount of mana spent to cast that spell\".\n54\t- Counterspell pattern (cf. fdn_160): remove the target spell's StackObject from the\n55\t  stack, remove the card from its controller's STACK zone, add to the OWNER's\n56\t  graveyard, and never run its `on_resolve`. `get_targets()` advertises one\n57\t  `TargetRequirement` with `zone == Zone.STACK` filtering for spells.\n58\t\n59\t## More engine infrastructure (from sos_97) — reuse for later cards\n60\t- **`GameState.flip_coin(player)`** — deterministic coin flip, scriptable through\n61\t  the existing DeterministicPlayer mechanism (`choose_yes_no`), falls back to RNG\n62\t  when no script. Use for any \"flip a coin\" card; tests force outcomes via the\n63\t  player's `_script`.\n64\t- **`Player.skipped_turns`** (int, default 0) — consumed by `_apply_skipped_turns()`\n65\t  in `GameState.advance_phase`. Default 0 is a strict no-op (loop never enters), so\n66\t  normal turn rotation is unaffected. Use `target.skipped_turns += X` for\n67\t  \"skips their next X turns\" effects.\n68\t- Engine extension recipe that worked twice (sos_57, sos_97): add new event\n69\t  classes / attributes / hooks ADDITIVELY, make the default value a no-op, and run\n70\t  `pytest engine_tests/` after each change to confirm zero regressions.\n71\t\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017AGMNzioYKWCAQpAoWPvcJ","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"bc54fd2f-870a-4db0-89a8-27df9c95080d","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:33:09.255Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_120"}
