{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Ppw571pBdoRqyWsd5prVDS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RdTPMfQzwdQb7d8mCTw9Qj","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — SOS 201, Lorehold, the Historian\n\nCard: `{3}{R}{W}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5.\nOracle text:\n- Flying, haste\n- Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}.\n- At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\n\n## File: `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`\n\n### `TestLoreholdProperties` — static card data\nValidates the printed characteristics straight from the spec:\n- `test_is_creature` — the impl subclasses `Creature`.\n- `test_name` — name is \"Lorehold, the Historian\".\n- `test_mana_cost` — `{3}{R}{W}`.\n- `test_power_toughness` — base P/T 5/5.\n- `test_is_legendary` — `Supertype.LEGENDARY` present.\n- `test_is_elder_dragon` — subtypes include both \"Elder\" and \"Dragon\".\n- `test_has_flying` / `test_has_haste` — both evergreen keywords are in `Keyword`, so they are asserted directly via the `keywords` flag set.\n- `test_is_red_white` — cost carries both a red and a white pip.\n\n### `TestLoreholdMiracleGrant` — \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}\"\nMiracle is NOT a member of `engine.types.Keyword` and, per `KEY_DECISIONS.md`,\nthe enum must not be extended (the `test_exactly_sixteen_members` regression\nlocks it). So the card must model miracle as a custom mechanic. These tests\npin the *granting contract* — a queryable miracle cost of `{2}` for the\ncontroller's instants/sorceries — without hard-coding the method name (the\nhelper `_miracle_cost` probes `get_miracle_cost` / `miracle_cost_for` /\n`granted_miracle_cost`).\n- `test_instant_in_your_hand_gets_miracle_two` — an instant in your hand reports miracle `{2}`.\n- `test_sorcery_in_your_hand_gets_miracle_two` — a sorcery in your hand reports miracle `{2}`.\n- `test_creature_in_your_hand_gets_no_miracle` — non-instant/non-sorcery cards get no grant (`None`). Edge case: the grant is type-restricted.\n- `test_opponent_hand_spell_gets_no_miracle` — restricted to \"your hand\"; an opponent's instant gets nothing. Edge case: controller scoping.\n- `test_spell_in_graveyard_gets_no_miracle` — restricted to the hand zone; a spell in the graveyard gets nothing. Edge case: zone scoping.\n\n### `TestLoreholdLootTriggerRegistration` — opponent-upkeep trigger wiring\nThe loot ability is \"at the beginning of each opponent's upkeep\". The engine's\n`BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` fires for the active player's upkeep and\ncarries no player field, so the controller-vs-opponent distinction must live in\nthe trigger's `condition` (keyed off `game.active_player_index`).\n- `test_registers_one_upkeep_trigger` — exactly one trigger registered.\n- `test_registered_trigger_watches_upkeep_event` — event type is `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`.\n- `test_trigger_fires_on_opponent_upkeep` — condition true when the opponent (index 1) is active.\n- `test_trigger_does_not_fire_on_own_upkeep` — condition false when the controller (index 0) is active. This test explicitly rejects an always-fire (`condition is None`) trigger, since \"each opponent's upkeep\" requires the distinction.\n\n### `TestLoreholdLootEffect` — \"you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card\"\nFires an opponent's upkeep via the trigger manager and resolves the stack. The\nshared `_fire_opponent_upkeep` helper returns the number of objects the event\npushed onto the stack, so every effect test also asserts `pushed >= 1` — a stub\nthat registers no trigger fails rather than passing trivially.\n- `test_discard_then_draw_keeps_hand_size` — looting one card is net-zero on hand size, the pitched card is in the graveyard, and the drawn library card is in hand.\n- `test_discard_card_goes_to_graveyard` — the discarded card lands in the controller's graveyard.\n- `test_drawn_card_enters_hand` — the looted draw moves the top library card from library to hand.\n- `test_declining_discard_draws_nothing` — \"you may\" / \"if you do\": declining (scripted `False`) means no discard and no draw, but the trigger still fires. Edge case: the conditional draw.\n- `test_empty_hand_is_a_noop` — empty hand: the trigger fires but loots nothing and does not raise. Edge case: nothing to discard.\n\n## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered\n- **Miracle \"cast when you drew it, first card this turn\" timing** — there is no\n  engine surface for the miracle draw/reveal/alternative-cast window\n  (`cards_drawn_this_turn` exists on the player but no miracle cast pipeline or\n  draw-window hook). Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n- **Flying combat restriction** (which creatures may block) — covered by the\n  engine's own `_can_block` and the FDN reference tests; out of scope for a\n  card whose flying is a plain evergreen keyword already asserted via the\n  `keywords` flag.\n- **Haste / summoning-sickness interaction** — haste is asserted as a keyword;\n  the engine owns summoning-sickness resolution, so re-testing it here would be\n  testing the engine rather than the card.\n- **Legend rule** for the legendary supertype — engine state-based action, out\n  of scope.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":504,"cache_read_input_tokens":81768,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":504,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012dceDh3xorVVFv4Ptv6oen","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"ac2a5d3d-4e03-47f8-a06d-e5ba7a5c2a15","request_id":"req_011CbcKBNc1o7Dy4sHGH1TaT","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_201"}
