{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Bn4mQqPEGTVc2Qheyy6vvL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EWcQDwFRYdpGN4JwCdvtSk","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md","old_string":"## Untestable resolution: sos_120","new_string":"## Untestable resolution: sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian)\n- Testable/implemented: Flying, Haste, the STATIC miracle grant (queryable {2}\n  miracle cost on controller's hand instants/sorceries), and the opponent-upkeep\n  loot trigger.\n- The DYNAMIC miracle clause (reveal the first card drawn this turn and cast it for\n  the {2} miracle cost) needs a reveal-on-draw window hook + an alternative-cost cast\n  entry. `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` and DrawsCardTriggeredEvent exist as partial\n  surface.\n- **Decision**: option (a) attempt to BUILD additively (mirroring sos_57/sos_97);\n  UNVERIFIED fallback for any part that can't be done additively without regressing\n  engine_tests/. Tester re-invoked once iff the miracle window lands.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_120"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":582,"cache_read_input_tokens":99103,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":582},"output_tokens":81,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"073e75a6-8a2f-4232-a089-7cafed028107","request_id":"req_011CbcKEZd8ZBvF1UmgkGtrB"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EWcQDwFRYdpGN4JwCdvtSk","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"61315736-b491-4249-8279-eb105b0dafd7","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:37:49.537Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"## Untestable resolution: sos_120","newString":"## Untestable resolution: sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian)\n- Testable/implemented: Flying, Haste, the STATIC miracle grant (queryable {2}\n  miracle cost on controller's hand instants/sorceries), and the opponent-upkeep\n  loot trigger.\n- The DYNAMIC miracle clause (reveal the first card drawn this turn and cast it for\n  the {2} miracle cost) needs a reveal-on-draw window hook + an alternative-cost cast\n  entry. `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` and DrawsCardTriggeredEvent exist as partial\n  surface.\n- **Decision**: option (a) attempt to BUILD additively (mirroring sos_57/sos_97);\n  UNVERIFIED fallback for any part that can't be done additively without regressing\n  engine_tests/. Tester re-invoked once iff the miracle window lands.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_120","originalFile":"# Run Decisions\n\nDecisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_120 (Improvisation Capstone)\n- Core (exile from top until a card with MV>=4 is found, free-cast it) is fully\n  testable/implemented.\n- The \"Paradigm\" mechanic (\"exile this spell; after you first resolve a spell with\n  this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the\n  beginning of each of your first main phases\") requires copy-from-exile machinery\n  that does NOT exist (same gap marked UNVERIFIED for sos_13's copy-cast). \"Paradigm\"\n  also can't be a Keyword (frozen 16-member enum).\n- **Decision**: option (b) accept partial coverage. The recurring copy-cast clause is\n  marked `# UNVERIFIED`. Implementer may add low-risk additive scaffolding (exile the\n  spell after resolution, record first-resolution state) but must NOT build a fragile\n  generic copy-from-exile system. No Tester re-invocation (no agreed observable contract).\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer — planeswalker)\n- Three of four abilities (Surveil 2, targeted discard, mv<=3 reanimation) fully\n  testable/implemented.\n- The -7 ultimate needs two ADDITIVE engine capabilities: (1) a deterministic\n  coin-flip helper (scriptable via DeterministicPlayer) so X = heads is assertable,\n  and (2) a per-player skipped-turns mechanism consulted by turn rotation.\n- **Decision**: option (a) attempt to BUILD both additively (mirroring sos_57). If a\n  part would regress engine_tests/ (esp. the turn loop) or need non-additive changes,\n  fall back to (b) `# UNVERIFIED` for that part. Tester re-invoked once for whatever lands.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)\n- Counter half (core) is fully testable/implemented.\n- The Wizard-gated delayed \"{C} at the beginning of your next main phase = mana\n  spent on the countered spell\" needs two ADDITIVE engine capabilities:\n  (1) a beginning-of-main-phase triggered event in engine/events.py fired from the\n  turn loop, and (2) recording total mana spent to cast a spell on the card/StackObject.\n- **Decision**: option (a) attempt to BUILD it additively. Implementer instructed to\n  add both capabilities additively; if any part would regress engine_tests/ or require\n  non-additive engine changes, fall back to (b) `# UNVERIFIED` markers for that part\n  and report. Tester re-invoked once IFF the engine support lands, to add {C}-bonus tests.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n- **Item 1 — \"Prepared\" keyword as a first-class flag**: INITIALLY directed as (a)\n  build it, but DOWNGRADED to (b) accept partial coverage. Adding `PREPARED` to\n  `engine.types.Keyword` regresses the authoritative read-only engine test\n  `engine_tests/test_types.py::TestKeyword::test_exactly_sixteen_members`\n  (asserts `len(Keyword) == 16`). Since engine_tests/ is authoritative for grading\n  and must not be modified, the keyword cannot be added without zeroing that test.\n  Implementer correctly declined and marked it `# UNVERIFIED`. The prepared state is\n  fully expressed via the `is_prepared` bool (tested). No Tester re-invocation.\n- **Item 2 — \"cast a copy of its spell while prepared, unpreparing it\"**: resolved\n  via (b) accept partial coverage. Requires major copy-cast/split-card engine\n  machinery; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:` marker added in card_impl.py.\n- **Item 3 — the \"Swords to Plowshares\" {W} instant face**: resolved via (b). The\n  engine has no second-castable-face representation; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:`\n  marker added in card_impl.py.\n- The conditional prepared STATE is exposed as an `is_prepared` bool (tested).\n\n## Test dispute: sos_4\n- **Disputed test**: `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player` (tests.py L180-198)\n- **Tester's intent**: verify \"you gain X life\" goes to the controller, not the target player, while the chosen any-target takes damage.\n- **Implementer's objection (feasibility)**: the test uses `chosen_targets=[p2, p1]`, naming p1 (controller) as the damage any-target (index 1), but asserts p2 (index 0) is damaged. This contradicts `test_two_colors_deals_two_damage_to_player` ([p1,p2] -> p2 damaged at index 1). No single index mapping satisfies both.\n- **Decision**: accept implementer (feasibility objection — test data is internally contradictory). Convention is draw=chosen_targets[0], damage any-target=chosen_targets[1], life gain=controller.\n- **Action**: re-invoke Tester to rewrite ONLY the disputed test, changing its data to `[p2, p2]` (draw target p2, damage any-target p2) so the intended \"life goes to controller p1\" check holds under the suite's index-1=damage convention.\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":6,"newStart":2,"newLines":18,"lines":[" "," Decisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`."," ","+## Untestable resolution: sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian)","+- Testable/implemented: Flying, Haste, the STATIC miracle grant (queryable {2}","+  miracle cost on controller's hand instants/sorceries), and the opponent-upkeep","+  loot trigger.","+- The DYNAMIC miracle clause (reveal the first card drawn this turn and cast it for","+  the {2} miracle cost) needs a reveal-on-draw window hook + an alternative-cost cast","+  entry. `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` and DrawsCardTriggeredEvent exist as partial","+  surface.","+- **Decision**: option (a) attempt to BUILD additively (mirroring sos_57/sos_97);","+  UNVERIFIED fallback for any part that can't be done additively without regressing","+  engine_tests/. Tester re-invoked once iff the miracle window lands.","+"," ## Untestable resolution: sos_120 (Improvisation Capstone)"," - Core (exile from top until a card with MV>=4 is found, free-cast it) is fully","   testable/implemented."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01GeaxcEDNpKCspN6dxdoJCs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Sni22mzm83hNsQqACmfyVK","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator directives — sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian)\n\n## Build (in scope, fully tested)\n- The creature with Flying and Haste (and whatever other static keywords the spec\n  lists), correct name/cost/P-T/colors/subtypes.\n- The STATIC half of the miracle grant: \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand\n  has miracle {2}.\" Expose a queryable miracle cost ({2}) on the controller's\n  hand instants/sorceries per the test contract.\n- The opponent-upkeep loot trigger (read spec for exact wording — e.g. \"At the\n  beginning of each opponent's upkeep, ...\").\nMake ALL current tests in `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` pass. Follow KEY_DECISIONS.md\nconventions (no Keyword enum additions — frozen; get_targets()==[] while on stack;\nexisting infra: BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent, etc.).\n\n## Attempt to BUILD the DYNAMIC miracle cast (additive engine work)\nOracle: \"(You may cast a card for its miracle cost when you draw it if it's the\nfirst card you drew this turn.)\"\n\nAttempt this ADDITIVELY, reusing existing surface:\n- There is already `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` tracking and a\n  `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`. Add a reveal/miracle WINDOW hook fired when a player\n  draws their FIRST card of the turn (consult `cards_drawn_this_turn`), that offers\n  to cast that drawn card for its granted miracle cost ({2}).\n- Add an alternative-cost cast path (e.g. extend the existing free/alternative cast\n  helper in `engine/casting.py`, analogous to `cast_spell_free`, to support paying a\n  specified alternative cost) that the miracle window routes through.\n- Implement so that ONLY the first card drawn this turn qualifies, and only while\n  Lorehold is on the battlefield (the grant is active).\n\n### HARD CONSTRAINT — additive only + green engine_tests/\n- All engine changes ADDITIVE: new methods/attributes/branches; do NOT rename/move/\n  delete existing engine symbols; do NOT add Keyword enum members; do NOT touch\n  engine_tests/ or FDN tests.\n- After ANY engine change run `pytest engine_tests/` — it MUST stay green. The draw\n  pipeline is heavily tested; the new window must be a no-op when no miracle grant is\n  active and must not change normal draw behavior.\n- If the dynamic miracle window cannot be built additively without regressing\n  engine_tests/ or non-additively, DO NOT force it: mark it\n  `# UNVERIFIED: <requirement> — <reason>` in `cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` and\n  report which parts you built vs. left UNVERIFIED.\n\nPrefer a green engine_tests/ suite and correct static behavior over miracle\ncompleteness.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1692,"cache_read_input_tokens":99685,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1692},"output_tokens":42,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"1217a29d-d23e-430d-99d6-c553a28edf74","request_id":"req_011CbcKG5DtezGdaGjsvACeo"}
