{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EvNjsgJCRfeQV17xNccA6C","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"requirement\": \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}. (You may cast a card for its miracle cost when you draw it if it's the first card you drew this turn.)\",\n4\t    \"reason\": \"Only the static granting half of miracle can be tested (a queryable {2} miracle cost on the controller's hand instants/sorceries). The dynamic half - the draw-trigger window that lets you reveal a freshly-drawn card and cast it for the miracle cost when it is the first card drawn this turn - has no engine surface. There is no miracle alternative-cast pipeline, no reveal-on-draw hook, and DrawsCardTriggeredEvent does not carry a 'first card drawn this turn' flag (player.cards_drawn_this_turn is incremented but no miracle-window machinery consumes it). Miracle is also not a Keyword enum member and KEY_DECISIONS forbids extending that enum, so it must be modeled as custom card state.\",\n5\t    \"what_would_unblock\": \"An engine miracle mechanism: a draw-window hook (e.g. fired from draw_card / the draw step) that reveals the first card drawn this turn and offers an alternative cast at the granted miracle cost, plus a cast_spell_alternative-style entry the card can route the miracle cost through. With that surface, tests could draw a spell as the first card of the turn under Lorehold and assert it can be cast for {2} (and that a second draw same turn cannot).\"\n6\t  }\n7\t]\n8\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EsetUBrXacwixHmPHKwsvR","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"c024ebea-bfb6-441b-92db-4de1d2727843","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:38:23.779Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_201"}
