{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FAtMsz7ng4bkj9SkT5BFmL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale — SOS 201, Lorehold, the Historian\n2\t\n3\tCard: `{3}{R}{W}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5.\n4\tOracle text:\n5\t- Flying, haste\n6\t- Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}.\n7\t- At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\n8\t\n9\t## File: `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`\n10\t\n11\t### `TestLoreholdProperties` — static card data\n12\tValidates the printed characteristics straight from the spec:\n13\t- `test_is_creature` — the impl subclasses `Creature`.\n14\t- `test_name` — name is \"Lorehold, the Historian\".\n15\t- `test_mana_cost` — `{3}{R}{W}`.\n16\t- `test_power_toughness` — base P/T 5/5.\n17\t- `test_is_legendary` — `Supertype.LEGENDARY` present.\n18\t- `test_is_elder_dragon` — subtypes include both \"Elder\" and \"Dragon\".\n19\t- `test_has_flying` / `test_has_haste` — both evergreen keywords are in `Keyword`, so they are asserted directly via the `keywords` flag set.\n20\t- `test_is_red_white` — cost carries both a red and a white pip.\n21\t\n22\t### `TestLoreholdMiracleGrant` — \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}\"\n23\tMiracle is NOT a member of `engine.types.Keyword` and, per `KEY_DECISIONS.md`,\n24\tthe enum must not be extended (the `test_exactly_sixteen_members` regression\n25\tlocks it). So the card must model miracle as a custom mechanic. These tests\n26\tpin the *granting contract* — a queryable miracle cost of `{2}` for the\n27\tcontroller's instants/sorceries — without hard-coding the method name (the\n28\thelper `_miracle_cost` probes `get_miracle_cost` / `miracle_cost_for` /\n29\t`granted_miracle_cost`).\n30\t- `test_instant_in_your_hand_gets_miracle_two` — an instant in your hand reports miracle `{2}`.\n31\t- `test_sorcery_in_your_hand_gets_miracle_two` — a sorcery in your hand reports miracle `{2}`.\n32\t- `test_creature_in_your_hand_gets_no_miracle` — non-instant/non-sorcery cards get no grant (`None`). Edge case: the grant is type-restricted.\n33\t- `test_opponent_hand_spell_gets_no_miracle` — restricted to \"your hand\"; an opponent's instant gets nothing. Edge case: controller scoping.\n34\t- `test_spell_in_graveyard_gets_no_miracle` — restricted to the hand zone; a spell in the graveyard gets nothing. Edge case: zone scoping.\n35\t\n36\t### `TestLoreholdLootTriggerRegistration` — opponent-upkeep trigger wiring\n37\tThe loot ability is \"at the beginning of each opponent's upkeep\". The engine's\n38\t`BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` fires for the active player's upkeep and\n39\tcarries no player field, so the controller-vs-opponent distinction must live in\n40\tthe trigger's `condition` (keyed off `game.active_player_index`).\n41\t- `test_registers_one_upkeep_trigger` — exactly one trigger registered.\n42\t- `test_registered_trigger_watches_upkeep_event` — event type is `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`.\n43\t- `test_trigger_fires_on_opponent_upkeep` — condition true when the opponent (index 1) is active.\n44\t- `test_trigger_does_not_fire_on_own_upkeep` — condition false when the controller (index 0) is active. This test explicitly rejects an always-fire (`condition is None`) trigger, since \"each opponent's upkeep\" requires the distinction.\n45\t\n46\t### `TestLoreholdLootEffect` — \"you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card\"\n47\tFires an opponent's upkeep via the trigger manager and resolves the stack. The\n48\tshared `_fire_opponent_upkeep` helper returns the number of objects the event\n49\tpushed onto the stack, so every effect test also asserts `pushed >= 1` — a stub\n50\tthat registers no trigger fails rather than passing trivially.\n51\t- `test_discard_then_draw_keeps_hand_size` — looting one card is net-zero on hand size, the pitched card is in the graveyard, and the drawn library card is in hand.\n52\t- `test_discard_card_goes_to_graveyard` — the discarded card lands in the controller's graveyard.\n53\t- `test_drawn_card_enters_hand` — the looted draw moves the top library card from library to hand.\n54\t- `test_declining_discard_draws_nothing` — \"you may\" / \"if you do\": declining (scripted `False`) means no discard and no draw, but the trigger still fires. Edge case: the conditional draw.\n55\t- `test_empty_hand_is_a_noop` — empty hand: the trigger fires but loots nothing and does not raise. Edge case: nothing to discard.\n56\t\n57\t## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered\n58\t- **Miracle \"cast when you drew it, first card this turn\" timing** — there is no\n59\t  engine surface for the miracle draw/reveal/alternative-cast window\n60\t  (`cards_drawn_this_turn` exists on the player but no miracle cast pipeline or\n61\t  draw-window hook). Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n62\t- **Flying combat restriction** (which creatures may block) — covered by the\n63\t  engine's own `_can_block` and the FDN reference tests; out of scope for a\n64\t  card whose flying is a plain evergreen keyword already asserted via the\n65\t  `keywords` flag.\n66\t- **Haste / summoning-sickness interaction** — haste is asserted as a keyword;\n67\t  the engine owns summoning-sickness resolution, so re-testing it here would be\n68\t  testing the engine rather than the card.\n69\t- **Legend rule** for the legendary supertype — engine state-based action, out\n70\t  of scope.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EsetUBrXacwixHmPHKwsvR","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"f293fe6a-b821-4804-9c1b-0611304354d3","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:38:27.828Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_201"}
