{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01FTBqfyx3Ndm4kd6PzgYXRN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014GFF5wJjQeFEvAadPVASdg","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation rationale — sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian)\n\n## Card: `cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py`\n`LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature)` — `{3}{R}{W}` 5/5 Legendary Elder Dragon with\n`Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.HASTE` (both already in the frozen 16-member enum, so\nno enum additions; respects KEY_DECISIONS).\n\n### Static miracle grant\nExposed as `get_miracle_cost(game, card) -> ManaCost | None` (one of the names the\ntest helper `_miracle_cost` probes). Returns `ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\")` only when\n`card` is an instant/sorcery AND is in *Lorehold's controller's* hand; otherwise\n`None`. Covers the type-restriction, controller-scoping, and zone-scoping edge\ncases the tests assert.\n\n### Opponent-upkeep loot trigger\n`register_triggers` registers exactly one `TriggerRegistration` watching\n`BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`. That event carries no player field and fires\nfor the active player's upkeep, so the \"each opponent's upkeep\" distinction lives\nin the `condition`: `game.active_player is not controller` (true on the\nopponent's upkeep, false on the controller's own — the test explicitly forbids an\nalways-fire `condition is None`). The effect (`_loot`) asks `choose_yes_no`\nfirst, then `choose_card` (matching the test scripts that `appendleft(pitch)` then\n`appendleft(True)`), discards the chosen card and draws one. It is a strict no-op\nwhen the player declines or has an empty hand, and never raises.\n\n## Dynamic miracle draw-window — BUILT (additive, engine_tests green)\nImplemented additively and verified end-to-end:\n\n### Engine capabilities added\n- `engine/casting.py`: `cast_spell_alternative(game, player, card, from_zone,\n  alternative_cost)` — mirrors `cast_spell_free` (legality, target choice,\n  `on_cast`, push StackObject, rollback on failure) but pays a caller-specified\n  `ManaCost` instead of the card's printed cost. This is the\n  \"cast it by paying [cost] rather than its mana cost\" path (rule 702.94a).\n- `engine/game_state.py`: a miracle-grant registry (`_miracle_grants`, empty by\n  default) with `register_miracle_grant(grant, *, source, controller)`,\n  `unregister_miracle_grant(source)`, and `fire_miracle_window(player, drawn)`.\n  `fire_miracle_window` is a strict no-op when the registry is empty; otherwise it\n  consults each grant `(game, player, drawn) -> ManaCost | None`, and for the\n  first one that returns a cost it offers the player (`choose_yes_no`) the option\n  to cast via `cast_spell_alternative`.\n- `engine/game.py` `draw_card`: after incrementing `cards_drawn_this_turn`, if\n  this is the FIRST card drawn this turn it calls `game.fire_miracle_window`. Only\n  the first draw of the turn qualifies (rule 702.94a); subsequent draws never fire\n  the window. Guarded with `getattr(... , None)`/`callable(...)` so it is a no-op\n  for any game/state lacking the hook.\n\n### Card wiring\n`register_miracle_window` registers a grant that returns `{2}` only when the\ndrawing player is Lorehold's controller, Lorehold is on the battlefield, and the\ndrawn card is an instant/sorcery. It is invoked from `register_triggers` (the\nmoment the permanent's abilities are wired up).\n\n### No-op safety\nThe whole window keys off the per-game `_miracle_grants` list, which is empty\nunless a card registers a grant. With no grant the window is bypassed entirely, so\nthe heavily-tested draw pipeline behaves exactly as before. Confirmed: full\n`pytest engine_tests/` (1168 tests) stays green, and an ad-hoc end-to-end check\nshowed the first instant/sorcery drawn under Lorehold is cast for {2} while a\nsecond same-turn draw stays in hand untouched.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` — 23 passed.\n- `pytest engine_tests/` — 1168 passed (pre-existing cleanup-discard warnings only).\n\n## UNVERIFIED\nNone. The static grant, loot trigger, and dynamic miracle draw-window were all\nbuilt and verified additively.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":186,"cache_read_input_tokens":80165,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":186,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":68,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EsetUBrXacwixHmPHKwsvR","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"e2a6ce93-d402-4590-8b1c-dd8a4f04f568","request_id":"req_011CbcKXYTuMLWvm275Jbdvr","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_201"}
