{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BFbLnCdUjhuGwSB9N3AUp3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation rationale — sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian)\n2\t\n3\t## Card: `cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py`\n4\t`LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature)` — `{3}{R}{W}` 5/5 Legendary Elder Dragon with\n5\t`Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.HASTE` (both already in the frozen 16-member enum, so\n6\tno enum additions; respects KEY_DECISIONS).\n7\t\n8\t### Static miracle grant\n9\tExposed as `get_miracle_cost(game, card) -> ManaCost | None` (one of the names the\n10\ttest helper `_miracle_cost` probes). Returns `ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\")` only when\n11\t`card` is an instant/sorcery AND is in *Lorehold's controller's* hand; otherwise\n12\t`None`. Covers the type-restriction, controller-scoping, and zone-scoping edge\n13\tcases the tests assert.\n14\t\n15\t### Opponent-upkeep loot trigger\n16\t`register_triggers` registers exactly one `TriggerRegistration` watching\n17\t`BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`. That event carries no player field and fires\n18\tfor the active player's upkeep, so the \"each opponent's upkeep\" distinction lives\n19\tin the `condition`: `game.active_player is not controller` (true on the\n20\topponent's upkeep, false on the controller's own — the test explicitly forbids an\n21\talways-fire `condition is None`). The effect (`_loot`) asks `choose_yes_no`\n22\tfirst, then `choose_card` (matching the test scripts that `appendleft(pitch)` then\n23\t`appendleft(True)`), discards the chosen card and draws one. It is a strict no-op\n24\twhen the player declines or has an empty hand, and never raises.\n25\t\n26\t## Dynamic miracle draw-window — BUILT (additive, engine_tests green)\n27\tImplemented additively and verified end-to-end:\n28\t\n29\t### Engine capabilities added\n30\t- `engine/casting.py`: `cast_spell_alternative(game, player, card, from_zone,\n31\t  alternative_cost)` — mirrors `cast_spell_free` (legality, target choice,\n32\t  `on_cast`, push StackObject, rollback on failure) but pays a caller-specified\n33\t  `ManaCost` instead of the card's printed cost. This is the\n34\t  \"cast it by paying [cost] rather than its mana cost\" path (rule 702.94a).\n35\t- `engine/game_state.py`: a miracle-grant registry (`_miracle_grants`, empty by\n36\t  default) with `register_miracle_grant(grant, *, source, controller)`,\n37\t  `unregister_miracle_grant(source)`, and `fire_miracle_window(player, drawn)`.\n38\t  `fire_miracle_window` is a strict no-op when the registry is empty; otherwise it\n39\t  consults each grant `(game, player, drawn) -> ManaCost | None`, and for the\n40\t  first one that returns a cost it offers the player (`choose_yes_no`) the option\n41\t  to cast via `cast_spell_alternative`.\n42\t- `engine/game.py` `draw_card`: after incrementing `cards_drawn_this_turn`, if\n43\t  this is the FIRST card drawn this turn it calls `game.fire_miracle_window`. Only\n44\t  the first draw of the turn qualifies (rule 702.94a); subsequent draws never fire\n45\t  the window. Guarded with `getattr(... , None)`/`callable(...)` so it is a no-op\n46\t  for any game/state lacking the hook.\n47\t\n48\t### Card wiring\n49\t`register_miracle_window` registers a grant that returns `{2}` only when the\n50\tdrawing player is Lorehold's controller, Lorehold is on the battlefield, and the\n51\tdrawn card is an instant/sorcery. It is invoked from `register_triggers` (the\n52\tmoment the permanent's abilities are wired up).\n53\t\n54\t### No-op safety\n55\tThe whole window keys off the per-game `_miracle_grants` list, which is empty\n56\tunless a card registers a grant. With no grant the window is bypassed entirely, so\n57\tthe heavily-tested draw pipeline behaves exactly as before. Confirmed: full\n58\t`pytest engine_tests/` (1168 tests) stays green, and an ad-hoc end-to-end check\n59\tshowed the first instant/sorcery drawn under Lorehold is cast for {2} while a\n60\tsecond same-turn draw stays in hand untouched.\n61\t\n62\t## Verification\n63\t- `pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` — 23 passed.\n64\t- `pytest engine_tests/` — 1168 passed (pre-existing cleanup-discard warnings only).\n65\t\n66\t## UNVERIFIED\n67\tNone. The static grant, loot trigger, and dynamic miracle draw-window were all\n68\tbuilt and verified additively.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0138E7VkeFj65rLGAvBcgNVS","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"3871cab8-1d8d-422e-bc80-814444e010a4","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:42:27.342Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend sos_201 tests for miracle"}
