{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XUXiEeD6qGRkXFkFQeandN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Run Decisions\n2\t\n3\tDecisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n4\t\n5\t## Untestable resolution: sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian)\n6\t- Testable/implemented: Flying, Haste, the STATIC miracle grant (queryable {2}\n7\t  miracle cost on controller's hand instants/sorceries), and the opponent-upkeep\n8\t  loot trigger.\n9\t- The DYNAMIC miracle clause (reveal the first card drawn this turn and cast it for\n10\t  the {2} miracle cost) needs a reveal-on-draw window hook + an alternative-cost cast\n11\t  entry. `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` and DrawsCardTriggeredEvent exist as partial\n12\t  surface.\n13\t- **Decision**: option (a) attempt to BUILD additively (mirroring sos_57/sos_97);\n14\t  UNVERIFIED fallback for any part that can't be done additively without regressing\n15\t  engine_tests/. Tester re-invoked once iff the miracle window lands.\n16\t\n17\t## Untestable resolution: sos_120 (Improvisation Capstone)\n18\t- Core (exile from top until a card with MV>=4 is found, free-cast it) is fully\n19\t  testable/implemented.\n20\t- The \"Paradigm\" mechanic (\"exile this spell; after you first resolve a spell with\n21\t  this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the\n22\t  beginning of each of your first main phases\") requires copy-from-exile machinery\n23\t  that does NOT exist (same gap marked UNVERIFIED for sos_13's copy-cast). \"Paradigm\"\n24\t  also can't be a Keyword (frozen 16-member enum).\n25\t- **Decision**: option (b) accept partial coverage. The recurring copy-cast clause is\n26\t  marked `# UNVERIFIED`. Implementer may add low-risk additive scaffolding (exile the\n27\t  spell after resolution, record first-resolution state) but must NOT build a fragile\n28\t  generic copy-from-exile system. No Tester re-invocation (no agreed observable contract).\n29\t\n30\t## Untestable resolution: sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer — planeswalker)\n31\t- Three of four abilities (Surveil 2, targeted discard, mv<=3 reanimation) fully\n32\t  testable/implemented.\n33\t- The -7 ultimate needs two ADDITIVE engine capabilities: (1) a deterministic\n34\t  coin-flip helper (scriptable via DeterministicPlayer) so X = heads is assertable,\n35\t  and (2) a per-player skipped-turns mechanism consulted by turn rotation.\n36\t- **Decision**: option (a) attempt to BUILD both additively (mirroring sos_57). If a\n37\t  part would regress engine_tests/ (esp. the turn loop) or need non-additive changes,\n38\t  fall back to (b) `# UNVERIFIED` for that part. Tester re-invoked once for whatever lands.\n39\t\n40\t## Untestable resolution: sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)\n41\t- Counter half (core) is fully testable/implemented.\n42\t- The Wizard-gated delayed \"{C} at the beginning of your next main phase = mana\n43\t  spent on the countered spell\" needs two ADDITIVE engine capabilities:\n44\t  (1) a beginning-of-main-phase triggered event in engine/events.py fired from the\n45\t  turn loop, and (2) recording total mana spent to cast a spell on the card/StackObject.\n46\t- **Decision**: option (a) attempt to BUILD it additively. Implementer instructed to\n47\t  add both capabilities additively; if any part would regress engine_tests/ or require\n48\t  non-additive engine changes, fall back to (b) `# UNVERIFIED` markers for that part\n49\t  and report. Tester re-invoked once IFF the engine support lands, to add {C}-bonus tests.\n50\t\n51\t## Untestable resolution: sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n52\t- **Item 1 — \"Prepared\" keyword as a first-class flag**: INITIALLY directed as (a)\n53\t  build it, but DOWNGRADED to (b) accept partial coverage. Adding `PREPARED` to\n54\t  `engine.types.Keyword` regresses the authoritative read-only engine test\n55\t  `engine_tests/test_types.py::TestKeyword::test_exactly_sixteen_members`\n56\t  (asserts `len(Keyword) == 16`). Since engine_tests/ is authoritative for grading\n57\t  and must not be modified, the keyword cannot be added without zeroing that test.\n58\t  Implementer correctly declined and marked it `# UNVERIFIED`. The prepared state is\n59\t  fully expressed via the `is_prepared` bool (tested). No Tester re-invocation.\n60\t- **Item 2 — \"cast a copy of its spell while prepared, unpreparing it\"**: resolved\n61\t  via (b) accept partial coverage. Requires major copy-cast/split-card engine\n62\t  machinery; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:` marker added in card_impl.py.\n63\t- **Item 3 — the \"Swords to Plowshares\" {W} instant face**: resolved via (b). The\n64\t  engine has no second-castable-face representation; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:`\n65\t  marker added in card_impl.py.\n66\t- The conditional prepared STATE is exposed as an `is_prepared` bool (tested).\n67\t\n68\t## Test dispute: sos_4\n69\t- **Disputed test**: `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player` (tests.py L180-198)\n70\t- **Tester's intent**: verify \"you gain X life\" goes to the controller, not the target player, while the chosen any-target takes damage.\n71\t- **Implementer's objection (feasibility)**: the test uses `chosen_targets=[p2, p1]`, naming p1 (controller) as the damage any-target (index 1), but asserts p2 (index 0) is damaged. This contradicts `test_two_colors_deals_two_damage_to_player` ([p1,p2] -> p2 damaged at index 1). No single index mapping satisfies both.\n72\t- **Decision**: accept implementer (feasibility objection — test data is internally contradictory). Convention is draw=chosen_targets[0], damage any-target=chosen_targets[1], life gain=controller.\n73\t- **Action**: re-invoke Tester to rewrite ONLY the disputed test, changing its data to `[p2, p2]` (draw target p2, damage any-target p2) so the intended \"life goes to controller p1\" check holds under the suite's index-1=damage convention.\n74\t\n75\t"}]},"parent