{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DFFfXec3M9Egn33Hf3TvX3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator directives — sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian)\n2\t\n3\t## Build (in scope, fully tested)\n4\t- The creature with Flying and Haste (and whatever other static keywords the spec\n5\t  lists), correct name/cost/P-T/colors/subtypes.\n6\t- The STATIC half of the miracle grant: \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand\n7\t  has miracle {2}.\" Expose a queryable miracle cost ({2}) on the controller's\n8\t  hand instants/sorceries per the test contract.\n9\t- The opponent-upkeep loot trigger (read spec for exact wording — e.g. \"At the\n10\t  beginning of each opponent's upkeep, ...\").\n11\tMake ALL current tests in `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` pass. Follow KEY_DECISIONS.md\n12\tconventions (no Keyword enum additions — frozen; get_targets()==[] while on stack;\n13\texisting infra: BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent, etc.).\n14\t\n15\t## Attempt to BUILD the DYNAMIC miracle cast (additive engine work)\n16\tOracle: \"(You may cast a card for its miracle cost when you draw it if it's the\n17\tfirst card you drew this turn.)\"\n18\t\n19\tAttempt this ADDITIVELY, reusing existing surface:\n20\t- There is already `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` tracking and a\n21\t  `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`. Add a reveal/miracle WINDOW hook fired when a player\n22\t  draws their FIRST card of the turn (consult `cards_drawn_this_turn`), that offers\n23\t  to cast that drawn card for its granted miracle cost ({2}).\n24\t- Add an alternative-cost cast path (e.g. extend the existing free/alternative cast\n25\t  helper in `engine/casting.py`, analogous to `cast_spell_free`, to support paying a\n26\t  specified alternative cost) that the miracle window routes through.\n27\t- Implement so that ONLY the first card drawn this turn qualifies, and only while\n28\t  Lorehold is on the battlefield (the grant is active).\n29\t\n30\t### HARD CONSTRAINT — additive only + green engine_tests/\n31\t- All engine changes ADDITIVE: new methods/attributes/branches; do NOT rename/move/\n32\t  delete existing engine symbols; do NOT add Keyword enum members; do NOT touch\n33\t  engine_tests/ or FDN tests.\n34\t- After ANY engine change run `pytest engine_tests/` — it MUST stay green. The draw\n35\t  pipeline is heavily tested; the new window must be a no-op when no miracle grant is\n36\t  active and must not change normal draw behavior.\n37\t- If the dynamic miracle window cannot be built additively without regressing\n38\t  engine_tests/ or non-additively, DO NOT force it: mark it\n39\t  `# UNVERIFIED: <requirement> — <reason>` in `cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` and\n40\t  report which parts you built vs. left UNVERIFIED.\n41\t\n42\tPrefer a green engine_tests/ suite and correct static behavior over miracle\n43\tcompleteness.\n44\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01PzUQHDyTL3F6xPfuQoCZ2o","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"37812332-a72e-4237-b35b-7cc2c5d2f7c5","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:46:47.631Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_201"}
