{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PzUQHDyTL3F6xPfuQoCZ2o","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review complete. I verified static card data (name, {3}{R}{W}, 5/5, Legendary, Elder Dragon, Flying+Haste, R/W colors), the static miracle grant scoping (instant/sorcery + controller's hand only), the opponent-upkeep loot trigger (condition keyed off `active_player is not controller`, discard-then-draw \"may\" with empty-hand no-op), the dynamic miracle window, and engine additivity.\n\nKey findings:\n- **Engine additivity (critical): PASS.** `cast_spell_alternative`, the `_miracle_grants` registry + `fire_miracle_window`, and the `draw_card` first-draw hook are all strictly additive — no existing engine symbol renamed/moved/deleted. The `draw_card` hook is a verified no-op when no grant is registered (`getattr(...)`/`callable(...)` guard + empty-registry early return in `fire_miracle_window`), fires only on `cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`, and cannot double-fire or alter draw counting. `cast_spell_alternative` mirrors `cast_spell_free` and does not touch the normal `cast_spell` path.\n- No strict issues. Three advisories: (1) `cards_drawn_this_turn` is never reset across turns in the engine (pre-existing limitation the coordinator directed reusing) so the dynamic miracle only works in unit tests, not in `run_game()`; (2) no unregister-on-leave, consistent with existing card convention and a safe no-op due to battlefield re-checks; (3) broad `except Exception` in `_loot`.\n\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 3\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/review.json"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aa05f69883ad5a897 (use SendMessage with to: 'aa05f69883ad5a897' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 56170\ntool_uses: 28\nduration_ms: 145202</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"6c59cc60-9dd8-4908-9db1-4e19923a0a6a","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:47:25.404Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Review the implementation diff for SOS card `sos_201` (Lorehold, the Historian — Flying/Haste creature granting miracle {2} to your hand instants/sorceries, plus an opponent-upkeep loot trigger). CARD_DIR = `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201`.\n\nDiff to review: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl.diff` (includes BOTH card and engine changes).\nCard spec for intent: `cards/sos/sos_201/card_spec.json`.\nImplementer's rationale: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-rationale.md`.\nContext: `FILES_MODIFIED.json`, `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n\nCoordinator-approved ADDITIVE engine changes (in scope): `engine.casting.cast_spell_alternative`, a per-game miracle-grant registry + `GameState.fire_miracle_window`, and a first-draw hook in `engine.game.draw_card`.\n\nReview focus:\n- Static correctness: Flying, Haste, P/T, name, cost, colors, subtypes; the static miracle {2} grant exposed only on the controller's hand instants/sorceries; the opponent-upkeep loot trigger (timing, who loots, what it does).\n- Dynamic miracle correctness: only the FIRST card drawn this turn qualifies; only instants/sorceries; only while the grant is active; casting uses the alternative {2} cost; \"you may\" (decline leaves card in hand).\n- ENGINE ADDITIVITY & REGRESSION RISK (CRITICAL): verify all engine changes are strictly additive (no existing symbol renamed/moved/deleted). The new first-draw hook in `draw_card` and the miracle-grant registry MUST be a NO-OP when no grant is registered, so normal draw behavior and the heavily-tested draw pipeline are unchanged. Flag STRICT if the hook could fire when no grant is active, alter draw counting, fire on non-first draws, double-fire, or otherwise change default draw/casting behavior. Also check `cast_spell_alternative` doesn't break normal casting.\n\nConstraints:\n- Do NOT flag conventions in KEY_DECISIONS.md.\n- Do NOT demand test rewrites — advisory only.\n- Only flag what's visible in the diff.\n\nOutput: write `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/review.json` as a JSON array of {\"severity\":\"strict\"|\"advisory\",\"file\",\"line\",\"comment\"}. \"strict\" only for correctness/spec/regression bugs that must be fixed. Empty [] if none.\n\nReturn: REVIEW_DONE with strict_count, advisory_count, review_path.","agentId":"aa05f69883ad5a897","agentType":"Reviewer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review complete. I verified static card data (name, {3}{R}{W}, 5/5, Legendary, Elder Dragon, Flying+Haste, R/W colors), the static miracle grant scoping (instant/sorcery + controller's hand only), the opponent-upkeep loot trigger (condition keyed off `active_player is not controller`, discard-then-draw \"may\" with empty-hand no-op), the dynamic miracle window, and engine additivity.\n\nKey findings:\n- **Engine additivity (critical): PASS.** `cast_spell_alternative`, the `_miracle_grants` registry + `fire_miracle_window`, and the `draw_card` first-draw hook are all strictly additive — no existing engine symbol renamed/moved/deleted. The `draw_card` hook is a verified no-op when no grant is registered (`getattr(...)`/`callable(...)` guard + empty-registry early return in `fire_miracle_window`), fires only on `cards_drawn_this_turn == 1`, and cannot double-fire or alter draw counting. `cast_spell_alternative` mirrors `cast_spell_free` and does not touch the normal `cast_spell` path.\n- No strict issues. Three advisories: (1) `cards_drawn_this_turn` is never reset across turns in the engine (pre-existing limitation the coordinator directed reusing) so the dynamic miracle only works in unit tests, not in `run_game()`; (2) no unregister-on-leave, consistent with existing card convention and a safe no-op due to battlefield re-checks; (3) broad `except Exception` in `_loot`.\n\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 3\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/review.json"}],"totalDurationMs":145202,"totalTokens":56170,"totalToolUseCount":28,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_