{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01RjGMQihTWfDgSHj9fv4QR8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019L22tiQhaA3zjwj2vjFpWB","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant)\n\n## Card summary\n\n`{2}{W}{B}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 4/4 (W/B). Keywords: Flying,\nVigilance. Static ability: \"Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has\ncasualty 1. (As you cast that spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power 1\nor greater. When you do, copy the spell and you may choose new targets for the\ncopy.)\"\n\n## File: `cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py`\n\n### TestSilverquillProperties — static data\nHard assertions for every printed characteristic in `card_spec.json`:\n- `test_is_creature` — is a `Creature`.\n- `test_name` — name is \"Silverquill, the Disputant\".\n- `test_mana_cost` — `{2}{W}{B}`.\n- `test_power_toughness` — base P/T 4/4.\n- `test_is_legendary` — `Supertype.LEGENDARY` present (Legendary Creature).\n- `test_is_elder_dragon` — subtypes include both \"Elder\" and \"Dragon\".\n- `test_has_flying` / `test_has_vigilance` — the two printed keywords.\n- `test_colors_are_white_and_black` — color identity W/B (from the spec `colors`).\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtyValue — casualty number\n- `test_casualty_value_is_one` — the granted ability is *casualty 1*, exposed as\n  `card.casualty_value == 1`. Casualty N would otherwise let you sacrifice for up\n  to N copies; this card is exactly 1.\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtyScope — which spells get casualty\n\"Each instant and sorcery spell **you** cast.\" Verified via a predicate\n`card.grants_casualty_to(game, spell)`:\n- `test_your_instant_qualifies` / `test_your_sorcery_qualifies` — your instant and\n  sorcery spells are granted casualty.\n- `test_your_creature_spell_does_not_qualify` — a creature spell is neither\n  instant nor sorcery, so it gets nothing.\n- `test_opponent_instant_does_not_qualify` — only spells *you* control qualify;\n  the opponent's instant does not. This is the \"you cast\" restriction.\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtySacrificeLegality — sacrifice constraint\n\"sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater.\" Verified via\n`card.is_valid_casualty_sacrifice(creature)`:\n- `test_power_two_creature_is_legal_sacrifice` — power 2 is legal.\n- `test_power_one_creature_is_legal_sacrifice` — boundary: power exactly 1 is legal.\n- `test_power_zero_creature_is_not_legal_sacrifice` — boundary: power 0 (e.g. a\n  Wall) is not.\n- `test_noncreature_is_not_legal_sacrifice` — the cost requires a *creature*; an\n  enchantment is rejected.\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtyResolution — sacrifice + copy\n\"When you do, copy the spell and you may choose new targets for the copy.\"\nVerified via `card.apply_casualty(game, spell_stack_object, sacrifice, new_targets=None)`:\n- `test_sacrifice_moves_creature_to_graveyard` — paying casualty sacrifices the\n  chosen creature (battlefield → graveyard).\n- `test_copy_is_added_to_the_stack` — casualty 1 puts exactly one copy on the\n  stack (stack length grows by 1).\n- `test_copy_is_a_distinct_object_from_original` — the copy is a separate\n  `StackObject` with its own source object (not the same instance), but\n  reproduces the same spell by name.\n- `test_copy_can_choose_new_targets` — when `new_targets` is supplied, the copy\n  carries the new targets instead of the original's.\n- `test_copy_controlled_by_caster` — the copy is controlled by the spell's\n  controller (you).\n\n## Edge cases covered and why\n- Casualty sacrifice power boundary (0 / 1 / 2) — the \"power 1 or greater\"\n  threshold is the only numeric constraint in the cost.\n- \"you cast\" restriction (opponent's spell excluded) — a common scoping bug.\n- Spell-type restriction (creature spell excluded) — casualty only applies to\n  instants/sorceries.\n- New-target selection on the copy — the explicit \"you may choose new targets\"\n  clause.\n- Copy identity/independence from the original stack object.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered\n- **Full \"as you cast\" pipeline integration** — the base casting pipeline\n  (`engine/casting.py`) has no casualty hook (no \"additional cost as you cast\"\n  surface). Whether casualty is actually *offered* during `cast_spell` cannot be\n  driven through the engine's public cast path, so this is recorded in\n  `untestable.json` rather than asserted. The card-local helpers above cover the\n  observable mechanics the implementation can deliver.\n- **Casualty optionality (\"you may\")** as a player-choice prompt during a real\n  cast — same reason; there is no casting-pipeline choice point to script. The\n  helper-driven tests treat the sacrifice/copy as the action taken when the\n  player opts in.\n- Legend rule, combat behavior of Flying/Vigilance (engine-owned and covered by\n  `engine_tests/` / FDN references — out of scope for this card's unique text).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1394,"cache_read_input_tokens":74545,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1394,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015YjqSJ8qf6KKiKFJ4NXToW","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"a4f53bb6-0c91-41d0-8d43-4c2dd0be918c","request_id":"req_011CbcLCvTa768DGyoN3jsrX","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_226"}
