{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WyaQ5wnmRoXJghz6kJdLhE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"requirement\": \"As you cast that spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater (casualty offered as an additional cost during the actual cast).\",\n4\t    \"reason\": \"The base casting pipeline (engine/casting.py cast_spell / cast_spell_alternative) has no 'additional cost as you cast' / casualty hook, and there is no choice point in the cast path to script the 'you may' decision. The casualty mechanic can only be modeled and tested via a card-local helper (apply_casualty / grants_casualty_to / is_valid_casualty_sacrifice), not through a real engine-driven cast.\",\n5\t    \"what_would_unblock\": \"An additive casting-pipeline hook (e.g. card.additional_cast_costs(game) or an as-you-cast callback invoked from cast_spell) plus a scriptable player choice for the optional sacrifice, so a test could cast a real instant/sorcery while Silverquill is on the battlefield and observe casualty being offered and applied.\"\n6\t  }\n7\t]\n8\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XTP7k3qVx6bF6TgihrKkLV","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"f90d9bb7-c90e-4378-9cf2-7ba5bceee60f","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:51:55.359Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_226"}
