{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CNXFYdD5BC1njgDEUAiMfk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale — sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant)\n2\t\n3\t## Card summary\n4\t\n5\t`{2}{W}{B}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 4/4 (W/B). Keywords: Flying,\n6\tVigilance. Static ability: \"Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has\n7\tcasualty 1. (As you cast that spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power 1\n8\tor greater. When you do, copy the spell and you may choose new targets for the\n9\tcopy.)\"\n10\t\n11\t## File: `cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py`\n12\t\n13\t### TestSilverquillProperties — static data\n14\tHard assertions for every printed characteristic in `card_spec.json`:\n15\t- `test_is_creature` — is a `Creature`.\n16\t- `test_name` — name is \"Silverquill, the Disputant\".\n17\t- `test_mana_cost` — `{2}{W}{B}`.\n18\t- `test_power_toughness` — base P/T 4/4.\n19\t- `test_is_legendary` — `Supertype.LEGENDARY` present (Legendary Creature).\n20\t- `test_is_elder_dragon` — subtypes include both \"Elder\" and \"Dragon\".\n21\t- `test_has_flying` / `test_has_vigilance` — the two printed keywords.\n22\t- `test_colors_are_white_and_black` — color identity W/B (from the spec `colors`).\n23\t\n24\t### TestSilverquillCasualtyValue — casualty number\n25\t- `test_casualty_value_is_one` — the granted ability is *casualty 1*, exposed as\n26\t  `card.casualty_value == 1`. Casualty N would otherwise let you sacrifice for up\n27\t  to N copies; this card is exactly 1.\n28\t\n29\t### TestSilverquillCasualtyScope — which spells get casualty\n30\t\"Each instant and sorcery spell **you** cast.\" Verified via a predicate\n31\t`card.grants_casualty_to(game, spell)`:\n32\t- `test_your_instant_qualifies` / `test_your_sorcery_qualifies` — your instant and\n33\t  sorcery spells are granted casualty.\n34\t- `test_your_creature_spell_does_not_qualify` — a creature spell is neither\n35\t  instant nor sorcery, so it gets nothing.\n36\t- `test_opponent_instant_does_not_qualify` — only spells *you* control qualify;\n37\t  the opponent's instant does not. This is the \"you cast\" restriction.\n38\t\n39\t### TestSilverquillCasualtySacrificeLegality — sacrifice constraint\n40\t\"sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater.\" Verified via\n41\t`card.is_valid_casualty_sacrifice(creature)`:\n42\t- `test_power_two_creature_is_legal_sacrifice` — power 2 is legal.\n43\t- `test_power_one_creature_is_legal_sacrifice` — boundary: power exactly 1 is legal.\n44\t- `test_power_zero_creature_is_not_legal_sacrifice` — boundary: power 0 (e.g. a\n45\t  Wall) is not.\n46\t- `test_noncreature_is_not_legal_sacrifice` — the cost requires a *creature*; an\n47\t  enchantment is rejected.\n48\t\n49\t### TestSilverquillCasualtyResolution — sacrifice + copy\n50\t\"When you do, copy the spell and you may choose new targets for the copy.\"\n51\tVerified via `card.apply_casualty(game, spell_stack_object, sacrifice, new_targets=None)`:\n52\t- `test_sacrifice_moves_creature_to_graveyard` — paying casualty sacrifices the\n53\t  chosen creature (battlefield → graveyard).\n54\t- `test_copy_is_added_to_the_stack` — casualty 1 puts exactly one copy on the\n55\t  stack (stack length grows by 1).\n56\t- `test_copy_is_a_distinct_object_from_original` — the copy is a separate\n57\t  `StackObject` with its own source object (not the same instance), but\n58\t  reproduces the same spell by name.\n59\t- `test_copy_can_choose_new_targets` — when `new_targets` is supplied, the copy\n60\t  carries the new targets instead of the original's.\n61\t- `test_copy_controlled_by_caster` — the copy is controlled by the spell's\n62\t  controller (you).\n63\t\n64\t## Edge cases covered and why\n65\t- Casualty sacrifice power boundary (0 / 1 / 2) — the \"power 1 or greater\"\n66\t  threshold is the only numeric constraint in the cost.\n67\t- \"you cast\" restriction (opponent's spell excluded) — a common scoping bug.\n68\t- Spell-type restriction (creature spell excluded) — casualty only applies to\n69\t  instants/sorceries.\n70\t- New-target selection on the copy — the explicit \"you may choose new targets\"\n71\t  clause.\n72\t- Copy identity/independence from the original stack object.\n73\t\n74\t## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered\n75\t- **Full \"as you cast\" pipeline integration** — the base casting pipeline\n76\t  (`engine/casting.py`) has no casualty hook (no \"additional cost as you cast\"\n77\t  surface). Whether casualty is actually *offered* during `cast_spell` cannot be\n78\t  driven through the engine's public cast path, so this is recorded in\n79\t  `untestable.json` rather than asserted. The card-local helpers above cover the\n80\t  observable mechanics the implementation can deliver.\n81\t- **Casualty optionality (\"you may\")** as a player-choice prompt during a real\n82\t  cast — same reason; there is no casting-pipeline choice point to script. The\n83\t  helper-driven tests treat the sacrifice/copy as the action taken when the\n84\t  player opts in.\n85\t- Legend rule, combat behavior of Flying/Vigilance (engine-owned and covered by\n86\t  `engine_tests/` / FDN references — out of scope for this card's unique text).\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XTP7k3qVx6bF6TgihrKkLV","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"0bf067d5-e5a5-4e3d-9df0-b90655afd808","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:51:55.853Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_226"}
