{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ny6LCHd4mSXYTCdzDeUALc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Card implementation for Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares (SOS 13).\n2\t\n3\tThis is a split / modal card. Per the coordinator directives, only the\n4\tcreature face (``Emeritus of Truce``) is built fully here. The casting of a\n5\tcopy of the spell while prepared, and the ``Swords to Plowshares`` instant\n6\tface, are recorded as ``# UNVERIFIED`` because the current engine has no\n7\tcopy-cast / second-castable-face machinery.\n8\t\"\"\"\n9\t\n10\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n11\t\n12\tfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\n13\t\n14\tfrom engine.card import Creature\n15\tfrom engine.types import CardType, Color, Keyword, ManaCost, Zone\n16\t\n17\tif TYPE_CHECKING:\n18\t    from engine.game_state import GameState\n19\t\n20\t\n21\tdef _is_creature(obj: Any) -> bool:\n22\t    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *obj* is a creature permanent.\"\"\"\n23\t    return CardType.CREATURE in getattr(obj, \"card_types\", set())\n24\t\n25\t\n26\tclass EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature):\n27\t    \"\"\"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares — creature face.\n28\t\n29\t    Emeritus of Truce — {1}{W}{W} — 3/3 — Creature — Cat Cleric (white).\n30\t\n31\t    When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white and black\n32\t    Inkling creature token with flying. Then if an opponent controls more\n33\t    creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared.\n34\t\n35\t    SOS collector number 13.\n36\t    \"\"\"\n37\t\n38\t    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n39\t        kwargs.setdefault(\"name\", \"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\")\n40\t        kwargs.setdefault(\"mana_cost\", ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{W}{W}\"))\n41\t        kwargs.setdefault(\"subtypes\", {\"Cat\", \"Cleric\"})\n42\t        # UNVERIFIED: A first-class Keyword.PREPARED member cannot be added —\n43\t        #   the read-only engine test engine_tests/test_types.py asserts the\n44\t        #   Keyword Flag enum has exactly 16 members, so adding PREPARED\n45\t        #   regresses it. The directive's own verify gate requires\n46\t        #   ``pytest engine_tests/`` to keep passing, which takes precedence.\n47\t        #   The prepared state is therefore exposed only via the runtime\n48\t        #   ``is_prepared`` bool (set by the conditional ETB clause below).\n49\t        kwargs.setdefault(\"keywords\", Keyword(0))\n50\t        kwargs.setdefault(\"base_power\", 3)\n51\t        kwargs.setdefault(\"base_toughness\", 3)\n52\t        kwargs.setdefault(\n53\t            \"rules_text\",\n54\t            \"When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white and \"\n55\t            \"black Inkling creature token with flying. Then if an opponent \"\n56\t            \"controls more creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared. \"\n57\t            \"(While it's prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell. Doing so \"\n58\t            \"unprepares it.)\",\n59\t        )\n60\t        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n61\t        # The creature face is mono-white.\n62\t        self.colors: set[Color] = {Color.WHITE}\n63\t        # Runtime \"becomes prepared\" state (the conditional ETB result).\n64\t        self.is_prepared: bool = False\n65\t        # Targets are chosen for the ETB triggered ability, not the spell.\n66\t        self.chosen_targets: list[Any] = []\n67\t\n68\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n69\t    # Targeting\n70\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n71\t\n72\t    def _is_being_cast(self, game: \"GameState\") -> bool:\n73\t        \"\"\"Return ``True`` while this card sits in any STACK zone.\n74\t\n75\t        The \"target player\" belongs to the enters-the-battlefield triggered"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XTP7k3qVx6bF6TgihrKkLV","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"8520dd38-d71d-49fb-b18d-f4c0082c5341","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:52:21.120Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_226"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"adfd7c2683d032aff","tool_use_id":"toolu_01XTP7k3qVx6bF6TgihrKkLV","description":"Writing cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py","subagent_type":"Implementer","usage":{"total_tokens":41890,"tool_uses":17,"duration_ms":55756},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"e1bed81a-5a68-4bf0-938e-62677fadfec8","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_015MeHUvwk6oNhTC2p4zF6PS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HBshHrWyrb9XNoikViSsp5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py","content":"\"\"\"Card implementation for Silverquill, the Disputant (SOS 226).\n\n{2}{W}{B} Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 4/4 (white & black) with Flying\nand Vigilance.\n\nStatic ability: \"Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1. (As\nyou cast that spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater. When\nyou do, copy the spell and you may choose new targets for the copy.)\"\n\nThe creature itself (static data, Flying/Vigilance) and the casualty-granting\nability are modeled as card-local helpers the casting machinery (or a test) can\ndrive:\n\n    * ``casualty_value``                            — the granted casualty number (1)\n    * ``grants_casualty_to(game, spell)``           — predicate: your instant/sorcery\n    * ``is_valid_casualty_sacrifice(creature)``     — power >= 1 creature\n    * ``apply_casualty(game, stack_obj, sac, ...)`` — sacrifice + copy the spell\n\nThe deep \"as you cast that spell\" REAL casting-pipeline integration has no\nexisting engine hook; see ``# UNVERIFIED`` note below and ``untestable.json``.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\n\nfrom engine import game as game_module\nfrom engine.card import Creature\nfrom engine.stack import StackObject, copy_spell\nfrom engine.types import CardType, Color, Keyword, ManaCost, Supertype\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from engine.game_state import GameState\n\n\ndef _is_creature(obj: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *obj* is a creature permanent/card.\"\"\"\n    return CardType.CREATURE in getattr(obj, \"card_types\", set())\n\n\ndef _is_instant_or_sorcery(obj: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *obj* is an instant or sorcery spell.\"\"\"\n    types = getattr(obj, \"card_types\", set())\n    return CardType.INSTANT in types or CardType.SORCERY in types\n\n\nclass SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature):\n    \"\"\"Silverquill, the Disputant — {2}{W}{B} Elder Dragon, 4/4.\"\"\"\n\n    #: The granted ability is *casualty 1* (sacrifice one creature, one copy).\n    casualty_value: int = 1\n\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"name\", \"Silverquill, the Disputant\")\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"mana_cost\", ManaCost.parse(\"{2}{W}{B}\"))\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"subtypes\", {\"Elder\", \"Dragon\"})\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"supertypes\", {Supertype.LEGENDARY})\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"keywords\", Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.VIGILANCE)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"base_power\", 4)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\"base_toughness\", 4)\n        kwargs.setdefault(\n            \"rules_text\",\n            \"Flying, vigilance\\n\"\n            \"Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1. (As you \"\n            \"cast that spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power 1 or \"\n            \"greater. When you do, copy the spell and you may choose new \"\n            \"targets for the copy.)\",\n        )\n        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n        self.colors: set[Color] = {Color.WHITE, Color.BLACK}\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Casualty grant — which spells qualify\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def grants_casualty_to(self, game: \"GameState\", spell: Any) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *spell* is one of your instant/sorcery spells.\n\n        \"Each instant and sorcery spell **you** cast has casualty 1.\" Only the\n        Silverquill controller's instant and sorcery spells qualify; creature\n        spells and opponents' spells do not.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not _is_instant_or_sorcery(spell):\n            return False\n        return getattr(spell, \"controller\", None) is self.controller\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Casualty sacrifice legality\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def is_valid_casualty_sacrifice(self, creature: Any) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *creature* may be sacrificed for casualty.\n\n        The casualty cost is \"sacrifice a creature with power 1 or greater.\"\n        \"\"\"\n        if not _is_creature(creature):\n            return False\n        power = getattr(creature, \"power\", None)\n        if power is None:\n            power = getattr(creature, \"base_power\", 0)\n        return power >= 1\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Applying casualty — sacrifice + copy the spell\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def apply_casualty(\n        self,\n        game: \"GameState\",\n        spell_stack_object: StackObject,\n        sacrifice_creature: Any,\n        new_targets: list[Any] | None = None,\n    ) -> StackObject:\n        \"\"\"Pay casualty: sacrifice *sacrifice_creature* and copy the spell.\n\n        Sacrifices the chosen creature, then places exactly one copy of the\n        spell on the stack controlled by the spell's controller (you), carrying\n        *new_targets* when supplied (else the original's targets).\n\n        Returns the copy's :class:`StackObject` (now on top of the stack).\n        \"\"\"\n        controller = spell_stack_object.controller\n        sac_controller = getattr(sacrifice_creature, \"controller\", controller)\n        game_module.sacrifice(game, sac_controller, sacrifice_creature)\n\n        copy_obj = copy_spell(\n            game,\n            spell_stack_object,\n            controller,\n            new_targets=new_targets,\n        )\n        game.stack.push(copy_obj)\n        return copy_obj\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # As-you-cast pipeline integration\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # UNVERIFIED: \"As you cast that spell, you may sacrifice a creature with\n    #   power 1 or greater\" — the base casting pipeline (engine/casting.py\n    #   cast_spell / cast_spell_alternative) exposes no \"additional cost as you\n    #   cast\" / casualty hook, and there is no scriptable choice point to drive\n    #   the optional \"you may\" sacrifice during a real engine-driven cast.\n    #   Adding such a hook would touch the heavily-tested cast path with no\n    #   no-op-by-default surface available, so the cast pipeline is left\n    #   untouched. The card-local helpers above (grants_casualty_to /\n    #   is_valid_casualty_sacrifice / apply_casualty) fully model and test the\n    #   observable casualty mechanic. See untestable.json.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1543,"cache_read_input_tokens":40261,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1543,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XTP7k3qVx6bF6TgihrKkLV","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"f0018f32-98f5-4ceb-a6a7-6edfe0cee103","request_id":"req_011CbcLNL7ciGXXboa4EVh3a","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_226"}
