{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014ZkUvYWWxVMPLe5XC7Aa6z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DXW6dRc6Ra1khYTG55tvLk","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation rationale — sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant)\n\n## Approach\n`SilverquillTheDisputant` subclasses `engine.card.Creature`. Static data is set\nvia `kwargs.setdefault` in `__init__`:\n- name `Silverquill, the Disputant`, cost `{2}{W}{B}`, 4/4\n- subtypes `{\"Elder\", \"Dragon\"}`, supertype `LEGENDARY`\n- keywords `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.VIGILANCE` (both already exist in the\n  frozen Keyword enum — no enum members added)\n- `self.colors = {Color.WHITE, Color.BLACK}` (no engine `colors` property\n  exists; cards set `.colors` directly, matching sos_13's convention)\n\nThe casualty grant is modeled with the card-local helper contract the tests\nassert:\n- `casualty_value = 1` (class attribute)\n- `grants_casualty_to(game, spell)` — true only for instant/sorcery spells\n  whose `controller is self.controller` (the \"you cast\" restriction; creature\n  spells and opponent spells excluded)\n- `is_valid_casualty_sacrifice(creature)` — must be a creature (by\n  `card_types`) with power >= 1; non-creatures (e.g. Enchantment) and power-0\n  creatures rejected. Reads `power` (falls back to `base_power`).\n- `apply_casualty(game, stack_obj, sac, new_targets=None)` — sacrifices the\n  creature via `engine.game.sacrifice` (using the creature's own controller),\n  then builds one copy via `engine.stack.copy_spell` controlled by the spell's\n  controller, pushes it on the stack, and returns it. `copy_spell` already\n  produces a distinct StackObject with a shallow-copied source (same name,\n  different instance) and honors `new_targets`.\n\n## Engine changes\nNone. No engine files were modified; `pytest engine_tests/` stays green\n(1145 passed).\n\n## UNVERIFIED parts\n- The REAL \"as you cast that spell\" casting-pipeline integration is left\n  UNVERIFIED (grep-able `# UNVERIFIED` comment in `card_impl.py`). The base\n  `engine/casting.py` cast pipeline has no additional-cost / casualty hook and\n  no scriptable choice point for the optional \"you may\" sacrifice. Per the\n  coordinator directive, I did NOT force a hook into the heavily-tested cast\n  path because no clean no-op-by-default surface exists there. The card-local\n  helpers fully model and test the observable casualty mechanic. The as-you-cast\n  hook was therefore NOT built (left UNVERIFIED), and the cast pipeline is\n  untouched.\n\n## Conventions for future cards\n- Casualty N can be modeled with the same four card-local helpers; reuse\n  `engine.stack.copy_spell` + `engine.game.sacrifice` for the sacrifice+copy.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":208,"cache_read_input_tokens":45302,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":208,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":62,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XTP7k3qVx6bF6TgihrKkLV","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"92b47ffe-ec41-4711-b3b5-a6a6b7e96353","request_id":"req_011CbcLRhKAEZQFkah2fhVBt","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_226"}
