{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ApS1wvEhpqGfTkFV4BDfaV","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator directives — sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant)\n2\t\n3\t## Build (in scope, fully tested)\n4\t- The creature: W/B 4/4 Flying + Vigilance Elder Dragon (read card_spec.json for\n5\t  exact name/cost/P-T/subtypes/colors). Static data correct.\n6\t- The casualty 1 grant modeled via the card-local helper contract the tests assert:\n7\t  - `card.casualty_value == 1`\n8\t  - `card.grants_casualty_to(game, spell) -> bool` (your instants/sorceries only)\n9\t  - `card.is_valid_casualty_sacrifice(creature) -> bool` (creature with power >= 1)\n10\t  - `card.apply_casualty(game, spell_stack_object, sacrifice_creature, new_targets=None)`\n11\t    — sacrifices the creature and pushes ONE copy of the spell on the stack,\n12\t    controlled by the caster, carrying new targets when supplied.\n13\t  Use `engine.stack.copy_spell` and `engine.game.sacrifice` to build `apply_casualty`.\n14\tMake ALL current tests in `cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py` pass. Follow KEY_DECISIONS.md\n15\tconventions (no Keyword enum additions; get_targets()==[] while on stack).\n16\t\n17\t## \"As you cast\" pipeline integration — attempt LOW-RISK only, else UNVERIFIED\n18\tThe full casualty mechanic is \"as you cast that spell, you may sacrifice a creature\n19\twith power 1+; if you do, copy the spell and may choose new targets for the copy.\"\n20\tWiring this into the REAL cast pipeline has no existing hook.\n21\t\n22\t- You MAY add a LOW-RISK, no-op-by-default additive hook (e.g.\n23\t  `card.additional_cast_costs(game)` consulted from `engine/casting.py cast_spell`,\n24\t  or an as-you-cast callback) ONLY IF it is clean and strictly no-op when no card\n25\t  grants casualty, so the heavily-tested cast pipeline is unaffected.\n26\t- If that hook risks regressing `engine_tests/` or requires non-additive changes to\n27\t  the cast path, DO NOT force it. Leave the cast pipeline untouched and mark the\n28\t  integration `# UNVERIFIED: <requirement> — <reason>` in\n29\t  `cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py`. The card-local `apply_casualty` helper already\n30\t  fully models the behavior for testing.\n31\t\n32\t## Constraints\n33\t- Make ALL tests pass; do NOT modify tests.\n34\t- Engine changes ADDITIVE only; after ANY engine change run `pytest engine_tests/`\n35\t  and keep it green. Do NOT add Keyword enum members. Do NOT touch engine_tests/ or\n36\t  FDN tests. Clean up any temp files (no FILES_MODIFIED.json.tmp left behind).\n37\t- Prefer a green engine_tests/ suite and correct helper behavior over pipeline\n38\t  completeness.\n39\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01USrUVvHtiAz1mgWrVoRyxW","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"cabc1807-2824-4f52-b2d9-3ae08c3cbec6","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:54:27.132Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_226"}
