{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cyos74z7zq5PJGQ3i3agMS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation rationale — sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant)\n2\t\n3\t## Approach\n4\t`SilverquillTheDisputant` subclasses `engine.card.Creature`. Static data is set\n5\tvia `kwargs.setdefault` in `__init__`:\n6\t- name `Silverquill, the Disputant`, cost `{2}{W}{B}`, 4/4\n7\t- subtypes `{\"Elder\", \"Dragon\"}`, supertype `LEGENDARY`\n8\t- keywords `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.VIGILANCE` (both already exist in the\n9\t  frozen Keyword enum — no enum members added)\n10\t- `self.colors = {Color.WHITE, Color.BLACK}` (no engine `colors` property\n11\t  exists; cards set `.colors` directly, matching sos_13's convention)\n12\t\n13\tThe casualty grant is modeled with the card-local helper contract the tests\n14\tassert:\n15\t- `casualty_value = 1` (class attribute)\n16\t- `grants_casualty_to(game, spell)` — true only for instant/sorcery spells\n17\t  whose `controller is self.controller` (the \"you cast\" restriction; creature\n18\t  spells and opponent spells excluded)\n19\t- `is_valid_casualty_sacrifice(creature)` — must be a creature (by\n20\t  `card_types`) with power >= 1; non-creatures (e.g. Enchantment) and power-0\n21\t  creatures rejected. Reads `power` (falls back to `base_power`).\n22\t- `apply_casualty(game, stack_obj, sac, new_targets=None)` — sacrifices the\n23\t  creature via `engine.game.sacrifice` (using the creature's own controller),\n24\t  then builds one copy via `engine.stack.copy_spell` controlled by the spell's\n25\t  controller, pushes it on the stack, and returns it. `copy_spell` already\n26\t  produces a distinct StackObject with a shallow-copied source (same name,\n27\t  different instance) and honors `new_targets`.\n28\t\n29\t## Engine changes\n30\tNone. No engine files were modified; `pytest engine_tests/` stays green\n31\t(1145 passed).\n32\t\n33\t## UNVERIFIED parts\n34\t- The REAL \"as you cast that spell\" casting-pipeline integration is left\n35\t  UNVERIFIED (grep-able `# UNVERIFIED` comment in `card_impl.py`). The base\n36\t  `engine/casting.py` cast pipeline has no additional-cost / casualty hook and\n37\t  no scriptable choice point for the optional \"you may\" sacrifice. Per the\n38\t  coordinator directive, I did NOT force a hook into the heavily-tested cast\n39\t  path because no clean no-op-by-default surface exists there. The card-local\n40\t  helpers fully model and test the observable casualty mechanic. The as-you-cast\n41\t  hook was therefore NOT built (left UNVERIFIED), and the cast pipeline is\n42\t  untouched.\n43\t\n44\t## Conventions for future cards\n45\t- Casualty N can be modeled with the same four card-local helpers; reuse\n46\t  `engine.stack.copy_spell` + `engine.game.sacrifice` for the sacrifice+copy.\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01USrUVvHtiAz1mgWrVoRyxW","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"4b2d289c-dba7-44ca-af81-e92a131f2ea9","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:54:27.651Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_226"}
