{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01JjFbayPvRSxvHsN1NL3YJU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SnBzyucBhhSJAyfTAuv57T","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — SOS 245 Witherbloom, the Balancer\n\nCard: `{6}{B}{G}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5.\nOracle text:\n- Affinity for creatures (costs {1} less to cast for each creature you control).\n- Flying, deathtouch.\n- Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\n\nTest file: `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`\n\n## TestWitherbloomProperties\nLocks the printed characteristics against the spec:\n- `test_is_creature` — is a `Creature` and has `CardType.CREATURE`.\n- `test_name` — name matches `\"Witherbloom, the Balancer\"`.\n- `test_mana_cost` — equals `ManaCost.parse(\"{6}{B}{G}\")`.\n- `test_power_toughness` — base 5/5.\n- `test_is_legendary` — `Supertype.LEGENDARY` present (type line is Legendary).\n- `test_is_elder_dragon` — subtypes include `\"Dragon\"` and `\"Elder\"`.\n\n## TestWitherbloomKeywords\n- `test_has_flying` / `test_has_deathtouch` — the two printed evergreen keywords.\n- `test_does_not_have_unrelated_keyword` — guards against accidentally OR-ing\n  in a keyword the card does not have (uses TRAMPLE as a negative control).\n\n## TestWitherbloomAffinity\nValidates the \"Affinity for creatures\" cost-reduction hook\n(`cost_reduction(game)`), which the engine only applies to the generic portion.\n- `test_no_creatures_no_reduction` — zero creatures → reduction 0.\n- `test_reduction_equals_creature_count` — three creatures → raw reduction 3.\n- `test_self_counts_when_on_battlefield_does_not_inflate` — two creatures → 2.\n- `test_only_counts_creatures` — artifacts/enchantments on the battlefield do\n  not contribute (affinity is specifically *for creatures*).\n- `test_only_counts_your_creatures` — opponent creatures do not reduce the cost\n  (\"creatures *you* control\").\n- `test_reduction_clamped_to_generic_via_pipeline` — with 9 creatures the raw\n  value is 9 but `get_cost_reduction` clamps it to the `{6}` generic, since the\n  `{B}{G}` pips are never reducible.\n\n## TestWitherbloomCastingWithAffinity\nEnd-to-end exercise through `engine.casting.cast_spell`:\n- `test_cast_with_three_creatures_pays_reduced_generic` — `{6}{B}{G}` with three\n  creatures becomes payable with `{3}{B}{G}`; the spell reaches the stack.\n- `test_cast_without_enough_mana_for_reduced_cost_fails` — one creature only\n  reduces by 1, so `{3}{B}{G}` worth of mana is insufficient → `CastingError`.\n- `test_colored_pips_never_reduced` — even with 8 creatures and 10 colorless\n  mana, the cast fails without black/green for the pips (affinity reduces only\n  generic mana).\n\n## TestWitherbloomFlying\nFlying's blocking restriction via `engine.combat._can_block` (same pattern as\nthe FDN 142 reference test):\n- `test_ground_creature_cannot_block` — keyword-less creature cannot block it.\n- `test_flying_blocker_can_block` — flyer can.\n- `test_reach_blocker_can_block` — reach creature can.\n\n## TestWitherbloomDeathtouch\nDeathtouch's lethal-damage rule via `engine.combat._get_lethal_damage`:\n- `test_one_damage_is_lethal_against_high_toughness` — with Witherbloom as the\n  attacker, 1 damage is lethal to a 10-toughness blocker.\n- `test_without_deathtouch_lethal_is_toughness` — control: a vanilla attacker\n  needs the full toughness, proving the deathtouch test is meaningful.\n\n## TestWitherbloomGrantsAffinity\n\"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\" The engine\nhas no central cost-reduction registry (see FDN 159 Mocking Sprite, whose\nanalogous \"cost {1} less\" clause is modeled only as a marker). These cover the\nobservable surface:\n- `test_register_triggers_does_not_raise` — wiring up the granted-affinity\n  machinery must not raise.\n- `test_card_advertises_no_spell_targets` — Witherbloom's abilities are all\n  static, so `get_targets` must be empty and casting it must not demand a target\n  (per KEY_DECISIONS: card-level `get_targets` is only for the spell itself).\n\n## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered\n- The actual cost reduction applied to *other* instant/sorcery spells the\n  controller casts. There is no central cost-reduction registry the casting\n  pipeline consults for granted affinity from another permanent — only a card's\n  own `cost_reduction()` hook is honored. Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n- Legend rule / two copies in play — engine-level SBA behavior, out of scope for\n  this card's own contract (covered by `engine_tests/`).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1320,"cache_read_input_tokens":74568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1320,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01A6VsMQ2xj7apqrjfRAgmGM","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"2c633a3c-e9bb-4cb2-a346-9cc6a69f2ea6","request_id":"req_011CbcLkHcugobVwkjXSHBzf","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_245"}
