{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01HEckoPyDbC2LWd68jthpUw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fks4m8HJodsELTPpX4rEAy","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md","old_string":"## Untestable resolution: sos_226","new_string":"## Untestable resolution: sos_245 (Witherbloom, the Balancer)\n- Testable/implemented: flying/deathtouch creature + own static data + its own\n  affinity cost reduction.\n- Untestable: \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures\" —\n  grants the controller's OTHER instant/sorcery spells a {1}-less-per-creature\n  reduction. The cast pipeline only consults a spell's OWN cost_reduction() hook;\n  no external registry exists (FDN 159 left the analogous clause inert).\n- **Decision**: option (a) BUILD it. Add an additive game-level cost-reduction\n  registry (e.g. GameState.spell_cost_reducers) that engine.casting.get_cost_reduction\n  sums alongside the spell's own hook, with a strict no-op default. Witherbloom\n  registers a reducer (affinity for creatures) for the controller's instant/sorcery\n  spells while on the battlefield. Tester re-invoked once after it lands.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_226"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":555,"cache_read_input_tokens":121439,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":555},"output_tokens":58,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"9bef199c-c357-4797-a12c-ab4f4f9b84da","request_id":"req_011CbcLoXA5ggbX3UKvuMw9M"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fks4m8HJodsELTPpX4rEAy","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"24692145-d732-49ee-b355-3745f4168215","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:58:15.880Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"## Untestable resolution: sos_226","newString":"## Untestable resolution: sos_245 (Witherbloom, the Balancer)\n- Testable/implemented: flying/deathtouch creature + own static data + its own\n  affinity cost reduction.\n- Untestable: \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures\" —\n  grants the controller's OTHER instant/sorcery spells a {1}-less-per-creature\n  reduction. The cast pipeline only consults a spell's OWN cost_reduction() hook;\n  no external registry exists (FDN 159 left the analogous clause inert).\n- **Decision**: option (a) BUILD it. Add an additive game-level cost-reduction\n  registry (e.g. GameState.spell_cost_reducers) that engine.casting.get_cost_reduction\n  sums alongside the spell's own hook, with a strict no-op default. Witherbloom\n  registers a reducer (affinity for creatures) for the controller's instant/sorcery\n  spells while on the battlefield. Tester re-invoked once after it lands.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_226","originalFile":"# Run Decisions\n\nDecisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant)\n- Testable/implemented: W/B 4/4 Flying/Vigilance Elder Dragon + the casualty 1 grant\n  modeled via card-local helpers (casualty_value, grants_casualty_to,\n  is_valid_casualty_sacrifice, apply_casualty = sacrifice + push one spell copy with\n  new targets). Uses engine.stack.copy_spell and engine.game.sacrifice.\n- Untestable: the \"as you cast\" pipeline integration (offering casualty as an\n  additional cost during a real engine-driven cast). The cast pipeline has no\n  as-you-cast hook / scriptable choice point.\n- **Decision**: option (b)-leaning. Build the helpers fully (tested). ATTEMPT only a\n  LOW-RISK, no-op-by-default additive as-you-cast hook in cast_spell; if it risks\n  regressing the heavily-tested cast pipeline or needs non-additive changes, leave the\n  pipeline untouched and mark the integration `# UNVERIFIED`. Tester re-invoked once\n  ONLY if the hook lands cleanly.\n- **Outcome**: Implementer found no clean no-op-by-default additional-cost hook in\n  engine/casting.py and left the as-you-cast integration UNVERIFIED (no engine\n  changes). Helpers built and fully tested (23/23). Cast pipeline untouched. No Tester\n  re-invocation.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian)\n- Testable/implemented: Flying, Haste, the STATIC miracle grant (queryable {2}\n  miracle cost on controller's hand instants/sorceries), and the opponent-upkeep\n  loot trigger.\n- The DYNAMIC miracle clause (reveal the first card drawn this turn and cast it for\n  the {2} miracle cost) needs a reveal-on-draw window hook + an alternative-cost cast\n  entry. `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` and DrawsCardTriggeredEvent exist as partial\n  surface.\n- **Decision**: option (a) attempt to BUILD additively (mirroring sos_57/sos_97);\n  UNVERIFIED fallback for any part that can't be done additively without regressing\n  engine_tests/. Tester re-invoked once iff the miracle window lands.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_120 (Improvisation Capstone)\n- Core (exile from top until a card with MV>=4 is found, free-cast it) is fully\n  testable/implemented.\n- The \"Paradigm\" mechanic (\"exile this spell; after you first resolve a spell with\n  this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the\n  beginning of each of your first main phases\") requires copy-from-exile machinery\n  that does NOT exist (same gap marked UNVERIFIED for sos_13's copy-cast). \"Paradigm\"\n  also can't be a Keyword (frozen 16-member enum).\n- **Decision**: option (b) accept partial coverage. The recurring copy-cast clause is\n  marked `# UNVERIFIED`. Implementer may add low-risk additive scaffolding (exile the\n  spell after resolution, record first-resolution state) but must NOT build a fragile\n  generic copy-from-exile system. No Tester re-invocation (no agreed observable contract).\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer — planeswalker)\n- Three of four abilities (Surveil 2, targeted discard, mv<=3 reanimation) fully\n  testable/implemented.\n- The -7 ultimate needs two ADDITIVE engine capabilities: (1) a deterministic\n  coin-flip helper (scriptable via DeterministicPlayer) so X = heads is assertable,\n  and (2) a per-player skipped-turns mechanism consulted by turn rotation.\n- **Decision**: option (a) attempt to BUILD both additively (mirroring sos_57). If a\n  part would regress engine_tests/ (esp. the turn loop) or need non-additive changes,\n  fall back to (b) `# UNVERIFIED` for that part. Tester re-invoked once for whatever lands.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)\n- Counter half (core) is fully testable/implemented.\n- The Wizard-gated delayed \"{C} at the beginning of your next main phase = mana\n  spent on the countered spell\" needs two ADDITIVE engine capabilities:\n  (1) a beginning-of-main-phase triggered event in engine/events.py fired from the\n  turn loop, and (2) recording total mana spent to cast a spell on the card/StackObject.\n- **Decision**: option (a) attempt to BUILD it additively. Implementer instructed to\n  add both capabilities additively; if any part would regress engine_tests/ or require\n  non-additive engine changes, fall back to (b) `# UNVERIFIED` markers for that part\n  and report. Tester re-invoked once IFF the engine support lands, to add {C}-bonus tests.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n- **Item 1 — \"Prepared\" keyword as a first-class flag**: INITIALLY directed as (a)\n  build it, but DOWNGRADED to (b) accept partial coverage. Adding `PREPARED` to\n  `engine.types.Keyword` regresses the authoritative read-only engine test\n  `engine_tests/test_types.py::TestKeyword::test_exactly_sixteen_members`\n  (asserts `len(Keyword) == 16`). Since engine_tests/ is authoritative for grading\n  and must not be modified, the keyword cannot be added without zeroing that test.\n  Implementer correctly declined and marked it `# UNVERIFIED`. The prepared state is\n  fully expressed via the `is_prepared` bool (tested). No Tester re-invocation.\n- **Item 2 — \"cast a copy of its spell while prepared, unpreparing it\"**: resolved\n  via (b) accept partial coverage. Requires major copy-cast/split-card engine\n  machinery; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:` marker added in card_impl.py.\n- **Item 3 — the \"Swords to Plowshares\" {W} instant face**: resolved via (b). The\n  engine has no second-castable-face representation; out of scope. `# UNVERIFIED:`\n  marker added in card_impl.py.\n- The conditional prepared STATE is exposed as an `is_prepared` bool (tested).\n\n## Test dispute: sos_4\n- **Disputed test**: `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player` (tests.py L180-198)\n- **Tester's intent**: verify \"you gain X life\" goes to the controller, not the target player, while the chosen any-target takes damage.\n- **Implementer's objection (feasibility)**: the test uses `chosen_targets=[p2, p1]`, naming p1 (controller) as the damage any-target (index 1), but asserts p2 (index 0) is damaged. This contradicts `test_two_colors_deals_two_damage_to_player` ([p1,p2] -> p2 damaged at index 1). No single index mapping satisfies both.\n- **Decision**: accept implementer (feasibility objection — test data is internally contradictory). Convention is draw=chosen_targets[0], damage any-target=chosen_targets[1], life gain=controller.\n- **Action**: re-invoke Tester to rewrite ONLY the disputed test, changing its data to `[p2, p2]` (draw target p2, damage any-target p2) so the intended \"life goes to controller p1\" check holds under the suite's index-1=damage convention.\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":6,"newStart":2,"newLines":19,"lines":[" "," Decisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`."," ","+## Untestable resolution: sos_245 (Witherbloom, the Balancer)","+- Testable/implemented: flying/deathtouch creature + own static data + its own","+  affinity cost reduction.","+- Untestable: \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures\" —","+  grants the controller's OTHER instant/sorcery spells a {1}-less-per-creature","+  reduction. The cast pipeline only consults a spell's OWN cost_reduction() hook;","+  no external registry exists (FDN 159 left the analogous clause inert).","+- **Decision**: option (a) BUILD it. Add an additive game-level cost-reduction","+  registry (e.g. GameState.spell_cost_reducers) that engine.casting.get_cost_reduction","+  sums alongside the spell's own hook, with a strict no-op default. Witherbloom","+  registers a reducer (affinity for creatures) for the controller's instant/sorcery","+  spells while on the battlefield. Tester re-invoked once after it lands.","+"," ## Untestable resolution: sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant)"," - Testable/implemented: W/B 4/4 Flying/Vigilance Elder Dragon + the casualty 1 grant","   modeled via card-local helpers (casualty_value, grants_casualty_to,"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01KWmQe44qogfHd6aWHRG1H2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WnZQ72CSYGrSiwACrpg7qA","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator directives — sos_245 (Witherbloom, the Balancer)\n\n## Build (in scope, fully tested)\n- The creature with Flying and Deathtouch (read card_spec.json for exact\n  name/cost/P-T/subtypes/colors). Static data correct.\n- The card's own affinity-for-creatures cost reduction (its OWN cost), per the\n  test contract.\nMake ALL current tests in `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` pass.\n\n## BUILD the external cost-reduction registry (additive engine work)\nOracle clause: \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"\nThis grants the CONTROLLER's OTHER instant/sorcery spells a {1}-less-per-creature\ngeneric cost reduction (clamped to the spell's generic cost). The cast pipeline\ncurrently only honors a spell's OWN `cost_reduction()` hook.\n\nAdd an ADDITIVE game-level cost-reduction registry:\n- e.g. `GameState.spell_cost_reducers` — a list/registry of reducer callables or\n  objects. `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` SUMS the registered reducers'\n  contributions ALONGSIDE the spell's own `cost_reduction()` hook.\n- STRICT no-op default: an empty registry must add zero reduction, so existing\n  casting tests are completely unaffected.\n- A reducer is keyed to a controller + spell predicate (instant/sorcery of that\n  controller) and produces a generic reduction (here: number of creatures the\n  controller controls — \"affinity for creatures\"), clamped so the spell's generic\n  cost never goes below 0.\n- Witherbloom registers its reducer while on the battlefield (and ideally\n  unregisters when it leaves, but a battlefield-presence re-check inside the reducer\n  is acceptable and safer). Look at how FDN 159 (Mocking Sprite) modeled the\n  analogous clause (as an inert marker) and improve on it via the registry.\n\n### HARD CONSTRAINT — additive only + green engine_tests/\n- All engine changes ADDITIVE: new attribute/registry/branches; do NOT\n  rename/move/delete existing engine symbols; do NOT add Keyword enum members; do\n  NOT touch engine_tests/ or FDN tests.\n- After ANY engine change run `pytest engine_tests/` — it MUST stay green. The empty\n  registry must be a strict no-op so cost-reduction/casting tests are unchanged.\n- If the registry cannot be added additively without regressing engine_tests/, mark\n  the clause `# UNVERIFIED` and report — but this is a clean additive change, so aim\n  to BUILD it.\n\n## Constraints\n- Make ALL tests pass; do NOT modify tests. Clean up temp files.\n- Prefer a green engine_tests/ suite over completeness.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1107,"cache_read_input_tokens":121994,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1107},"output_tokens":54,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"eae833dc-1c88-4cf5-9189-7b6e2533a0fa","request_id":"req_011CbcLpUZLesumLuPZaf9dz"}
