{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BD22idkCucPv518vuXonrC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator directives — sos_245 (Witherbloom, the Balancer)\n2\t\n3\t## Build (in scope, fully tested)\n4\t- The creature with Flying and Deathtouch (read card_spec.json for exact\n5\t  name/cost/P-T/subtypes/colors). Static data correct.\n6\t- The card's own affinity-for-creatures cost reduction (its OWN cost), per the\n7\t  test contract.\n8\tMake ALL current tests in `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` pass.\n9\t\n10\t## BUILD the external cost-reduction registry (additive engine work)\n11\tOracle clause: \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"\n12\tThis grants the CONTROLLER's OTHER instant/sorcery spells a {1}-less-per-creature\n13\tgeneric cost reduction (clamped to the spell's generic cost). The cast pipeline\n14\tcurrently only honors a spell's OWN `cost_reduction()` hook.\n15\t\n16\tAdd an ADDITIVE game-level cost-reduction registry:\n17\t- e.g. `GameState.spell_cost_reducers` — a list/registry of reducer callables or\n18\t  objects. `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` SUMS the registered reducers'\n19\t  contributions ALONGSIDE the spell's own `cost_reduction()` hook.\n20\t- STRICT no-op default: an empty registry must add zero reduction, so existing\n21\t  casting tests are completely unaffected.\n22\t- A reducer is keyed to a controller + spell predicate (instant/sorcery of that\n23\t  controller) and produces a generic reduction (here: number of creatures the\n24\t  controller controls — \"affinity for creatures\"), clamped so the spell's generic\n25\t  cost never goes below 0.\n26\t- Witherbloom registers its reducer while on the battlefield (and ideally\n27\t  unregisters when it leaves, but a battlefield-presence re-check inside the reducer\n28\t  is acceptable and safer). Look at how FDN 159 (Mocking Sprite) modeled the\n29\t  analogous clause (as an inert marker) and improve on it via the registry.\n30\t\n31\t### HARD CONSTRAINT — additive only + green engine_tests/\n32\t- All engine changes ADDITIVE: new attribute/registry/branches; do NOT\n33\t  rename/move/delete existing engine symbols; do NOT add Keyword enum members; do\n34\t  NOT touch engine_tests/ or FDN tests.\n35\t- After ANY engine change run `pytest engine_tests/` — it MUST stay green. The empty\n36\t  registry must be a strict no-op so cost-reduction/casting tests are unchanged.\n37\t- If the registry cannot be added additively without regressing engine_tests/, mark\n38\t  the clause `# UNVERIFIED` and report — but this is a clean additive change, so aim\n39\t  to BUILD it.\n40\t\n41\t## Constraints\n42\t- Make ALL tests pass; do NOT modify tests. Clean up temp files.\n43\t- Prefer a green engine_tests/ suite over completeness.\n44\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y8yGfyN1K4izYt6a4vpeSv","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"a8fd8e17-742c-40a7-a6f6-3f2d4dfa30d0","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:58:44.843Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_245"}
