{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017U5KUoEqxMzE3dPA7mHcfG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"requirement\": \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures. (This grants the controller's OTHER instant/sorcery spells a {1}-less-per-creature cost reduction.)\",\n4\t    \"reason\": \"The casting pipeline (engine/casting.py:get_cost_reduction) only consults a spell's OWN cost_reduction() hook. There is no central/external cost-reduction registry that one permanent on the battlefield can use to reduce the cost of a DIFFERENT spell its controller casts. FDN 159 (Mocking Sprite), which has the analogous 'instant and sorcery spells you cast cost {1} less' clause, models this only as an inert marker flag for the same reason. Without engine infrastructure, casting an unrelated instant cannot be asserted to receive the affinity discount.\",\n5\t    \"what_would_unblock\": \"Add an additive game-level cost-reduction registry (e.g. GameState.spell_cost_reducers) that engine.casting.get_cost_reduction sums alongside the card's own cost_reduction() hook, with a no-op default so existing tests are unaffected. Witherbloom would register a reducer granting 'affinity for creatures' to the controller's instant/sorcery spells; a test could then cast a vanilla instant with N creatures in play and assert its effective generic cost dropped by N (clamped to its generic).\"\n6\t  }\n7\t]\n8\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y8yGfyN1K4izYt6a4vpeSv","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"841a52e5-e0b4-42d0-b378-455bde3a3fd6","timestamp":"2026-06-01T09:58:45.312Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_245"}
