{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01CtA5945VYLJC2811Z4h38t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AVq3cYxmHi2yPa1ZfB3Qiq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation rationale — sos_245 (Witherbloom, the Balancer)\n\n## Card\n`cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py` — `WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature)`:\n- Static data per spec: `{6}{B}{G}`, 5/5, Legendary, subtypes `{Elder, Dragon}`,\n  keywords `FLYING | DEATHTOUCH`. (No new `Keyword` enum members — both already\n  exist; respects KEY_DECISIONS.)\n- **Affinity for creatures (own cost)** via `cost_reduction(game)`: counts\n  creatures the controller controls on the battlefield. Witherbloom is on the\n  stack while being cast, so it never counts itself — matching \"for each creature\n  you control\". The generic-only clamp is handled centrally by\n  `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`.\n- `get_targets` returns `[]` (static abilities; casting must not demand a target).\n- **Granted affinity** to other instant/sorcery spells: registered in\n  `register_triggers` via the new game-level registry (see below). Improves on\n  FDN 159, which modeled the analogous clause as an inert marker flag.\n\n## Engine registry BUILT (additive)\nAdded to `engine/game_state.py`:\n- `GameState.spell_cost_reducers: list[dict]` — empty by default.\n- `register_spell_cost_reducer(predicate, amount, *, source)` —\n  `predicate(game, card, controller) -> bool`, `amount(game, card, controller) -> int`.\n- `unregister_spell_cost_reducer(source)` — identity-based cleanup.\n- `spell_cost_reduction_from_reducers(card, controller) -> int` — sums every\n  applicable reducer's amount; **strict no-op (returns 0) when the registry is\n  empty**, and swallows per-reducer exceptions so a bad reducer can't break casting.\n\nWired into `engine/casting.py::get_cost_reduction`: the external reducer sum is\nADDED to the spell's own `cost_reduction()` hook, then the combined total is\nclamped to the spell's generic (`max(0, min(raw, generic))`). The hook is looked\nup with `getattr(..., None)` so casting still works against any `game`-like object\nthat lacks the method.\n\nWitherbloom's registered reducer:\n- **predicate**: card is not Witherbloom itself, card is instant/sorcery, the\n  casting controller is Witherbloom's controller, and Witherbloom is currently on\n  a battlefield (battlefield-presence re-check, so it auto-disables if it leaves\n  even without an explicit unregister — the safer option the directives allowed).\n- **amount**: number of creatures the controller controls (\"affinity for creatures\").\n\nVerified end-to-end (manually): with Witherbloom + 3 bears, an unrelated `{4}{R}`\ninstant gets reduction 4 (clamped to its generic); Witherbloom's own spell is\nunaffected by the reducer; after `unregister_spell_cost_reducer` the reduction\nreturns to 0. `pytest engine_tests/` stays fully green (1145 passed) — the empty\nregistry is a strict no-op.\n\n## Test results\n24/25 sos_245 tests pass. One test is DISPUTED (see below).\n\n## DISPUTED test (impossible as written)\n`TestWitherbloomCastingWithAffinity::test_cast_with_three_creatures_pays_reduced_generic`\nexpects `cast_spell` to succeed but never advances the game to a main phase\n(`create_game()` leaves it in `Phase.BEGINNING`). Witherbloom is a non-flash\ncreature, so `cast_spell` requires sorcery-speed timing. The authoritative\n`engine_tests/test_casting.py` forbids loosening this\n(`test_beginning_phase_returns_false`, and `test_creature_during_combat_phase_raises`\nrequires a non-main-phase active-player cast to raise). There is no additive engine\nchange that makes the BEGINNING-phase cast succeed without breaking those read-only\nengine tests. The test is missing a `game.phase = Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN` setup line;\nadding it makes the cast succeed (verified). Full details in `test-dispute.md`.\n\n## UNVERIFIED\nNone. The registry is fully BUILT and exercised; only one test is disputed as\ntesting impossible behavior (missing phase setup), not an engine limitation.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":179,"cache_read_input_tokens":79804,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":179,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":68,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y8yGfyN1K4izYt6a4vpeSv","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"fee2e577-62a0-4b58-aaa8-969b12c9461a","request_id":"req_011CbcM6hA4vBFuVLMLpUTht","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_245"}
