{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y8yGfyN1K4izYt6a4vpeSv","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Final state: engine tests fully green, 24/25 sos_245 tests pass, and the one remaining failure is the disputed test that omits main-phase setup (impossible to satisfy without breaking authoritative `engine_tests/`).\n\nThe engine cost-reduction registry was BUILT and verified end-to-end. I'm returning DISPUTE because one test is genuinely impossible as written (not an engine limitation).\n\nDISPUTE\ntests_failing: 1\ndisputed_tests: cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py::TestWitherbloomCastingWithAffinity::test_cast_with_three_creatures_pays_reduced_generic (lines 173-193)\ndispute_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-dispute.md\nnotes: Registry BUILT and green (engine_tests 1145 passed; full suite 1169 passed, 1 failed). The single failure expects `cast_spell` to succeed but never advances `create_game()` past `Phase.BEGINNING`; Witherbloom is a non-flash creature needing sorcery-speed timing. The authoritative `engine_tests/test_casting.py` (`test_beginning_phase_returns_false`, `test_creature_during_combat_phase_raises`) forbid any additive change that lets a BEGINNING-phase active-player cast succeed without breaking them. Adding the missing `game.phase = Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN` makes the cast pass (verified). 24/25 tests pass; full implementation (static data, Flying/Deathtouch, own affinity reduction + pipeline clamp) and the requested additive `GameState.spell_cost_reducers` registry summed in `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` are in place and exercised.\n\nRelevant files (all absolute):\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-dispute.md\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl.diff\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-rationale.md\n- /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-files.txt\n- /workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py\n- /workspace/engine/game_state.py\n- /workspace/engine/casting.py\n- /workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json"}