{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L5Q18a3C5rnpdtmdUo1xyP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test dispute — sos_245\n2\t\n3\t## Disputed test\n4\t\n5\t`cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py::TestWitherbloomCastingWithAffinity::test_cast_with_three_creatures_pays_reduced_generic`\n6\t(lines 173-193)\n7\t\n8\t### What the test does\n9\t```python\n10\tgame = create_game()\n11\tp1 = game.players[0]\n12\tgame.active_player_index = 0\n13\tgame.priority_player_index = 0\n14\tset_board_state(game, 0, battlefield=[_bear(\"A\"), _bear(\"B\"), _bear(\"C\")])\n15\t\n16\tcard = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=p1, controller=p1)\n17\tgame.get_hand(p1).add(card)\n18\tset_board_state(game, 0, mana={ManaType.COLORLESS: 3, ManaType.BLACK: 1, ManaType.GREEN: 1})\n19\t\n20\tcast_spell(game, p1, card)\n21\tassert not game.stack.is_empty()\n22\t```\n23\t\n24\tThe test expects `engine.casting.cast_spell` to succeed (the spell hits the stack).\n25\t\n26\t### Why this is impossible given the engine contract\n27\t`create_game()` (and `GameState.__init__`) leaves the game in\n28\t`Phase.BEGINNING` / `Step.UNTAP`. The test never advances to a main phase\n29\t(it sets `active_player_index` and `priority_player_index` only). Witherbloom\n30\tis a **creature** (no flash, not an instant), so `cast_spell` requires\n31\t**sorcery-speed timing** via `is_sorcery_speed(game, player)`.\n32\t\n33\tThe authoritative engine regression tests in `engine_tests/test_casting.py`\n34\tfix the timing rule and forbid loosening it:\n35\t\n36\t- `TestIsSorcerySpeed::test_beginning_phase_returns_false` (line 94) asserts\n37\t  `is_sorcery_speed(...) is False` during the BEGINNING phase.\n38\t- `TestCastTiming::test_creature_during_combat_phase_raises` (line 251) asserts\n39\t  that casting a non-flash creature while the **active player** has an\n40\t  **empty stack** but is **not in a main phase** raises `CastingError`.\n41\t\n42\tBecause BEGINNING and COMBAT are both non-main phases for the active player\n43\twith an empty stack, there is **no additive engine change** that lets the cast\n44\tsucceed during BEGINNING without also making the COMBAT case succeed — which\n45\twould break `test_creature_during_combat_phase_raises`. `engine_tests/` is\n46\tread-only and authoritative for grading, so the timing rule cannot change.\n47\t\n48\t### Correct behavior / how the test should read\n49\tThe test almost certainly intended to set a main phase before casting, e.g.:\n50\t```python\n51\tgame.phase = Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN\n52\tgame.step = None\n53\t```\n54\t(or import `Phase` and call `advance_to_phase`). With that one-line fix the\n55\tcast succeeds: 3 creatures → affinity reduces `{6}{B}{G}` to `{3}{B}{G}`, which\n56\tthe scripted `{3}{B}{G}` worth of mana pays exactly, and the spell hits the\n57\tstack — exactly what the assertion checks.\n58\t\n59\tNote the two sibling negative tests\n60\t(`test_cast_without_enough_mana_for_reduced_cost_fails`,\n61\t`test_colored_pips_never_reduced`) currently pass regardless of this bug,\n62\tbecause they expect a `CastingError` and would get one from either the timing\n63\tgate or the mana gate. Only the positive test exposes the missing phase setup.\n64\t\n65\t### Implementation status\n66\tEverything else is implemented and passing (24/25 tests):\n67\t- Static data, Flying, Deathtouch, affinity-for-creatures own cost reduction\n68\t  (including the `get_cost_reduction` clamp-to-generic path).\n69\t- The requested additive engine cost-reduction registry\n70\t  (`GameState.spell_cost_reducers` + `register_spell_cost_reducer` /\n71\t  `unregister_spell_cost_reducer` / `spell_cost_reduction_from_reducers`,\n72\t  summed in `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`). `pytest engine_tests/`\n73\t  stays fully green (1145 passed).\n74\t\n75\tThe implementation is left in place; only this one test is disputed as\n76\ttesting impossible behavior (missing main-phase setup).\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"786c5558-9cee-4963-863a-bc466eede9cc","timestamp":"2026-06-01T10:03:00.053Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-dispute.md","content":"# Test dispute — sos_245\n\n## Disputed test\n\n`cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py::TestWitherbloomCastingWithAffinity::test_cast_with_three_creatures_pays_reduced_generic`\n(lines 173-193)\n\n### What the test does\n```python\ngame = create_game()\np1 = game.players[0]\ngame.active_player_index = 0\ngame.priority_player_index = 0\nset_board_state(game, 0, battlefield=[_bear(\"A\"), _bear(\"B\"), _bear(\"C\")])\n\ncard = WitherbloomTheBalancer(owner=p1, controller=p1)\ngame.get_hand(p1).add(card)\nset_board_state(game, 0, mana={ManaType.COLORLESS: 3, ManaType.BLACK: 1, ManaType.GREEN: 1})\n\ncast_spell(game, p1, card)\nassert not game.stack.is_empty()\n```\n\nThe test expects `engine.casting.cast_spell` to succeed (the spell hits the stack).\n\n### Why this is impossible given the engine contract\n`create_game()` (and `GameState.__init__`) leaves the game in\n`Phase.BEGINNING` / `Step.UNTAP`. The test never advances to a main phase\n(it sets `active_player_index` and `priority_player_index` only). Witherbloom\nis a **creature** (no flash, not an instant), so `cast_spell` requires\n**sorcery-speed timing** via `is_sorcery_speed(game, player)`.\n\nThe authoritative engine regression tests in `engine_tests/test_casting.py`\nfix the timing rule and forbid loosening it:\n\n- `TestIsSorcerySpeed::test_beginning_phase_returns_false` (line 94) asserts\n  `is_sorcery_speed(...) is False` during the BEGINNING phase.\n- `TestCastTiming::test_creature_during_combat_phase_raises` (line 251) asserts\n  that casting a non-flash creature while the **active player** has an\n  **empty stack** but is **not in a main phase** raises `CastingError`.\n\nBecause BEGINNING and COMBAT are both non-main phases for the active player\nwith an empty stack, there is **no additive engine change** that lets the cast\nsucceed during BEGINNING without also making the COMBAT case succeed — which\nwould break `test_creature_during_combat_phase_raises`. `engine_tests/` is\nread-only and authoritative for grading, so the timing rule cannot change.\n\n### Correct behavior / how the test should read\nThe test almost certainly intended to set a main phase before casting, e.g.:\n```python\ngame.phase = Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN\ngame.step = None\n```\n(or import `Phase` and call `advance_to_phase`). With that one-line fix the\ncast succeeds: 3 creatures → affinity reduces `{6}{B}{G}` to `{3}{B}{G}`, which\nthe scripted `{3}{B}{G}` worth of mana pays exactly, and the spell hits the\nstack — exactly what the assertion checks.\n\nNote the two sibling negative tests\n(`test_cast_without_enough_mana_for_reduced_cost_fails`,\n`test_colored_pips_never_reduced`) currently pass regardless of this bug,\nbecause they expect a `CastingError` and would get one from either the timing\ngate or the mana gate. Only the positive test exposes the missing phase setup.\n\n### Implementation status\nEverything else is implemented and passing (24/25 tests):\n- Static data, Flying, Deathtouch, affinity-for-creatures own cost reduction\n  (including the `get_cost_reduction` clamp-to-generic path).\n- The requested additive engine cost-reduction registry\n  (`GameState.spell_cost_reducers` + `register_spell_cost_reducer` /\n  `unregister_spell_cost_reducer` / `spell_cost_reduction_from_reducers`,\n  summed in `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`). `pytest engine_tests/`\n  stays fully green (1145 passed).\n\nThe implementation is left in place; only this one test is disputed as\ntesting impossible behavior (missing main-phase setup).\n","numLines":77,"startLine":1,"totalLines":77}}}
