e\n```\n(or use `advance_to_phase` if that's the established convention in the file). Keep the\nexisting assertion that the spell hits the stack and that 3 creatures reduce the\ngeneric cost so the scripted `{3}{B}{G}` mana pays exactly.\n\nDo NOT modify any other test. Do NOT change the implementation. After the edit, run\n`pytest cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` and confirm all 25 tests pass.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":43,"newStart":1,"newLines":33,"lines":["-# Coordinator directives — sos_245 (Witherbloom, the Balancer)","+# Coordinator directives — sos_245 (dispute resolution)"," ","-## Build (in scope, fully tested)","-- The creature with Flying and Deathtouch (read card_spec.json for exact","-  name/cost/P-T/subtypes/colors). Static data correct.","-- The card's own affinity-for-creatures cost reduction (its OWN cost), per the","-  test contract.","-Make ALL current tests in `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` pass.","+**Decision: the Implementer's feasibility objection is UPHELD.** The disputed test","+`TestWitherbloomCastingWithAffinity::test_cast_with_three_creatures_pays_reduced_generic`","+casts a non-flash creature (Witherbloom) while the game is still in `Phase.BEGINNING`","+(the `create_game()` default), never advancing to a main phase. Creatures require","+sorcery-speed timing, and the authoritative read-only engine tests","+(`engine_tests/test_casting.py::test_beginning_phase_returns_false`,","+`::test_creature_during_combat_phase_raises`) forbid any additive engine change that","+would let a non-main-phase active-player cast succeed. The cast can therefore never","+reach the stack as the test is written."," ","-## BUILD the external cost-reduction registry (additive engine work)","-Oracle clause: \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"","-This grants the CONTROLLER's OTHER instant/sorcery spells a {1}-less-per-creature","-generic cost reduction (clamped to the spell's generic cost). The cast pipeline","-currently only honors a spell's OWN `cost_reduction()` hook.","+The implementation (static data, Flying/Deathtouch, affinity-for-creatures own cost","+reduction, and the additive `GameState.spell_cost_reducers` registry summed in","+`engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`) is CORRECT and stays. Do NOT change it."," ","-Add an ADDITIVE game-level cost-reduction registry:","-- e.g. `GameState.spell_cost_reducers` — a list/registry of reducer callables or","-  objects. `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` SUMS the registered reducers'","-  contributions ALONGSIDE the spell's own `cost_reduction()` hook.","-- STRICT no-op default: an empty registry must add zero reduction, so existing","-  casting tests are completely unaffected.","-- A reducer is keyed to a controller + spell predicate (instant/sorcery of that","-  controller) and produces a generic reduction (here: number of creatures the","-  controller controls — \"affinity for creatures\"), clamped so the spell's generic","-  cost never goes below 0.","-- Witherbloom registers its reducer while on the battlefield (and ideally","-  unregisters when it leaves, but a battlefield-presence re-check inside the reducer","-  is acceptable and safer). Look at how FDN 159 (Mocking Sprite) modeled the","-  analogous clause (as an inert marker) and improve on it via the registry.","+## Fix ONLY this one test","+In `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`, the test","+`TestWitherbloomCastingWithAffinity::test_cast_with_three_creatures_pays_reduced_generic`","+(~L173-193): add the missing main-phase setup before the `cast_spell(...)` call so the","+sorcery-speed creature can legally be cast, e.g.:","+```python","+from engine.types import Phase   # if not already imported","+...","+game.phase = Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN","+game.step = None","+```","+(or use `advance_to_phase` if that's the established convention in the file). Keep the","+existing assertion that the spell hits the stack and that 3 creatures reduce the","+generic cost so the scripted `{3}{B}{G}` mana pays exactly."," ","-### HARD CONSTRAINT — additive only + green engine_tests/","-- All engine changes ADDITIVE: new attribute/registry/branches; do NOT","-  rename/move/delete existing engine symbols; do NOT add Keyword enum members; do","-  NOT touch engine_tests/ or FDN tests.","-- After ANY engine change run `pytest engine_tests/` — it MUST stay green. The empty","-  registry must be a strict no-op so cost-reduction/casting tests are unchanged.","-- If the registry cannot be added additively without regressing engine_tests/, mark","-  the clause `# UNVERIFIED` and report — but this is a clean additive change, so aim","-  to BUILD it.","-","-## Constraints","-- Make ALL tests pass; do NOT modify tests. Clean up temp files.","-- Prefer a green engine_tests/ suite over completeness.","+Do NOT modify any other test. Do NOT change the implementation. After the edit, run","+`pytest cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` and confirm all 25 tests pass."]}],"originalFile":"# Coordinator directives — sos_245 (Witherbloom, the Balancer)\n\n## Build (in scope, fully tested)\n- The creature with Flying and Deathtouch (read card_spec.json for exact\n  name/cost/P-T/subtypes/colors). Static data correct.\n- The card's own affinity-for-creatures cost reduction (its OWN cost), per the\n  test contract.\nMake ALL current tests in `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` pass.\n\n## BUILD the external cost-reduction registry (additive engine work)\nOracle clause: \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"\nThis grants the CONTROLLER's OTHER instant/sorcery spells a {1}-less-per-creature\ngeneric cost reduction (clamped to the spell's generic cost). The cast pipeline\ncurrently only honors a spell's OWN `cost_reduction()` hook.\n\nAdd an ADDITIVE game-level cost-reduction registry:\n- e.g. `GameState.spell_cost_reducers` — a list/registry of reducer callables or\n  objects. `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` SUMS the registered reducers'\n  contributions ALONGSIDE the spell's own `cost_reduction()` hook.\n- STRICT no-op default: an empty registry must add zero reduction, so existing\n  casting tests are completely unaffected.\n- A reducer is keyed to a controller + spell predicate (instant/sorcery of that\n  controller) and produces a generic reduction (here: number of creatures the\n  controller controls — \"affinity for creatures\"), clamped so the spell's generic\n  cost never goes below 0.\n- Witherbloom registers its reducer while on the battlefield (and ideally\n  unregisters when it leaves, but a battlefield-presence re-check inside the reducer\n  is acceptable and safer). Look at how FDN 159 (Mocking Sprite) modeled the\n  analogous clause (as an inert marker) and improve on it via the registry.\n\n### HARD CONSTRAINT — additive only + green engine_tests/\n- All engine changes ADDITIVE: new attribute/registry/branches; do NOT\n  rename/move/delete existing engine symbols; do NOT add Keyword enum members; do\n  NOT touch engine_tests/ or FDN tests.\n- After ANY engine change run `pytest engine_tests/` — it MUST stay green. The empty\n  registry must be a strict no-op so cost-reduction/casting tests are unchanged.\n- If the registry cannot be added additively without regressing engine_tests/, mark\n  the clause `# UNVERIFIED` and report — but this is a clean additive change, so aim\n  to BUILD it.\n\n## Constraints\n- Make ALL tests pass; do NOT modify tests. Clean up temp files.\n- Prefer a green engine_tests/ suite over completeness.\n","userModified":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01DuU4WFoGxGvE6Lv1DopUn7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PFg5XqEDo62ZsYBssDgRPv","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix disputed sos_245 test","subagent_type":"Tester","prompt":"Dispute resolution for SOS card `sos_245`. The coordinator has ruled on a test dispute. CARD_DIR = `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245`.\n\nRead `$CARD_DIR/coordinator-directives.md` — it contains the binding ruling and the exact fix.\n\nYou must fix ONLY the single disputed test in `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`:\n`TestWitherbloomCastingWithAffinity::test_cast_with_three_creatures_pays_reduced_generic` (~L173-193).\n\nThe fix: the test casts a non-flash creature while the game is still in `Phase.BEGINNING` (create_game default), so the cast can never legally reach the stack. Add the missing main-phase setup (e.g. `game.phase = Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN` and `game.step = None`, importing `Phase` from `engine.types` if needed, or use the file's established `advance_to_phase` convention) before the `cast_spell(...)` call. Keep the existing assertions (spell hits the stack; 3 creatures reduce the generic cost so the scripted `{3}{B}{G}` mana pays exactly).\n\nDo NOT modify any other test. Do NOT modify the implementation (`cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py`, engine/) — it is correct and the registry is built.\n\nCard spec: `cards/sos/sos_245/card_spec.json`.\n\nAfter editing, run `pytest cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` and confirm ALL 25 tests pass.\n\nOutput:\n- Append a short note to `$CARD_DIR/test-rationale.md` describing the dispute-resolution edit.\n- Ensure `$CARD_DIR/test-files.txt` still lists `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`.\n\nReturn a short status: which test changed and whether the full file passes now."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":863,"cache_read_input_tokens":130459,"c