{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01DNH4eWbT84ygv1pz1MY6AR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HwcPhRpe1q2HYXdHiQNaBQ","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Extend sos_245 tests for registry","subagent_type":"Tester","prompt":"Extend the test suite for SOS card `sos_245` (Witherbloom, the Balancer). CARD_DIR = `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245`.\n\nCONTEXT: Your original `untestable.json` recorded that \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures\" — i.e. Witherbloom granting the controller's OTHER instant/sorcery spells a {1}-less-per-creature generic reduction — was UNTESTABLE because there was no external cost-reduction registry. The Implementer has now BUILT it additively. Read `$CARD_DIR/impl-rationale.md` for the exact API; per the implementer it added:\n- `GameState.spell_cost_reducers` plus `register_spell_cost_reducer` / `unregister_spell_cost_reducer` / `spell_cost_reduction_from_reducers`.\n- `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` now SUMS the registered reducers alongside a spell's own `cost_reduction()` hook (no-op when the registry is empty).\n- Witherbloom registers a reducer (affinity for creatures) for the controller's instant/sorcery spells while it is on the battlefield.\n\nYOUR TASK: ADD new tests to `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` covering the registry / granted-affinity behavior. Do NOT remove or alter existing passing tests. Cover at least:\n- With Witherbloom on the battlefield and N creatures in play, casting a SEPARATE vanilla instant/sorcery (NOT Witherbloom) has its generic cost reduced by N (clamped so generic never goes below 0). Set up a main phase / proper timing as needed (note: instants don't need sorcery speed, but match the file's conventions). Use a simple test instant/sorcery card (define a tiny local one or reuse an FDN/SOS instant).\n- The reduction applies only to the CONTROLLER's instant/sorcery spells (an opponent's spell, or a creatur