{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XNnxDFZbvPYeRakh88X8dw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation rationale — sos_245 (Witherbloom, the Balancer)\n2\t\n3\t## Card\n4\t`cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py` — `WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature)`:\n5\t- Static data per spec: `{6}{B}{G}`, 5/5, Legendary, subtypes `{Elder, Dragon}`,\n6\t  keywords `FLYING | DEATHTOUCH`. (No new `Keyword` enum members — both already\n7\t  exist; respects KEY_DECISIONS.)\n8\t- **Affinity for creatures (own cost)** via `cost_reduction(game)`: counts\n9\t  creatures the controller controls on the battlefield. Witherbloom is on the\n10\t  stack while being cast, so it never counts itself — matching \"for each creature\n11\t  you control\". The generic-only clamp is handled centrally by\n12\t  `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`.\n13\t- `get_targets` returns `[]` (static abilities; casting must not demand a target).\n14\t- **Granted affinity** to other instant/sorcery spells: registered in\n15\t  `register_triggers` via the new game-level registry (see below). Improves on\n16\t  FDN 159, which modeled the analogous clause as an inert marker flag.\n17\t\n18\t## Engine registry BUILT (additive)\n19\tAdded to `engine/game_state.py`:\n20\t- `GameState.spell_cost_reducers: list[dict]` — empty by default.\n21\t- `register_spell_cost_reducer(predicate, amount, *, source)` —\n22\t  `predicate(game, card, controller) -> bool`, `amount(game, card, controller) -> int`.\n23\t- `unregister_spell_cost_reducer(source)` — identity-based cleanup.\n24\t- `spell_cost_reduction_from_reducers(card, controller) -> int` — sums every\n25\t  applicable reducer's amount; **strict no-op (returns 0) when the registry is\n26\t  empty**, and swallows per-reducer exceptions so a bad reducer can't break casting.\n27\t\n28\tWired into `engine/casting.py::get_cost_reduction`: the external reducer sum is\n29\tADDED to the spell's own `cost_reduction()` hook, then the combined total is\n30\tclamped to the spell's generic (`max(0, min(raw, generic))`). The hook is looked\n31\tup with `getattr(..., None)` so casting still works against any `game`-like object\n32\tthat lacks the method.\n33\t\n34\tWitherbloom's registered reducer:\n35\t- **predicate**: card is not Witherbloom itself, card is instant/sorcery, the\n36\t  casting controller is Witherbloom's controller, and Witherbloom is currently on\n37\t  a battlefield (battlefield-presence re-check, so it auto-disables if it leaves\n38\t  even without an explicit unregister — the safer option the directives allowed).\n39\t- **amount**: number of creatures the controller controls (\"affinity for creatures\").\n40\t\n41\tVerified end-to-end (manually): with Witherbloom + 3 bears, an unrelated `{4}{R}`\n42\tinstant gets reduction 4 (clamped to its generic); Witherbloom's own spell is\n43\tunaffected by the reducer; after `unregister_spell_cost_reducer` the reduction\n44\treturns to 0. `pytest engine_tests/` stays fully green (1145 passed) — the empty\n45\tregistry is a strict no-op.\n46\t\n47\t## Test results\n48\t24/25 sos_245 tests pass. One test is DISPUTED (see below).\n49\t\n50\t## DISPUTED test (impossible as written)\n51\t`TestWitherbloomCastingWithAffinity::test_cast_with_three_creatures_pays_reduced_generic`\n52\texpects `cast_spell` to succeed but never advances the game to a main phase\n53\t(`create_game()` leaves it in `Phase.BEGINNING`). Witherbloom is a non-flash\n54\tcreature, so `cast_spell` requires sorcery-speed timing. The authoritative\n55\t`engine_tests/test_casting.py` forbids loosening this\n56\t(`test_beginning_phase_returns_false`, and `test_creature_during_combat_phase_raises`\n57\trequires a non-main-phase active-player cast to raise). There is no additive engine\n58\tchange that makes the BEGINNING-phase cast succeed without breaking those read-only\n59\tengine tests. The test is missing a `game.phase = Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN` setup line;\n60\tadding it makes the cast succeed (verified). Full details in `test-dispute.md`.\n61\t\n62\t## UNVERIFIED\n63\tNone. The registry is fully BUILT and exercised; only one test is disputed as\n64\ttesting impossible behavior (missing phase setup), not an engine limitation.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01HwcPhRpe1q2HYXdHiQNaBQ","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"10e13e9a-316c-4cb0-abed-ca80f3d49946","timestamp":"2026-06-01T10:05:09.129Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend sos_245 tests for registry"}
