{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016WtgmjhqnQd2yRPD5iVk1W","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale — SOS 245 Witherbloom, the Balancer\n2\t\n3\tCard: `{6}{B}{G}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5.\n4\tOracle text:\n5\t- Affinity for creatures (costs {1} less to cast for each creature you control).\n6\t- Flying, deathtouch.\n7\t- Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\n8\t\n9\tTest file: `cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`\n10\t\n11\t## TestWitherbloomProperties\n12\tLocks the printed characteristics against the spec:\n13\t- `test_is_creature` — is a `Creature` and has `CardType.CREATURE`.\n14\t- `test_name` — name matches `\"Witherbloom, the Balancer\"`.\n15\t- `test_mana_cost` — equals `ManaCost.parse(\"{6}{B}{G}\")`.\n16\t- `test_power_toughness` — base 5/5.\n17\t- `test_is_legendary` — `Supertype.LEGENDARY` present (type line is Legendary).\n18\t- `test_is_elder_dragon` — subtypes include `\"Dragon\"` and `\"Elder\"`.\n19\t\n20\t## TestWitherbloomKeywords\n21\t- `test_has_flying` / `test_has_deathtouch` — the two printed evergreen keywords.\n22\t- `test_does_not_have_unrelated_keyword` — guards against accidentally OR-ing\n23\t  in a keyword the card does not have (uses TRAMPLE as a negative control).\n24\t\n25\t## TestWitherbloomAffinity\n26\tValidates the \"Affinity for creatures\" cost-reduction hook\n27\t(`cost_reduction(game)`), which the engine only applies to the generic portion.\n28\t- `test_no_creatures_no_reduction` — zero creatures → reduction 0.\n29\t- `test_reduction_equals_creature_count` — three creatures → raw reduction 3.\n30\t- `test_self_counts_when_on_battlefield_does_not_inflate` — two creatures → 2.\n31\t- `test_only_counts_creatures` — artifacts/enchantments on the battlefield do\n32\t  not contribute (affinity is specifically *for creatures*).\n33\t- `test_only_counts_your_creatures` — opponent creatures do not reduce the cost\n34\t  (\"creatures *you* control\").\n35\t- `test_reduction_clamped_to_generic_via_pipeline` — with 9 creatures the raw\n36\t  value is 9 but `get_cost_reduction` clamps it to the `{6}` generic, since the\n37\t  `{B}{G}` pips are never reducible.\n38\t\n39\t## TestWitherbloomCastingWithAffinity\n40\tEnd-to-end exercise through `engine.casting.cast_spell`:\n41\t- `test_cast_with_three_creatures_pays_reduced_generic` — `{6}{B}{G}` with three\n42\t  creatures becomes payable with `{3}{B}{G}`; the spell reaches the stack.\n43\t- `test_cast_without_enough_mana_for_reduced_cost_fails` — one creature only\n44\t  reduces by 1, so `{3}{B}{G}` worth of mana is insufficient → `CastingError`.\n45\t- `test_colored_pips_never_reduced` — even with 8 creatures and 10 colorless\n46\t  mana, the cast fails without black/green for the pips (affinity reduces only\n47\t  generic mana).\n48\t\n49\t## TestWitherbloomFlying\n50\tFlying's blocking restriction via `engine.combat._can_block` (same pattern as\n51\tthe FDN 142 reference test):\n52\t- `test_ground_creature_cannot_block` — keyword-less creature cannot block it.\n53\t- `test_flying_blocker_can_block` — flyer can.\n54\t- `test_reach_blocker_can_block` — reach creature can.\n55\t\n56\t## TestWitherbloomDeathtouch\n57\tDeathtouch's lethal-damage rule via `engine.combat._get_lethal_damage`:\n58\t- `test_one_damage_is_lethal_against_high_toughness` — with Witherbloom as the\n59\t  attacker, 1 damage is lethal to a 10-toughness blocker.\n60\t- `test_without_deathtouch_lethal_is_toughness` — control: a vanilla attacker\n61\t  needs the full toughness, proving the deathtouch test is meaningful.\n62\t\n63\t## TestWitherbloomGrantsAffinity\n64\t\"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\" The engine\n65\thas no central cost-reduction registry (see FDN 159 Mocking Sprite, whose\n66\tanalogous \"cost {1} less\" clause is modeled only as a marker). These cover the\n67\tobservable surface:\n68\t- `test_register_triggers_does_not_raise` — wiring up the granted-affinity\n69\t  machinery must not raise.\n70\t- `test_card_advertises_no_spell_targets` — Witherbloom's abilities are all\n71\t  static, so `get_targets` must be empty and casting it must not demand a target\n72\t  (per KEY_DECISIONS: card-level `get_targets` is only for the spell itself).\n73\t\n74\t## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered\n75\t- The actual cost reduction applied to *other* instant/sorcery spells the\n76\t  controller casts. There is no central cost-reduction registry the casting\n77\t  pipeline consults for granted affinity from another permanent — only a card's\n78\t  own `cost_reduction()` hook is honored. Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n79\t- Legend rule / two copies in play — engine-level SBA behavior, out of scope for\n80\t  this card's own contract (covered by `engine_tests/`).\n81\t\n82\t## Dispute resolution edit (2026-06-01)\n83\t\n84\tPer the coordinator's binding ruling (Implementer's feasibility objection UPHELD),\n85\tthe single disputed test\n86\t`TestWitherbloomCastingWithAffinity::test_cast_with_three_creatures_pays_reduced_generic`\n87\twas fixed. The test previously cast a non-flash creature while the game was still in\n88\t`Phase.BEGINNING` (the `create_game()` default), so the sorcery-speed cast could never\n89\tlegally reach the stack. Added the missing main-phase setup before `cast_spell(...)`:\n90\t`game.phase = Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN` and `game.step = None` (with `Phase` now imported\n91\tfrom `engine.types`). The existing assertions are unchanged — the spell still must hit\n92\tthe stack and the 3 creatures still reduce {6}{B}{G} -> {3}{B}{G} so the scripted\n93\t`{3}{B}{G}` mana pays exactly. No other test and no implementation file was modified.\n94\tAll 25 tests in the file pass.\n95\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01HwcPhRpe1q2HYXdHiQNaBQ","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"abb086d6-e1ae-4531-82d9-f5ca09f466b6","timestamp":"2026-06-01T10:05:10.498Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend sos_245 tests for registry"}
