{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JjmHBjGEyJ1mjacdFiQTo1","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"REVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 1\nadvisory_count: 1\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/review.json\n\nKey finding (strict): `register_triggers` registers the spell-cost reducer on every battlefield entry, but nothing calls `unregister_spell_cost_reducer` on leave (the engine leave path at `/workspace/engine/zones.py:297-299` only unregisters triggers/replacements). Since `register_triggers` is non-idempotent and runs again on re-entry (blink/recursion), two reducers with the same source coexist and both pass the predicate, double-counting the affinity reduction on the controller's instant/sorcery spells — the over-reduction failure the brief flags as STRICT.\n\nThe engine additivity is otherwise sound: `get_cost_reduction` sums own `cost_reduction()` + registry then clamps with `max(0, min(raw, generic))`, so colored pips are untouched and generic never goes below 0; the registry is a strict no-op when empty; the predicate correctly excludes Witherbloom's own spell and limits to the controller's instant/sorcery spells; static data matches the spec."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a4b3da04f9d1b2e8c (use SendMessage with to: 'a4b3da04f9d1b2e8c' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 25958\ntool_uses: 14\nduration_ms: 128893</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"1f575954-4ebe-41a9-a08e-e9d883ac91d3","timestamp":"2026-06-01T10:10:27.342Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Review the implementation diff for SOS card `sos_245` (Witherbloom, the Balancer — Flying/Deathtouch creature with affinity-for-creatures on itself AND granting affinity for creatures to the controller's other instant/sorcery spells). CARD_DIR = `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245`.\n\nDiff to review: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl.diff` (includes BOTH card and engine changes).\nCard spec for intent: `cards/sos/sos_245/card_spec.json`.\nImplementer's rationale: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-rationale.md`.\nContext: `FILES_MODIFIED.json`, `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n\nCoordinator-approved ADDITIVE engine changes (in scope): a game-level cost-reduction registry `GameState.spell_cost_reducers` with `register_spell_cost_reducer` / `unregister_spell_cost_reducer` / `spell_cost_reduction_from_reducers`, summed in `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`.\n\nReview focus:\n- Static correctness: Flying, Deathtouch, P/T, name, cost, colors, subtypes, legendary.\n- Affinity reduction correctness: generic cost reduced by creature count, COLORED pips never reduced, clamped so generic never goes below 0.\n- Registry correctness: reduction applies only to the CONTROLLER's instant/sorcery spells (not opponents', not creature spells); reducer registered while Witherbloom is on the battlefield; unregister works.\n- ENGINE ADDITIVITY & REGRESSION RISK (CRITICAL): verify all engine changes are strictly additive (no existing symbol renamed/moved/deleted). The registry summed in `get_cost_reduction` MUST be a NO-OP when empty, so the heavily-tested cost-reduction/casting pipeline is unchanged. Flag STRICT if the registry could over-reduce, reduce colored pips, apply to the wrong spells, double-count a spell's own reduction plus the registry, or change default get_cost_reduction behavior when the registry is empty.\n\nConstraints:\n- Do NOT flag conventions in KEY_DECISIONS.md.\n- Do NOT demand test rewrites — advisory only.\n- Only flag what's visible in the diff.\n\nOutput: write `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/review.json` as a JSON array of {\"severity\":\"strict\"|\"advisory\",\"file\",\"line\",\"comment\"}. \"strict\" only for correctness/spec/regression bugs that must be fixed. Empty [] if none.\n\nReturn: REVIEW_DONE with strict_count, advisory_count, review_path.","agentId":"a4b3da04f9d1b2e8c","agentType":"Reviewer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"REVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 1\nadvisory_count: 1\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/review.json\n\nKey finding (strict): `register_triggers` registers the spell-cost reducer on every battlefield entry, but nothing calls `unregister_spell_cost_reducer` on leave (the engine leave path at `/workspace/engine/zones.py:297-299` only unregisters triggers/replacements). Since `register_triggers` is non-idempotent and runs again on re-entry (blink/recursion), two reducers with the same source coexist and both pass the predicate, double-counting the affinity reduction on the controller's instant/sorcery spells — the over-reduction failure the brief flags as STRICT.\n\nThe engine additivity is otherwise sound: `get_cost_reduction` sums own `cost_reduction()` + registry then clamps with `max(0, min(raw, generic))`, so colored pips are untouched and generic never goes below 0; the registry is a strict no-op when empty; the predicate correctly excludes Witherbloom's own spell and limits to the controller's instant/sorcery spells; static data matches the spec."}],"totalDurationMs":128893,"totalTokens":25958,"totalToolUseCount":14,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1275,"cache_read_input_tokens":24292,"output_tokens":389,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1275},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":389,"cache_read_input_tokens":24292,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1275,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1275,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":9,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":4,"editFileCount":1,"linesAdded":15,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
