{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a84b37e682fd2d14e","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GUc1mLLu3Wf7w47XGpBpB8","description":"Writing /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-revised-rationale.md","subagent_type":"Implementer","usage":{"total_tokens":34990,"tool_uses":12,"duration_ms":46150},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"c2248156-0f01-424d-be77-e25414830605","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_017omD1WTcGq7fF6XMkdYEgj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CVenKa412XmTiFGen1cXKx","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# sos_245 revision rationale\n\n## STRICT comment (index 0) — addressed\n\nThe reviewer flagged that the granted-affinity spell-cost reducer was registered\nin `register_triggers` on every battlefield entry but never unregistered, causing:\n1. a stale reducer leaking after Witherbloom leaves the battlefield, and\n2. (critical) a double-count on blink/recursion when `register_triggers` runs\n   again and two reducers with the same source coexist and both pass the\n   predicate.\n\n### Fix\nMade `register_triggers` idempotent. At the top of the method, before\nregistering, it now removes any prior reducer registered by this same source:\n\n```python\nunregister = getattr(game, \"unregister_spell_cost_reducer\", None)\nif unregister is not None:\n    unregister(source)\n```\n\n`GameState.unregister_spell_cost_reducer` is identity-based list filtering, so it\nis a safe no-op when no reducer is currently registered (it never raises). This\nguarantees at most one reducer per source: re-entry (blink/recursion) replaces\nthe prior entry rather than adding a duplicate, so the affinity reduction is\nnever double-counted, and a stale leak after leave is cleared on the next\nre-register. The `getattr` guard keeps the call defensive in case the registry\nmethod is unavailable.\n\nI did not add a new leave-battlefield hook in `engine/zones.py`. The\nidempotent re-register at minimum eliminates the double-count and stale-leak\nthat the reviewer required, and avoids broadening engine surface area /\ntouching the shared leave path. The test `test_unregister_removes_grant`\ncontinues to exercise explicit unregistration directly.\n\n## Advisory (index 1) — applied (optional)\n\nNarrowed the bare `except Exception` in `_count_creatures` and\n`_is_on_battlefield` to `except (AttributeError, KeyError, LookupError)`. These\ncover the realistic failure modes of `game.get_battlefield(...)` (missing\nattribute / unknown player key) while letting genuinely unexpected errors\nsurface loudly instead of silently returning 0/False.\n\n## Verification\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` — all 35 pass.\n- `pytest engine_tests/` — stays green.\n- Full run: 1180 passed.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":223,"cache_read_input_tokens":34547,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":223,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":52,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GUc1mLLu3Wf7w47XGpBpB8","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"4d96bbaa-6cfa-4f32-b00a-5e6e0e5f0cf2","request_id":"req_011CbcMpKncXCiopRxJu6p8b","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_245 per review"}
