{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01SdcTbEvW4w3QK9Eu63iSCA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JZ2F6ZBo5j7Jtwn8tv5F3i","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/review.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1288,"cache_read_input_tokens":11606,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1288,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019WkGf7oeuD1zaqTQz8z1KJ","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"102f717a-dabb-45fb-830c-bc0c352a92e2","request_id":"req_011CbcNfZqaELPxTqW8j2dzo","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_257 per review"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JZ2F6ZBo5j7Jtwn8tv5F3i","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n4\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py\",\n5\t    \"line\": 246,\n6\t    \"comment\": \"Prowess pump is not 'until end of turn' — it is permanent. The trigger does `source._power_bonus += 1` into a plain instance attribute, and `power` returns `_base_power + _power_bonus`. Nothing ever decrements `_power_bonus`: the engine's end-of-turn cleanup (engine/turn.py step 2) only calls `effect_manager.remove_expired()` + `apply_all()`, and `CardImpl._reset_characteristics()`/`Creature._reset_characteristics()` only reset `card_types`, `keywords`, and `modified_*` — none touch `_power_bonus`. So a Hall that casts two instants on turn 3 is permanently +2/+0 on turns 4, 5, ... which contradicts the spec/oracle text 'gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' The established convention for this exact pattern (see cards/fdn/fdn_83 'gets +3/+0 until end of turn') is to register a `ContinuousEffect(layer=Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS, sublayer=SubLayer.MODIFY_PT, duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN)` so the bonus is swept by `remove_expired` at cleanup. The in-run tests only assert accumulation within a single turn, so they don't catch the missing expiry.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n10\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py\",\n11\t    \"line\": 120,\n12\t    \"comment\": \"The 'add one mana of any color' ability always produces GREEN with no way for the controller to choose a different color. Tests only require that some colored mana is produced, and there is no color-choice infrastructure being exercised here, so this is acceptable for now; noting that it does not yet honor 'any color' (the controller cannot pick white/blue/black/red).\"\n13\t  }\n14\t]\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019WkGf7oeuD1zaqTQz8z1KJ","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"b17e20c6-b712-451e-93d4-0a2afdbd7451","timestamp":"2026-06-01T10:22:31.101Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_257 per review"}
