{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01XkqfNPqaUszLeVidqcdcSH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016Q3BnY4toaSCze8vaSA92B","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# sos_257 revision rationale\n\n## STRICT comment (index 0): prowess pump must be \"until end of turn\"\n\nThe original implementation accumulated the +1/+0 buff into a plain\n`_power_bonus` attribute that nothing ever reset, making the buff permanent.\nFixed by modeling each pump as a duration-limited continuous effect, following\nthe established `cards/fdn/fdn_83` convention:\n\n- The prowess trigger's `_effect` now registers a\n  `ContinuousEffect(layer=Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS, sublayer=SubLayer.MODIFY_PT,\n  duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN)` whose `apply` callable bumps\n  `_power_bonus` by 1. Each instant/sorcery cast adds one such effect; they\n  stack within a turn.\n- Because the Hall is a `Land` (not a `Creature`), `_power_bonus` is the\n  field the `power` property reads. To make `apply_all` idempotent and to let\n  the end-of-turn sweep clear the buff, I added a `_reset_characteristics`\n  override that calls `super()._reset_characteristics()` and then zeroes\n  `_power_bonus`. The engine's `EffectManager._reset_objects` already calls\n  `_reset_characteristics` on every battlefield object before reapplying\n  effects, so the bonus is rebuilt from scratch each recalculation.\n- At end of turn the engine cleanup runs `remove_expired()` (which drops the\n  `DURATION_END_OF_TURN` effects) followed by `apply_all()` (which resets\n  `_power_bonus` to 0 and reapplies only surviving effects), so the buff is\n  back to 0 on the following turn. Verified manually: after a cast power is 3,\n  and after `remove_expired` + `apply_all` it returns to 2.\n- The trigger also calls `effect_manager.apply_all(game)` right after adding\n  the effect so the buff is observable as soon as the trigger resolves (the\n  test harness also calls `apply_all` itself, so this is belt-and-suspenders).\n- A defensive fallback to the old direct `_power_bonus += 1` bump is kept only\n  for a harness with no `effect_manager` / missing continuous-effects module,\n  so the within-turn buff stays observable in any environment.\n\nAll 25 `cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` tests still pass; `engine_tests/`\n(1145 tests) stays green. Engine changes: none (additive-only is satisfied —\nno engine files were modified at all).\n\n## Advisory comment (index 1): \"any color\" always produces GREEN\n\nAcknowledged, not changed. There is no color-choice infrastructure in the\nmana/casting pipeline to exercise, and the tests only require that exactly one\ncolored mana be produced. Honoring a true color choice would require new\nengine plumbing beyond this card's scope.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":224,"cache_read_input_tokens":33467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":224,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":52,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019WkGf7oeuD1zaqTQz8z1KJ","session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"1d85f88b-adc0-433b-bf91-161f1d4222ba","request_id":"req_011CbcNkFjno2rZpqwWDf6dF","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_257 per review"}
