{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_0167oyDM8Yd7PqT5cRzTD13q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017nUKfvXpn2Lxgu3QBwrJhw","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","old_string":"  exists. Apply the same idempotency to any other custom per-source registry you add.","new_string":"  exists. Apply the same idempotency to any other custom per-source registry you add.\n\n## Man-lands & \"until end of turn\" buffs (from sos_257)\n- **Animate a land into a creature** (e.g. \"{N}: becomes a 2/4 Wizard, still a land\"):\n  register a TYPE-layer `ContinuousEffect` that ADDS the creature type and sets P/T,\n  so it survives `EffectManager.apply_all` characteristic resets and the land remains\n  a land. Do NOT mutate `card_types`/power directly — that gets wiped on recalculation.\n- **\"Until end of turn\" pump (prowess-style)**: do NOT accumulate into a plain\n  attribute (e.g. `_power_bonus`) — nothing resets it, so the buff becomes permanent.\n  Model each pump as a `DURATION_END_OF_TURN` continuous effect in the\n  POWER_TOUGHNESS / MODIFY_PT layer (see `cards/fdn/fdn_83/card_impl.py`); the engine's\n  end-of-turn cleanup (`engine/turn.py` remove_expired + apply_all) clears it. Buffs\n  stack within the turn and all expire together at cleanup.\n- **Restricted/earmarked mana** (\"spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery\"):\n  `engine.mana.ManaPool` has NO restricted-mana concept and the payment path is core\n  and heavily tested. Adding it safely-no-op is hard — left UNVERIFIED for sos_257.\n  Revisit only if a future card makes it worth a careful additive ManaPool extension."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":153,"cache_read_input_tokens":152876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":153},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"332c8bf7-8030-4e47-8fca-84d078f00c18","request_id":"req_011CbcNpzpjykPqXSdD4pTPp"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017nUKfvXpn2Lxgu3QBwrJhw","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6f4bd5-6767-4f31-a917-ac0bdc13b45e","uuid":"fc9ca4d7-2897-42ba-b3a1-117e90b553de","timestamp":"2026-06-01T10:24:48.189Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"  exists. Apply the same idempotency to any other custom per-source registry you add.","newString":"  exists. Apply the same idempotency to any other custom per-source registry you add.\n\n## Man-lands & \"until end of turn\" buffs (from sos_257)\n- **Animate a land into a creature** (e.g. \"{N}: becomes a 2/4 Wizard, still a land\"):\n  register a TYPE-layer `ContinuousEffect` that ADDS the creature type and sets P/T,\n  so it survives `EffectManager.apply_all` characteristic resets and the land remains\n  a land. Do NOT mutate `card_types`/power directly — that gets wiped on recalculation.\n- **\"Until end of turn\" pump (prowess-style)**: do NOT accumulate into a plain\n  attribute (e.g. `_power_bonus`) — nothing resets it, so the buff becomes permanent.\n  Model each pump as a `DURATION_END_OF_TURN` continuous effect in the\n  POWER_TOUGHNESS / MODIFY_PT layer (see `cards/fdn/fdn_83/card_impl.py`); the engine's\n  end-of-turn cleanup (`engine/turn.py` remove_expired + apply_all) clears it. Buffs\n  stack within the turn and all expire together at cleanup.\n- **Restricted/earmarked mana** (\"spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery\"):\n  `engine.mana.ManaPool` has NO restricted-mana concept and the payment path is core\n  and heavily tested. Adding it safely-no-op is hard — left UNVERIFIED for sos_257.\n  Revisit only if a future card makes it worth a careful additive ManaPool extension.","originalFile":"# Key Decisions\n\nPersistent, append-only conventions and decisions across runs.\n\n## Card-level `get_targets()` vs. triggered-ability targets (from sos_1)\nThe casting pipeline (`engine/casting.py`) calls `card.get_targets(game)` for the\nSPELL ITSELF and forces the controller to choose those targets when the spell is\ncast. So `get_targets()` must only advertise targets the *spell* takes. If a card's\ntargeting belongs to a triggered ability (e.g. \"whenever this attacks, target ...\"),\ndo NOT expose it via the card-level `get_targets()` — otherwise casting the permanent\nwrongly requires/consumes a target (and can raise `CastingError` when none is legal).\nThe pipeline moves the card into the controller's `STACK` zone before querying\n`get_targets()`, so a card can detect \"am I being cast right now?\" by checking\nwhether `self` is in any player's `STACK` zone and return `[]` in that case. Have the\ntriggered ability choose its own target (via `player.choose_target`) at resolution.\n\n## Converge / multi-target / life-gain conventions (from sos_4)\n- **Converge X** = `len(self.colors_spent)`. The casting pipeline records the\n  distinct colors of mana spent as a LIST of `engine.types.Color` on\n  `card.colors_spent` (not an int). Initialize `colors_spent` to `[]` in\n  `__init__`; compute X with `len(...)`. (Note: fdn_205 used an int because it\n  bypassed the cast pipeline — prefer the list shape for real cards.)\n- **Multi-target ordering**: `chosen_targets` is ordered to match the oracle text\n  order of the `TargetRequirement`s returned by `get_targets()`. E.g. \"Target\n  player ... deals X damage to any target\" → `chosen_targets[0]` = target player,\n  `chosen_targets[1]` = any-target.\n- **Life gain**: there is no `gain_life` engine helper. Gain life directly via\n  `controller.life += x`. Damage uses `engine.game.deal_damage`, draw uses\n  `engine.game.draw_card`.\n- Resolution should short-circuit on X <= 0 and defend against missing\n  `chosen_targets`/`colors_spent` so it never raises.\n\n## Do NOT add members to `engine.types.Keyword` (from sos_13)\nThe authoritative engine regression test\n`engine_tests/test_types.py::TestKeyword::test_exactly_sixteen_members` asserts\n`len(Keyword) == 16`. `engine_tests/` is read-only and authoritative for grading,\nso adding ANY new `Keyword` enum member zeros that test. For cards introducing a\nnew \"keyword\" that isn't already in the enum (e.g. \"Prepared\"), DO NOT add an enum\nmember. Instead model the mechanic's runtime state with a plain attribute/bool on\nthe card (e.g. `is_prepared`) and mark unimplementable sub-clauses with grep-able\n`# UNVERIFIED: <requirement> — <reason>` comments. Same caution likely applies to\nother \"exactly N members\" enum-count tests — check `engine_tests/test_types.py`\nbefore extending any engine enum.\n\n## New engine infrastructure added (from sos_57) — reuse for later cards\n- **`BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`** added to `engine/events.py`, fired from\n  `GameState.advance_phase` via `_fire_beginning_of_main_phase()`. It pushes a\n  StackObject (does NOT resolve immediately), so `empty_mana_pools()` after it does\n  not wipe mana the trigger later produces during stack resolution. Use this for any\n  \"at the beginning of your/the next (pre/post-combat) main phase\" delayed trigger.\n- **`card.mana_spent`** is now recorded during casting in `engine/casting.py`\n  (`= effective_cost.cmc`), alongside `colors_spent`. Use it for effects keyed on\n  \"the amount of mana spent to cast that spell\".\n- Counterspell pattern (cf. fdn_160): remove the target spell's StackObject from the\n  stack, remove the card from its controller's STACK zone, add to the OWNER's\n  graveyard, and never run its `on_resolve`. `get_targets()` advertises one\n  `TargetRequirement` with `zone == Zone.STACK` filtering for spells.\n\n## More engine infrastructure (from sos_97) — reuse for later cards\n- **`GameState.flip_coin(player)`** — deterministic coin flip, scriptable through\n  the existing DeterministicPlayer mechanism (`choose_yes_no`), falls back to RNG\n  when no script. Use for any \"flip a coin\" card; tests force outcomes via the\n  player's `_script`.\n- **`Player.skipped_turns`** (int, default 0) — consumed by `_apply_skipped_turns()`\n  in `GameState.advance_phase`. Default 0 is a strict no-op (loop never enters), so\n  normal turn rotation is unaffected. Use `target.skipped_turns += X` for\n  \"skips their next X turns\" effects.\n- Engine extension recipe that worked twice (sos_57, sos_97): add new event\n  classes / attributes / hooks ADDITIVELY, make the default value a no-op, and run\n  `pytest engine_tests/` after each change to confirm zero regressions.\n\n## Miracle / alternative-cost infrastructure (from sos_201) — reuse for later cards\n- **`engine.casting.cast_spell_alternative`** — cast a spell paying a specified\n  ALTERNATIVE cost (mirrors `cast_spell_free` but with a cost). Use for miracle,\n  flashback-style, and other \"cast for an alternative cost\" effects.\n- **Per-game miracle-grant registry + `GameState.fire_miracle_window`**, plus a\n  first-draw hook in `engine.game.draw_card`: when a player draws their FIRST card of\n  the turn and a grant is registered, the window offers an alternative-cost cast.\n  Strict no-op when the registry is empty (guarded), so the draw pipeline is\n  unaffected. Cards register/observe grants while on the battlefield.\n- **CAVEAT**: `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` is NOT reset across turns by the engine\n  (pre-existing limitation). The miracle \"first card drawn this turn\" window\n  therefore behaves correctly in unit tests that drive `draw_card` directly, but does\n  not reset across turns in a full `run_game()`. Do not rely on it resetting; if a\n  future card needs per-turn draw counting, add an additive reset at turn start and\n  re-run engine_tests/ to confirm no regressions before depending on it.\n\n## External cost-reduction registry (from sos_245) — reuse for later cards\n- **`GameState.spell_cost_reducers`** registry, with `register_spell_cost_reducer` /\n  `unregister_spell_cost_reducer` / `spell_cost_reduction_from_reducers`.\n  `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` SUMS registered reducers alongside a spell's own\n  `cost_reduction()` hook, then clamps `max(0, min(raw, generic))` — colored pips are\n  never reduced and generic never goes below 0. Strict no-op when the registry is\n  empty. Use this whenever ONE permanent must discount its controller's OTHER spells\n  (\"spells you cast cost {N} less / have affinity for X\"). FDN 159's analogous clause\n  was previously an inert marker — prefer the registry now.\n- **GOTCHA (cost reducer / continuous-effect registration on enter)**: `register_triggers`\n  runs on EVERY battlefield ENTRY, and the engine's leave-battlefield path only\n  unregisters triggers/replacements — NOT custom registries like spell_cost_reducers.\n  So a naive register-on-enter leaks a stale reducer on leave and DOUBLE-registers on\n  blink/recursion (double-counting). Make registration idempotent: at the top of\n  `register_triggers`, call `game.unregister_spell_cost_reducer(self)` (identity-based,\n  safe no-op when absent) BEFORE re-registering, so at most one reducer per source\n  exists. Apply the same idempotency to any other custom per-source registry you add.\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":103,"oldLines":3,"newStart":103,"newLines":19,"lines":["   safe no-op when absent) BEFORE re-registering, so at most one reducer per source","   exists. Apply the same idempotency to any other custom per-source registry you add."," ","+## Man-lands & \"until end of turn\" buffs (from sos_257)","+- **Animate a land into a creature** (e.g. \"{N}: becomes a 2/4 Wizard, still a land\"):","+  register a TYPE-layer `ContinuousEffect` that ADDS the creature type and sets P/T,","+  so it survives `EffectManager.apply_all` characteristic resets and the land remains","+  a land. Do NOT mutate `card_types`/power directly — that gets wiped on recalculation.","+- **\"Until end of turn\" pump (prowess-style)**: do NOT accumulate into a plain","+  attribute (e.g. `_power_bonus`) — nothing resets it, so the buff becomes permanent.","+  Model each pump as a `DURATION_END_OF_TURN` continuous effect in the","+  POWER_TOUGHNESS / MODIFY_PT layer (see `cards/fdn/fdn_83/card_impl.py`); the engine's","+  end-of-turn cleanup (`engine/turn.py` remove_expired + apply_all) clears it. Buffs","+  stack within the turn and all expire together at cleanup.","+- **Restricted/earmarked mana** (\"spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery\"):","+  `engine.mana.ManaPool` has NO restricted-mana concept and the payment path is core","+  and heavily tested. Adding it safely-no-op is hard — left UNVERIFIED for sos_257.","+  Revisit only if a future card makes it worth a careful additive ManaPool extension.","+"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
